// Vygenerováno z i18n/en/ skriptem tools/i18n-build.mjs – neupravovat ručně.
registerLanguage('en', {" a ":" and "," – ale tvůj mix praktik ji neumožnil.":" – but your practice mix did not allow it.","(Harmonogram {h}, potřeba ≥ {need}.)":"(Schedule {h}, needed ≥ {need}.)","(Skutečná hodnota pro uživatele: {value}, cíl {target}.)":"(Actual value for users: {value}, target {target}.)","(nesplněno)":"(missed)","(rozhodnutí „{choice}“)":"(decision “{choice}”)","(učí {who})":"(taught by {who})","(zpoždění)":"(late)","+{d} zpoždění etapy":"+{d} stage delay",", další cíl: {name} – {target}":", next goal: {name} – {target}",". Když odejdou, je problém.":". If they leave, there is trouble.","/100 bodů":"/100 points","<b>Agilně řízené prvky</b>: na začátku každého sprintu vyber z backlogu položky do <b>kapacity týmu</b> (story pointy). Kapacitu ovlivňuje morálka i tvůj mix praktik.":"<b>Agile-managed parts</b>: at the start of each sprint, pick backlog items up to the <b>team capacity</b> (story points). Capacity depends on morale and your practice mix.","<b>Bez nápověd:</b> nikdo ti neřekne, jestli byla volba dobrá, jak praktiky působí ani které vzorce v projektu vznikají. Všechno se dozvíš až na konci.":"<b>No hints:</b> nobody tells you whether a choice was good, how practices work or which patterns are forming. You find out everything at the end.","<b>Dosáhl(a) jsi nejvyšší pozice.</b> Gratulujeme, mistře projektové alchymie.":"<b>You have reached the top position.</b> Congratulations, Master of Project Alchemy.","<b>Lidé a znalosti:</b> každý člověk umí jen některé oblasti. Práci, kterou nikdo neumí, dělá tým o polovinu pomaleji. Přetížení lidé vyhoří a odejdou – i se svými znalostmi.":"<b>People and knowledge:</b> each person knows only some areas. Work nobody knows takes the team 50% longer. Overloaded people burn out and leave – taking their knowledge with them.","<b>Mlha reportingu:</b> ukazatele vidíš jen v rozmezí a o období zpožděné – pokud v mixu nemáš praktiku, která ukazuje skutečný stav projektu.":"<b>Reporting fog:</b> you see metrics only as a range and one period late – unless your mix has a practice that shows the real status of the project.","<b>Náročná úroveň:</b> rozpočet režie jen {budget} bodů, ukazatele začínají na {start} a projekt končí už při poklesu na {fail}. Po {n}. {loc} se <b>změní kontext</b> a odhalí se skrytý faktor – pak můžeš přeskládat mix. Některá rozhodnutí se <b>vrátí později</b>.":"<b>Hard level:</b> an overhead budget of only {budget} points, metrics start at {start} and the project ends as soon as one drops to {fail}. After {loc} {n} the <b>context changes</b> and a hidden factor is revealed – then you can rebuild your mix. Some decisions <b>come back later</b>.","<b>Následek dřívějšího rozhodnutí</b> ({title}, {period} {n}): „{choice}“":"<b>Consequence of an earlier decision</b> ({title}, {period} {n}): “{choice}”","<b>Pravidlo palce:</b> Jasné a stabilní požadavky + drahá změna → prediktivně. Nejistota, potřeba zpětné vazby, možnost dodávat po částech → agilně. <b>Hybridní</b> řízení potřebuje jen projekt, který obsahuje obojí.":"<b>Rule of thumb:</b> Clear, stable requirements + expensive change → predictive. Uncertainty, a need for feedback, the option to deliver in parts → agile. Only a project that contains both needs <b>hybrid</b> management.","<b>Prediktivně řízené prvky</b> ({pred}) běží podle plánu. S tvým mixem se milníky splní, pokud udržíš <b>{icon} Harmonogram ≥ {n}</b>.":"The <b>predictively managed parts</b> ({pred}) follow the plan. With your mix, milestones are met if you keep <b>{icon} Schedule ≥ {n}</b>.","<b>Projekt mění tvář:</b> během projektu se {n}× změní jeho povaha. Pokaždé můžeš přeskládat mix praktik.":"<b>A shape-shifting project:</b> its nature changes {n}× during the project. Each time you can rebuild your practice mix.","<b>Projekt, nebo provoz?</b> Některé položky backlogu jsou rutina, která do projektu nepatří. Tlačítkem {icon} je předáš provozu – ale skutečná projektová práce tam nepatří.":"<b>Project or operations?</b> Some backlog items are routine work that does not belong in the project. The {icon} button hands them over to operations – but real project work does not belong there.","<b>Převzatý projekt:</b> na dokončení máš jen zbytek projektu – a dědíš to, co předchozí vedení rozbilo.":"<b>Inherited project:</b> you only have the rest of the project to finish it – and you inherit what the previous management broke.","<b>Rok poté:</b> po konci projektu se ukáže, co z něj zbylo: kvalita, předání do provozu, znalosti, lidé a podpora stakeholderů. Započítá se do skóre.":"<b>A year later:</b> after the project ends you see what is left of it: quality, handover to operations, knowledge, people and stakeholder support. It counts towards the score.","<b>Skutečné závislosti</b> se ukážou až během etapy. Když úkol začne dřív, než skončí jeho předchůdce, práce se přeruší a den se dělá znovu. Přetížený tým etapu natáhne.":"The <b>real dependencies</b> only show during the stage. If a task starts before its predecessor ends, work is interrupted and the day is redone. An overloaded team stretches the stage.","<b>Stakeholdeři:</b> {n} strany s různými zájmy. Každá sleduje hlavně svou práci; když některá klesne na {fail}, projekt končí.":"<b>Stakeholders:</b> {n} parties with different interests. Each mostly watches its own work; if any drops to {fail}, the project ends.","<b>Velmi obtížná úroveň</b> – ukazatele končí už při poklesu na {fail}, rozpočet režie je {budget} bodů.":"<b>Very difficult level</b> – the project ends as soon as a metric drops to {fail}; the overhead budget is {budget} points.","<b>{a}</b> byl naplánovaný před příjezdem inspektora/zkušebny ({d}. den) – musel čekat.":"<b>{a}</b> was scheduled before the inspector/test lab arrived (day {d}) – it had to wait.","<b>{a}</b> začal dřív, než skončil <b>{b}</b> – práce se přerušila a den se dělal znovu.":"<b>{a}</b> started before <b>{b}</b> finished – work was interrupted and the day had to be redone.","A opakovaná rutina není projekt vůbec – patří do provozu.":"And recurring routine work is not a project at all – it belongs to operations.","Agilní prvky":"Agile parts","Agilně":"Agile","Agilně řízené prvky: co tým dodal":"Agile parts: what the team delivered","Analýza kritické cesty ukáže <b>kritické úkoly a vůli</b> ostatních.":"Critical path analysis shows the <b>critical tasks and the float</b> of the others.","Ani mlha nepomohla":"Not even the fog stopped you","Ano, smazat vše":"Yes, delete everything","Antivzorce se nepoznají podle formy, ale podle důsledků – a ty přicházejí pozdě.":"Anti-patterns are recognized not by their form but by their consequences – and those come late.","Antivzorce – mechanismy, které vedou k dysfunkcím":"Anti-patterns – mechanisms that lead to dysfunction","Aspoň 24 z {n} vzorců v atlasu":"At least 24 of {n} patterns in the atlas","Aspoň jeden náročný projekt za ★★★":"At least one hard project with ★★★","Aspoň jeden velmi obtížný projekt za ★★":"At least one very difficult project with ★★","Atlas":"Atlas","Atlas vzorců":"Pattern atlas","Bez analýzy kritické cesty nevidíš, které úkoly nesmí sklouznout.":"Without critical path analysis you cannot see which tasks must not slip.","Bez dashboardu nebo EVM vidíš stav jen nahrubo a s jednoperiodovým zpožděním.":"Without a dashboard or EVM you see the status only roughly and one period late.","Bez praktiky pro harmonogram musíš všechno rozvrhnout ručně.":"Without a scheduling practice you have to plan everything by hand.","Bez review ji ale uživatelé skoro nevidí.":"Without a review, though, users barely see it.","Body máš na tři hvězdy, chybí ale podmínka pro mistrovství – viz níže.":"You have the points for three stars, but a mastery condition is missing – see below.","Během každé etapy přijde <b>událost</b>. V polovině projektu tě čeká <b>kontrolní bod</b>.":"Every stage brings an <b>event</b>. Halfway through the project there is a <b>checkpoint</b>.","Během každého sprintu přijde <b>událost</b>. Některé volby odemyká jen správná praktika. V polovině projektu tě čeká <b>stage gate</b>.":"Every sprint brings an <b>event</b>. Some options are unlocked only by the right practice. Halfway through the project there is a <b>stage gate</b>.","Během každého sprintu přijde <b>událost</b>. V polovině projektu tě čeká <b>demo day</b> pro investory.":"Every sprint brings an <b>event</b>. Halfway through the project there is a <b>demo day</b> for investors.","Celkem 15 ★":"15 ★ in total","Celkem 22 ★":"22 ★ in total","Celkem 28 ★":"28 ★ in total","Celkem 3 ★":"3 ★ in total","Celkem 33 ★":"33 ★ in total","Celkem 8 ★":"8 ★ in total","Celkem {n} ★ z {all} · odznaky {b} z {ball}.":"{n} ★ of {all} in total · badges {b} of {ball}.","Celkové vyhodnocení":"Final evaluation","Celý atlas: {n} / {all} objeveno":"Full atlas: {n} / {all} discovered","Chybí: {list}.":"Missing: {list}.","Co projekt zahrnuje:":"What the project includes:","Co se nevejde do délky etapy, ukrojí z <b>rezervy projektu ({buffer})</b>. Když dojde, každý další den stojí {h} i {b}.":"Whatever does not fit into the stage eats into the <b>project buffer ({buffer})</b>. Once it runs out, every extra day costs {h} and {b}.","Co se nevejde do jednoho sprintu, nedodáš nikdy celé. Malé kusy jdou dodat i ověřit.":"If it doesn’t fit into one sprint, you will never deliver it whole. Small pieces can be delivered and tested.","Co se nevejde do jednoho sprintu, nedodáš nikdy celé. Velkou položku rozděl na menší části, z nichž každá jde dokončit a předvést – třeba podle kroků procesu, typů dat nebo skupin uživatelů.":"If it doesn't fit into one sprint, you will never deliver it whole. Split a large item into smaller parts that can each be finished and demonstrated – for example by process step, data type or user group.","Co se skrývalo v mlze":"What was hidden in the fog","Co se v etapě dokončilo":"What was finished in the stage","Co sis z projektu odnesl(a)":"What you took away from the project","Co tvůj mix v projektu doopravdy způsobil – dobré i špatné.":"What your mix really caused in the project – good and bad.","Co tvůj mix v projektu doopravdy způsobí, se ukáže až za pochodu. Vzorce a antivzorce budeš odhalovat během projektu – každý jako řetězec <b>kontext → forma → mechanismus → důsledek</b>.":"What your mix really does to the project only shows along the way. You will uncover patterns and anti-patterns during the project – each as a chain of <b>context → form → mechanism → consequence</b>.","Co tým dodal":"What the team delivered","Co tě čeká":"What awaits you","Co vidíš v prvním týdnu":"What you see in the first week","Co řídit prediktivně a co agilně? A je to vůbec hybrid?":"What to manage predictively and what agilely? Is it a hybrid at all?","Cíl trakce":"Traction goal","Cíl: <b>{name}</b>.":"Goal: <b>{name}</b>.","Cíle projektu:":"Project goals:","Cíle trakce":"Traction goals","Diagnóza je zapsaná":"Your diagnosis is recorded","Diagnóza převzatého projektu":"Diagnosis of the inherited project","Diagnóza: co se v projektu děje?":"Diagnosis: what is going on in the project?","Do týmu přišel{a} {name} ({role}).":"{name} joined the team ({role}).","Dobré řízení je hlavně řada malých rozhodnutí, která nic nezhorší.":"Good management is mostly a series of small decisions that make nothing worse.","Dobrý Gantt má správné závislosti, respektuje kapacitu lidí a vejde se do délky etapy – ideálně s malou vůlí na neočekávané.":"A good Gantt chart has the right dependencies, respects people’s capacity and fits within the stage – ideally with a little float for the unexpected.","Dobrý hybridní mix pokryje plán a rizika prediktivně řízených prvků, iterace a Product Ownera u agilně řízených prvků a hlavně jejich propojení v jednom projektu – bez zbytečné režie.":"A good hybrid mix covers planning and risks for the predictively managed parts, iterations and a Product Owner for the agile parts, and above all links them within one project – without unnecessary overhead.","Dodaná hodnota":"Delivered value","Dodaná hodnota zatím <b>{v}</b>":"Value delivered so far: <b>{v}</b>","Dodaná hodnota: +{value}.":"Value delivered: +{value}.","Dodané funkce mohou odhalit <b>nové podněty od uživatelů</b> – backlog se vyvíjí.":"Delivered features may reveal <b>new requests from users</b> – the backlog evolves.","Dodání v termínu":"On-time delivery","Dokonči etapový projekt, aniž bys sáhl(a) do rezervy.":"Finish a stage-based project without touching the buffer.","Dokonči projekt bez jediného špatného rozhodnutí.":"Finish a project without a single poor decision.","Dopad zmírnila praktika: {list}":"Impact softened by: {list}","Dosáhni udržitelnosti výsledku aspoň 80 %.":"Reach a sustainability of at least 80 %.","Dozvuky po projektu":"Aftershocks of the project","Délka etapy":"Stage length","Délka výluky":"Closure length","Důsledek":"Consequence","Etapy":"Stages","Etapy jsou <b>výluky</b>: co se ve výluce nestihne, přesune se do další a stojí to {s} i {b}. Rezervu projektu ({buffer}) čerpá jen poslední výluka.":"The stages are <b>track closures</b>: whatever does not fit into a closure moves to the next one and costs {s} and {b}. Only the last closure draws on the project buffer ({buffer}).","Experimenty v tomto sprintu: {n} / {all}":"Experiments this sprint: {n} / {all}","Finanční oddělení se začíná vyptávat na každou fakturu.":"Finance has started asking questions about every invoice.","Forma":"Form","Fáze {n} / 3":"Phase {n} / 3","Gantt etapy {n}: {name}":"Stage {n} Gantt: {name}","Hodnota pro uživatele":"Value for users","Hodnota u položek je jen <b>odhad (hypotéza)</b> – skutečnost ukáže až dodání, nebo ji <b>ověříš experimentem {icon}</b> (až {n} za sprint).":"The value of items is only an <b>estimate (hypothesis)</b> – delivery shows the reality, or you can <b>test it with an experiment {icon}</b> (up to {n} per sprint).","Hodnota u položek je jen <b>odhad (hypotéza)</b> – skutečnost ukáže až dodání.":"The value of items is only an <b>estimate (hypothesis)</b> – delivery shows the reality.","Hra se dá nainstalovat jako aplikace a pak běží i offline.":"You can install the game as an app, and then it runs offline too.","Hraj i bez internetu":"Play offline too","Hraješ staženou verzi z počítače. Postup se ukládá jen v tomto prohlížeči.":"You are playing the downloaded version from your computer. Progress is saved only in this browser.","Hrdina týdne":"Hero of the week","Hrát znovu":"Play again","Hybrid je propojení dvou světů ve společných milnících, ne dva projekty vedle sebe.":"A hybrid links two worlds through shared milestones – it is not two projects side by side.","Hybridní alchymista":"Hybrid alchemist","Hypotéza ověřena":"Hypothesis confirmed","I bez nápověd, s unaveným týmem a rozhádanými stakeholdery jde řídit dobře.":"Even without hints, with a tired team and quarreling stakeholders, you can manage well.","Inspekce / zkušebna":"Inspection / test lab","Investoři rozhodují":"The investors decide","Jak dobře jsi práci rozdělil(a), se ukáže během projektu a v závěrečném hodnocení.":"How well you split the work will show during the project and in the final evaluation.","Jak projekt řídit, je na tobě – přijdeš na to v první fázi.":"How to run the project is up to you – you will figure it out in the first phase.","Jak to funguje":"How it works","Jasná hranice":"Clear boundary","Jasná hranice projektu":"A clear project boundary","Jasné a stabilní požadavky → prediktivně. Nejistota a potřeba zpětné vazby → agilně. Hybrid jen tam, kde projekt obsahuje obojí.":"Clear, stable requirements → predictive. Uncertainty and a need for feedback → agile. Hybrid only where the project contains both.","Je to <b>výluka</b> – co se nestihne, čeká na další.":"It is a <b>track closure</b> – whatever is not finished waits for the next one.","Jestli úprava odpovídá nové situaci, ukáže projekt.":"Whether the adjustment fits the new situation, the project will show.","Jiný projekt":"Another project","Junior PM":"Junior PM","Kapacita týmu":"Team capacity","Kapacita týmu je do konce projektu nižší o {n}.":"Team capacity is {n} lower until the end of the project.","Kapacita: {list}.":"Capacity: {list}.","Kariéra":"Career","Kariéra: {rank}":"Career: {rank}","Karty se synergiemi, konflikty a omezenou režií.":"Cards with synergies, conflicts and limited overhead.","Každou část řešení umí aspoň dva lidé.":"At least two people know every part of the solution.","Každá hra vylosuje jiné události a odpovědi jsou pokaždé v jiném pořadí.":"Every game draws different events, and the answers come in a different order each time.","Každá nově zavedená praktika stojí −3 {b} a −2 {m} (změna procesu uprostřed projektu). Odebrat můžeš cokoli zdarma.":"Every newly introduced practice costs −3 {b} and −2 {m} (changing the process mid-project). You can remove anything for free.","Každý bod nad rozpočet sníží kapacitu týmu.":"Every point over budget reduces team capacity.","Kde nikdo předem neví, co uživatelé ocení, vyhrává krátký cyklus a rychlá zpětná vazba.":"Where nobody knows in advance what users will value, short cycles and fast feedback win.","Když se svět kolem projektu změní, přizpůsobíš řízení – metodika pro tebe není dogma.":"When the world around the project changes, you adapt your management – a methodology is not dogma to you.","Klikni na položky, které tým v tomto sprintu udělá. Pořadí kliknutí = priorita.":"Click the items the team will do in this sprint. Click order = priority.","Klikni na položky, které tým v této etapě udělá. Pořadí kliknutí = priorita.":"Click the items the team will do in this stage. Click order = priority.","Klikni na položky, které tým ve sprintu udělá. {v} ~ je jen odhad hodnoty – skutečnost ukáže dodání nebo experiment {e}.":"Click the items the team will do in this sprint. {v} ~ is only an estimate of value – delivery or an experiment {e} shows the reality.","Klikni na položky, které tým ve sprintu udělá. {v} ~ je jen odhad hodnoty – skutečnost ukáže dodání.":"Click the items the team will do in this sprint. {v} ~ is only an estimate of value – delivery shows the reality.","Klikni v řádku úkolu na den, kdy má začít. Ve sloupci <b>Začíná po</b> vyznač, po kterých úkolech smí začít. Dole vidíš, kolik lidí je který den potřeba. Skutečné závislosti se ukážou až během {gen} – odvoď je z popisu práce.":"Click the day in a task row when it should start. In the <b>Starts after</b> column, mark which tasks it may start after. Below you see how many people are needed each day. The real dependencies only show during the {gen} – work them out from the task descriptions.","Klikni v řádku úkolu na den, kdy má začít. Ve sloupci <b>Začíná po</b> vyznač, po kterých úkolech smí začít. Dole vidíš, kolik lidí každé profese je který den potřeba. Skutečné závislosti se ukážou až během {gen} – odvoď je z popisu práce.":"Click the day in a task row when it should start. In the <b>Starts after</b> column, mark which tasks it may start after. Below you see how many people of each trade are needed each day. The real dependencies only show during the {gen} – work them out from the task descriptions.","Komise schválila komisi":"The board approved the board","Konec projektu – a co dál?":"End of the project – what next?","Konflikt":"Conflict","Konflikty":"Conflicts","Kontext":"Context","Kontext projektu:":"Project context:","Kontext teď:":"Context now:","Kontrola: {name}":"Review: {name}","Kontrolní bod":"Checkpoint","Kontrolní den":"Checkpoint review","Kotel: {n} praktik, režie {cost} z {budget}. Poměr: {ratio}.":"Cauldron: {n} practices, overhead {cost} of {budget}. Ratio: {ratio}.","Levný experiment je lepší než drahá funkce, o kterou nikdo nestojí.":"A cheap experiment beats an expensive feature nobody wants.","Lidé a udržitelnost":"People and sustainability","Lidé chtějí na řešení dál pracovat a rozvíjet ho.":"People want to keep working on the solution and improve it.","Lidé v týmu si potichu aktualizují životopisy.":"People on the team are quietly updating their résumés.","MD":"PD","Manažerský úsudek":"Management judgment","Mechanismus":"Mechanism","Mechanismus působil od chvíle, kdy jsi zvolil(a) svůj mix praktik. Teď se ukázal jeho důsledek.":"The mechanism has been at work since you chose your practice mix. Now its consequence shows.","Meloun roku":"Watermelon of the year","Metodika nastavená na začátku řeší včerejší problémy. Když se svět změní, změň i řízení.":"A methodology set at the start solves yesterday’s problems. When the world changes, change your management too.","Metodika zůstala stejná, i když se svět změnil":"The methodology stayed the same even though the world changed","Milník":"Milestone","Milník: {name}":"Milestone: {name}","Milníky":"Milestones","Mistr projektové alchymie":"Master of Project Alchemy","Mistr řízení projektů":"Master of project management","Mistrovství":"Mastery","Mix je upravený":"The mix is adjusted","Mix praktik":"Practice mix","Morálka":"Morale","Must – v projektu dodaná nebude":"Must – will not be delivered by the project","Musí platit, jinak 0 ★":"Must hold, otherwise 0 ★","Myslíš na lidi, stakeholdery i na to, co z projektu zbude po roce.":"You think about people, stakeholders and what will be left of the project a year later.","Méně zdrojů, skrytý faktor, změna kontextu uprostřed projektu a rozhodnutí, která se vrací. Ukazatele startují na {start}, na mix praktik máš {budget} bodů režie a projekt končí už při poklesu ukazatele na {fail}.":"Fewer resources, a hidden factor, a context change mid-project and decisions that come back. Metrics start at {start}, you have {budget} overhead points for your practice mix, and the project ends as soon as a metric drops to {fail}.","Měsíční komise pro každou změnu backlogu zabije to hlavní, proč je projekt agilní: rychlou reakci.":"A monthly board for every backlog change kills the very thing that makes a project agile: fast response.","Na chodbě se šušká, že termín je nereálný.":"Word in the hallway is that the deadline is unrealistic.","Na demo day":"To the demo day","Na iPhonu a iPadu ji nainstaluješ v Safari: Sdílet → Přidat na plochu.":"On iPhone and iPad, install it in Safari: Share → Add to Home Screen.","Na kontrolní den":"To the checkpoint review","Na odhalený faktor sedí: {list}.":"Fits the revealed factor: {list}.","Na plánování {n}. {gen}":"To {gen} {n} planning","Na povýšení na {rank} chybí:":"Missing for promotion to {rank}:","Na stage gate":"To the stage gate","Na velmi obtížné úrovni ti nikdo neřekne, jestli mix sedí. Poznáš to podle toho, jak se bude projekt vyvíjet – a v závěrečném hodnocení.":"At the very difficult level nobody tells you whether the mix fits. You will see it from how the project develops – and in the final evaluation.","Na začátku každé etapy vyber z plánu položky do <b>kapacity týmu</b>. Hlídej návaznosti a milníky; milník se splní, když udržíš harmonogram.":"At the start of each stage, pick items from the plan up to the <b>team capacity</b>. Watch dependencies and milestones; a milestone is met when you keep the schedule.","Na začátku sprintu vyber z backlogu položky do <b>kapacity týmu</b> (story pointy).":"At the start of each sprint, pick backlog items up to the <b>team capacity</b> (story points).","Na zásah do mixu":"To the mix intervention","Na {review}":"To the {review}","Nainstalovat aplikaci":"Install the app","Nainstaluješ ji ikonou instalace v adresním řádku Chromu nebo Edge, v Safari na Macu přes Soubor → Přidat do Docku.":"Install it with the install icon in the Chrome or Edge address bar, or in Safari on a Mac via File → Add to Dock.","Namíchej správné řízení pro každý projekt":"Brew the right management for every project","Navíc pro ★★★":"Extra for ★★★","Nebo si stáhni <a href=\"{url}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ZIP s hrou</a>, rozbal ho a otevři soubor index.html.":"Or download the <a href=\"{url}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">game as a ZIP</a>, unzip it and open the index.html file.","Nejdřív musí být hotové: {list}":"Must be done first: {list}","Nejlepší volba:":"Best choice:","Neobjevený antivzorec":"Undiscovered anti-pattern","Neobjevený vzorec":"Undiscovered pattern","Nesplněno":"Not achieved","Nestihlo se v minulé výluce – dokončuje se teď.":"Didn't fit into the last track closure – being finished now.","Nevejde se do kapacity týmu ({n} SP) – celá se nedokončí.":"Does not fit the team capacity ({n} SP) – it will never be finished whole.","Nevyznačil(a) jsi {n} skutečnou závislost(i), ale plán je náhodou dodržel.":"You did not mark {n} real dependency(ies), but the plan happened to respect them.","Než začneš měnit, zjisti, co v projektu doopravdy nefunguje.":"Before you change anything, find out what is really broken in the project.","Nikdo jiný neumí: {areas} – práce v {where} bude o polovinu pracnější.":"Nobody else knows: {areas} – work in {where} will take 50% more effort.","Nikdo neodešel":"Nobody left","Nikdo tomu nerozumí":"Nobody understands it","Nové odznaky":"New badges","Nové podněty od uživatelů":"New requests from users","Nový odznak":"New badge","Nový osobní rekord v tomto projektu!":"New personal record in this project!","Nový stakeholder: <b>{name}</b> – {wants}":"New stakeholder: <b>{name}</b> – {wants}","Nově přidané, ale tady nevhodné: {list}.":"Newly added but unsuitable here: {list}.","Nově {stars} v tomto projektu!":"New {stars} in this project!","Náročná úroveň":"Hard level","Něco se mění…":"Something is changing…","Některé položky na sobě závisí – a {hint} Tady se oba přístupy v jednom projektu potkávají!":"Some items depend on each other – and {hint} This is where both approaches meet in one project!","Některé položky na sobě závisí. Integrační milník ověří, že prediktivně i agilně řízené části do sebe zapadají.":"Some items depend on each other. The integration milestone checks that the predictive and agile parts fit together.","Některé projekty se dají naplánovat dopředu, jiné se musí objevovat za pochodu a některé kombinují obojí. Univerzální recept neexistuje.":"Some projects can be planned in advance, others have to be discovered along the way, and some combine both. There is no universal recipe.","Některé úkoly smí začít až v den, kdy přijede <b>inspektor nebo zkušebna {icon}</b>.":"Some tasks may start only on the day the <b>inspector or test lab {icon}</b> arrives.","Objev všechny antivzorce v atlasu.":"Discover all anti-patterns in the atlas.","Objev všechny vzorce v atlasu.":"Discover all patterns in the atlas.","Objeveno {n} z {all} vzorců a antivzorců.":"{n} of {all} patterns and anti-patterns discovered.","Objevíš ho, až ho získáš.":"You will discover it when you earn it.","Obrys = tvůj plán, plná barva = skutečnost. Teď vidíš i skutečné závislosti.":"Outline = your plan, solid color = actual. Now you also see the real dependencies.","Občasné výpadky":"Occasional outages","Odchody z týmu":"Team departures","Odemkne se, až v kterémkoli projektu náročné úrovně dosáhneš alespoň {n} bodů. Bez nápověd, s mlhou v reportech, se stakeholdery, lidmi a tím, co z projektu zbude po roce.":"Unlocks once you score at least {n} points in any hard-level project. No hints, with fog in the reports, stakeholders, people and what is left of the project a year later.","Odemkne se, až v kterémkoli projektu základní úrovně dosáhneš alespoň {n} bodů. Čeká tě méně zdrojů, skrytý faktor, změna kontextu a rozhodnutí, která se vrací.":"Unlocks once you score at least {n} points in any basic-level project. Expect fewer resources, a hidden factor, a context change and decisions that come back.","Odemčená náročná úroveň":"Hard level unlocked","Odhad nahrubo byl {rough}, podrobný plán má <b>{md} MD</b> ({diff} %). Hrubé odhady bývají optimistické.":"The rough estimate was {rough}; the detailed plan has <b>{md} PD</b> ({diff} %). Rough estimates tend to be optimistic.","Odhady budoucích etap <b>nahrubo bývají optimistické</b> – podrobný plán ukáže skutečnou pracnost.":"<b>Rough estimates</b> of future stages tend to be optimistic – the detailed plan shows the real effort.","Odhal vzorce":"Reveal patterns","Odhalen vzorec":"Pattern revealed","Odhaleny vzorce":"Patterns revealed","Odhalí se během projektu":"Revealed during the project","Odkud se vlivy berou, musíš vyčíst sám/sama.":"You have to work out for yourself where the effects come from.","Odložené problémy":"Postponed problems","Odznaky":"Badges","Opravdu smazat veškerý postup?":"Really delete all progress?","Ověř v jednom projektu hodnotu aspoň 4 experimenty.":"Test value with at least 4 experiments in one project.","Ověřit skutečnou hodnotu levným experimentem (landing page, rozhovory)":"Test the real value with a cheap experiment (landing page, interviews)","Označil(a) jsi {n} {word}. Jestli jsi trefil(a) skutečné příčiny, se ukáže až na konci – teď podle diagnózy zasáhni do mixu praktik.":"You marked {n} {word}. Whether you hit the real causes will only show at the end – now act on your diagnosis and adjust the practice mix.","Past: lákavá, ale tady škodí":"Trap: tempting, but harmful here","Pasti v mixu: {list}":"Traps in the mix: {list}","Plán":"Plan","Plán končí":"Plan ends","Plán po etapách":"Stage plan","Plán počítal s víc lidmi, než tým má ({d} přetížení). Úkoly {list} musely čekat, až se lidé uvolní.":"The plan needed more people than the team has ({d} of overload). Tasks {list} had to wait for people to free up.","Plán prací":"Work plan","Plán předem není přežitek: kde je zadání jasné a změna drahá, vyhrává.":"Planning up front is not outdated: where the brief is clear and change is expensive, it wins.","Plánování {gen}":"{gen} planning","Po roce už nikdo nerozumí: {areas}. Každá změna je dobrodružství.":"A year later nobody understands: {areas}. Every change is an adventure.","Po změně kontextu přeskládej mix správně ve třech hrách.":"Rebuild your mix correctly after a context change in three games.","Podpora všech stran":"Support from all sides","Podrobný plán: {name}":"Detailed plan: {name}","Pokaždé jinak":"Different every time","Pokračovat":"Continue","Pokračovat: mix praktik":"Continue: practice mix","Položka je větší než kapacita týmu – celá se nikdy nedokončí. Rozdělí ji na menší části, které se vejdou.":"The item is larger than the team capacity – it will never be finished whole. Splits it into smaller parts that fit.","Položky přibyly do backlogu.":"The items were added to the backlog.","Potvrdit diagnózu":"Confirm diagnosis","Potvrdit mix":"Confirm mix","Potvrdit zásah":"Confirm intervention","Potvrdit úpravu mixu":"Confirm mix changes","Potvrzení smazání postupu":"Confirm deleting progress","Povýšení":"Promotion","Poznání":"Knowledge","Poznáš, co řídit prediktivně a co agilně – a kdy projekt hybrid vůbec nepotřebuje.":"You can tell what to manage predictively and what agilely – and when a project does not need a hybrid at all.","Praktikant":"Intern","Praxe":"Experience","Prediktivní milník":"Predictive milestone","Prediktivní prvky":"Predictive parts","Prediktivně":"Predictive","Prioritizuj podle <b>MoSCoW</b>. Všechny <b>Must</b> položky musí být hotové do {launch}.":"Prioritize using <b>MoSCoW</b>. All <b>Must</b> items have to be done by {launch}.","Pro každý projekt namícháš řízení přesně podle jeho povahy.":"For every project you brew management that fits its nature exactly.","Pro tento typ projektu nevhodné:":"Unsuitable for this type of project:","Proběhlo přesně podle plánu.":"Went exactly as planned.","Programový manažer":"Program manager","Projekt doběhl do cíle, ale se šrámy. Mrkni na poučení níže a zkus to znovu.":"The project made it to the finish, but with scars. Check the lessons below and try again.","Projekt doběhl, ale na první hvězdu chybí {n} bodů. Zkus hru znovu – události budou jiné.":"The project finished, but it is {n} points short of the first star. Try again – the events will be different.","Projekt doběhl, ale nesplnil zásadní podmínku: {list}.":"The project finished but failed a key condition: {list}.","Projekt je dočasné úsilí s jedinečným výsledkem. Opakovanou rutinu (reporty, podpora, údržba) má dělat linie – když se řídí jako projekt, jen spotřebovává kapacitu a nic nového nevznikne.":"A project is a temporary effort with a unique result. Recurring routine work (reports, support, maintenance) belongs to the line organization – managed as a project, it only eats capacity and creates nothing new.","Projekt je dočasný a jedinečný. Rutina patří linii, jinak po projektu nikdo nezůstane.":"A project is temporary and unique. Routine work belongs to the line organization, otherwise nobody is left after the project.","Projekt je předaný a tým se rozešel k dalším úkolům. Co z něj zůstalo?":"The project has been handed over and the team has moved on. What is left of it?","Projekt jsi řídil(a) přesně tak, jak jeho povaha vyžadovala.":"You ran the project exactly the way its nature required.","Projekt má {n} etapy různé délky ({days} pracovních dní). Plánuje se <b>po vlnách</b>: budoucí etapy znáš jen nahrubo (délka, odhad práce v MD, milník), nejbližší etapu naplánuješ podrobně v <b>Ganttu</b>.":"The project has {n} stages of different lengths ({days} working days). Planning is <b>rolling-wave</b>: you know future stages only roughly (length, effort estimate in PD, milestone) and plan the next stage in detail in the <b>Gantt chart</b>.","Projekt nekončí předáním. To, jestli jeho výsledek po roce žije, rozhoduje kvalita, předání do provozu, znalosti v týmu, odpočatí lidé a podpora stakeholderů.":"A project does not end at handover. Whether its result is still alive a year later depends on quality, the handover to operations, knowledge in the team, rested people and stakeholder support.","Projekt přebíráš rozjetý. Nejdřív zjisti, co se v něm děje, pak zasáhni.":"You are taking over a project already in motion. First find out what is going on, then step in.","Projekt se dá dotáhnout na úkor lidí jen jednou. Další už s tebou nikdo dělat nebude.":"You can push a project through at the expense of people only once. Nobody will work with you on the next one.","Projekt se zpozdil natolik, že ho vedení zrušilo.":"The project slipped so far that management cancelled it.","Projekt skončil":"The project is over","Projekt skončil předčasně. Přečti si poučení a zkus to znovu!":"The project ended early. Read the lessons and try again!","Projekt skončil, ale provoz nedostal dokumentaci ani školení. Projektový tým je další rok „na telefonu“.":"The project ended, but operations got neither documentation nor training. The project team spends the next year \"on call\".","Projekt v krizi":"Project in crisis","Projekt, nebo provoz?":"Project or operations?","Projekt:":"Project:","Projektová alchymie":"Project Alchemy","Projektová alchymie – namíchej správné řízení pro každý projekt":"Project Alchemy – brew the right management for every project","Projektový manažer":"Project manager","Provoz":"Operations","Provoz převzal dokumentaci a proškolené lidi. Projektový tým se může věnovat dalšímu projektu.":"Operations took over the documentation and trained staff. The project team can move on to the next project.","Provoz týmu stál {burn}, tržby z nové verze přinesly {revenue}.":"Running the team cost {burn}; revenue from the new version brought in {revenue}.","Provoz v projektu":"Operations in the project","Provoz v převleku za projekt":"Operations disguised as a project","Prvky řízené agilně":"Agile-managed parts","Prvky řízené prediktivně":"Predictively managed parts","První trojka":"First three","Práce":"Work","Prázdný kotel – zatím žádná praktika.":"Empty cauldron – no practice yet.","Průběh projektu":"Project progress","Průběžný vliv tvého mixu":"Ongoing effect of your mix","Pět projektů na seznámení se hrou: tři hybridní, jeden prediktivní a jeden agilní. Ukazatele startují na {start}, na mix praktik máš {budget} bodů režie a projekt končí, až když některý ukazatel klesne na nulu.":"Five projects to get to know the game: three hybrid, one predictive and one agile. Metrics start at {start}, you have {budget} overhead points for your practice mix, and the project ends only when a metric drops to zero.","Předat liniové organizaci – v projektu se dělat nebude":"Hand over to the line organization – it will not be done in the project","Předchozí vedení řídilo projekt praktikami označenými {icon}. Ponech, co pomáhá, zruš, co škodí, a zaveď, co chybí.":"The previous management ran the project with the practices marked {icon}. Keep what helps, drop what hurts and introduce what is missing.","Předej provozu všechnu rutinu a žádnou skutečnou projektovou práci.":"Hand all routine work to operations and no real project work.","Předáno do provozu":"Handed over to operations","Předáno provozu":"Handed over to operations","Předání bez předání":"Handover without a handover","Přetížení týmu":"Team overload","Přetížení! Tým nestihne vše a morálka i kvalita utrpí.":"Overload! The team will not finish everything and both morale and quality will suffer.","Převzít projekt":"Take over the project","Přibyla práce: {list}.":"New work added: {list}.","Přidáno {n} / {max}":"Added {n} / {max}","Přidáno: {added} · odebráno: {removed}":"Added: {added} · removed: {removed}","Přijatelná volba":"Acceptable choice","Přizpůsobivý":"Adaptable","Příliš velká položka":"Item too large","Přírůstek si vyzkoušeli na review.":"They tried the increment at the review.","Příznaky jsou <b>důsledky</b>. Najdi <b>mechanismy</b>, které je způsobují – antivzorce, které předchozí vedení do projektu zavedlo. Pozor, ne všechny nabízené v projektu působí.":"Symptoms are <b>consequences</b>. Find the <b>mechanisms</b> causing them – the anti-patterns the previous management brought into the project. Careful: not all of the ones offered are at work in this project.","Realizace: {n} {unit} do cíle":"Delivery: {n} {unit} to the finish","Rezerva je pojistka, ne rozpočet na neplánování. Nejlepší je ta, kterou nepotřebuješ.":"A buffer is insurance, not a budget for not planning. The best one is the one you never need.","Rezerva nedotčena":"Buffer untouched","Rezerva projektu":"Project buffer","Rezerva projektu je vyčerpaná – {d} navíc stojí harmonogram i peníze.":"The project buffer is used up – {d} extra costs schedule and money.","Režie je {n} bod(y) nad rozpočtem – kapacita týmu klesne o {n} každé období.":"Overhead is {n} point(s) over budget – team capacity drops by {n} every period.","Režie řízení":"Management overhead","Rok poté":"A year later","Rozděl a panuj":"Divide and conquer","Rozděl práci":"Split the work","Rozděl příliš velkou položku a dodej všechny její části.":"Split an oversized item and deliver all of its parts.","Rozdělení je zapsané":"Your split is recorded","Rozdělení práce":"Splitting the work","Rozehraná hra: {name}":"Game in progress: {name}","Rozhlížíš se po stavbě a zjišťuješ, že univerzální recept neexistuje.":"You are looking around the construction site and finding out there is no universal recipe.","Rozpočet je vyčerpaný. Sponzor projekt zastavil.":"The budget is exhausted. The sponsor stopped the project.","Rozsah <b>není pevný</b>. Cílem je co nejvíc <b>skutečné hodnoty pro uživatele</b> – měří se trakce po 2., 4. a 6. sprintu.":"The scope is <b>not fixed</b>. The goal is as much <b>real value for users</b> as possible – traction is measured after sprints 2, 4 and 6.","Ruda Gantt s deskami s Ganttovým diagramem míchá kotel praktik a Bára Backlogová s tabletem do něj přihazuje lístečky. Z páry stoupá na jedné straně harmonogram s milníky, na druhé šipky iterací a nahoře se spojí do zelené fajfky.":"Ruda Gantt, holding a clipboard with a Gantt chart, stirs the cauldron of practices while Bára Backlogová, holding a tablet, drops sticky notes into it. On one side the steam rises as a schedule with milestones, on the other as iteration arrows, and at the top they merge into a green check mark.","Rutina, která se řídila jako projekt, zůstala bez vlastníka v linii. Po skončení projektu ji nikdo nedělá.":"Routine work that was run as a project has no owner in the line organization. After the project ends, nobody does it.","Rutinu od začátku dělala linie – po projektu se nic nerozpadlo.":"The line organization handled routine work from the start – nothing fell apart after the project.","S praktikou pro harmonogram by úkoly seřadil nástroj.":"With a scheduling practice, a tool would sort the tasks for you.","Sběratel vzorců":"Pattern collector","Senior PM":"Senior PM","Seřadit co nejdřív podle závislostí":"Schedule as early as dependencies allow","Skryté":"Hidden","Skrytý faktor":"Hidden factor","Skrytý odznak":"Hidden badge","Skrytý odznak.":"Hidden badge.","Skutečnost":"Actual","Skutečné hodnoty ukazatelů – během hry jsi je viděl(a) jen v mlze reportingu.":"Actual metric values – during the game you saw them only through the reporting fog.","Skutečné ukazatele na konci":"Actual metrics at the end","Skvělé – každá část má přístup, který jí sedí.":"Great – every part has an approach that suits it.","Sleduj pět ukazatelů projektu; když některý spadne na nulu, projekt končí.":"Watch the five project metrics; if any drops to zero, the project ends.","Sleduj pět ukazatelů projektu; když některý spadne na {n}, projekt končí.":"Watch the five project metrics; if any drops to {n}, the project ends.","Slovníček":"Glossary","Slovníček řízení projektů":"Project management glossary","Slož mix praktik":"Build a practice mix","Složíš mix praktik, který sedí na kontext projektu a nepadá do pastí.":"You build a practice mix that fits the project context and avoids the traps.","Smazat veškerý postup":"Delete all progress","Soulad s kontextem":"Fit with the context","Současná pozice":"Current position","Sprint po sprintu, nebo etapu po etapě. Plánuj, řeš krize, hlídej milníky.":"Sprint by sprint or stage by stage. Plan, handle crises, watch the milestones.","Sprinty":"Sprints","Správná diagnóza":"Correct diagnosis","Správně: {answer}.":"Correct: {answer}.","Spustit {acc} {n}":"Start {acc} {n}","Stabilní provoz":"Stable operations","Stakeholdeři":"Stakeholders","Stakeholdeři:":"Stakeholders:","Stav projektu":"Project status","Styl řízení":"Management style","Synergie":"Synergy","Synergie a konflikty":"Synergies and conflicts","Synergie a konflikty praktik musíš odhadnout sám/sama.":"You have to judge synergies and conflicts between practices yourself.","Série incidentů":"A string of incidents","Tabulka hodnot":"Table of values","Testeři si stěžují na čím dál víc chyb.":"Testers complain about more and more bugs.","Tip: Jak jasné jsou požadavky? Jak drahá je změna v průběhu? Dá se výsledek dodávat po kouscích? Projekt nemusí být hybridní.":"Tip: How clear are the requirements? How expensive is a change midway? Can the result be delivered in pieces? A project does not have to be hybrid.","Tohle je {label}":"This is {art} {label}","Tohle nebyla výhra. Přesčasy jako rezerva kapacity jen odkládají účet – zaplatí ho kvalita a lidé.":"That was not a win. Overtime as a capacity reserve only postpones the bill – quality and people pay it.","Tohle rozhodnutí bude mít dohru.":"This decision will have consequences later.","Tvůj mix je nastavený":"Your mix is set","Tvůj mix praktik byl nastavený pro původní situaci. Zvaž, které praktiky nová situace vyžaduje – a které už nedávají smysl.":"Your practice mix was set up for the original situation. Consider which practices the new situation needs – and which no longer make sense.","Tvůj mix praktik působí celou dobu – a až na konci uvidíš, jaké <b>vzorce a antivzorce</b> v projektu vytvořil.":"Your practice mix works the whole time – and only at the end will you see which <b>patterns and anti-patterns</b> it created.","Tvůj mix praktik působí celou dobu – a postupně odhalíš, jaké <b>vzorce a antivzorce</b> v projektu vytvořil.":"Your practice mix works the whole time – and you will gradually uncover which <b>patterns and anti-patterns</b> it created.","Tvůj mix:":"Your mix:","Tvůj nástroj pro harmonogram umí úkoly jedním kliknutím <b>seřadit co nejdřív podle závislostí</b>.":"Your scheduling tool can <b>sort tasks as early as dependencies allow</b> with one click.","Tvůj rekord v tomto projektu: {n} bodů":"Your record in this project: {n} points","Tým":"Team","Tým má <b>několik profesí</b> (dělníci, svářeči, jeřáb) a každá má vlastní kapacitu – hlídej každou zvlášť.":"The team has <b>several trades</b> (workers, welders, a crane), each with its own capacity – watch each one separately.","Tým na konci":"The team at the end","Tým nevyužil velkou část kapacity, i když byla dostupná práce.":"The team left much of its capacity unused even though work was available.","Tým se rozešel":"The team broke up","Tým se rozpadl – většina lidí odešla.":"The team fell apart – most people left.","Tým se zavázal k víc práci, než zvládne. Nedokončené položky se vrací zpět, lidé jsou vyčerpaní a sliby nesplněné.":"The team committed to more work than it can handle. Unfinished items go back, people are exhausted and promises are broken.","Tým zůstal":"The team stayed","Tým:":"Team:","Tři hvězdy znamenají, že řízení sedělo na povahu projektu – nejen že to nějak dopadlo.":"Three stars mean the management fit the nature of the project – not just that it somehow worked out.","U každé oblasti projektu rozhodni, zda ji řídit <b>prediktivně</b> (plán předem, vodopád) nebo <b>agilně</b> (iterace, zpětná vazba) – nebo jestli to vůbec není projekt, ale běžný <b>provoz</b>, který patří linii.":"For each area of the project, decide whether to manage it <b>predictively</b> (plan up front, waterfall) or <b>agilely</b> (iterations, feedback) – or whether it is not a project at all but regular <b>operations</b> that belong to the line organization.","U každé oblasti projektu rozhodni, zda ji řídit <b>prediktivně</b> (plán předem, vodopád) nebo <b>agilně</b> (iterace, zpětná vazba).":"For each area of the project, decide whether to manage it <b>predictively</b> (plan up front, waterfall) or <b>agilely</b> (iterations, feedback).","U převzatého projektu najdi všechny antivzorce a žádný navíc.":"In an inherited project, find all the anti-patterns and no extra ones.","Udržitelnost výsledku: {n} %":"Sustainability of the result: {n} %","Události":"Events","Ukazatel":"Metric","Unavení lidé po projektu odešli – i s tím, co věděli.":"Exhausted people left after the project – and took their knowledge with them.","Uprostřed {gen} se něco stalo…":"Something happened mid-{gen}…","V Ganttu kliknutím nastavíš začátek každého úkolu a vyznačíš <b>závislosti</b> – po kterých úkolech smí začít. Hlídej, kolik lidí je který den potřeba: tým má omezenou velikost.":"In the Gantt chart, click to set the start of each task and mark its <b>dependencies</b> – which tasks it may start after. Watch how many people are needed each day: the team is limited.","V agilním projektu se vyplatí iterace, Product Owner, ověřování hypotéz a průběžné zlepšování. Detailní plán by stál na neověřených předpokladech.":"In an agile project, iterations, a Product Owner, hypothesis testing and continuous improvement pay off. A detailed plan would rest on untested assumptions.","V jednom projektu se potkávají prvky, které sedí tradičnímu, i prvky, které sedí agilnímu přístupu. Proto potřebuje <b>hybridní řízení</b>: nejde o dva samostatné projekty s různými metodikami (to by byl program), ale o kombinaci prvků obou přístupů v jednom projektu.":"This project combines parts that suit a traditional approach and parts that suit an agile one. That is why it needs <b>hybrid management</b>: not two separate projects with different methods (that would be a program), but a combination of both approaches within one project.","V každé etapě přijde <b>událost</b>; některé volby odemyká jen správná praktika. Po 2. etapě tě čeká <b>kontrolní den</b>.":"Every stage brings an <b>event</b>; some options are unlocked only by the right practice. After stage 2 there is a <b>checkpoint review</b>.","V prediktivním projektu se vyplatí detailní plán s kritickou cestou, řízení změn a rizik a přesné měření stavu. Agilní ceremonie by tu byly jen režií.":"In a predictive project, a detailed plan with a critical path, change and risk control, and precise progress tracking pay off. Agile ceremonies would only be overhead here.","V tomto projektu se žádný vzorec neprojevil.":"No pattern showed up in this project.","V tomto typu projektu zbytečná režie":"Unnecessary overhead for this type of project","Ve velmi obtížném projektu udrž celý tým a morálku aspoň 60.":"In a very difficult project, keep the whole team and morale at 60 or more.","Ve výluce se nestihlo: {list}. Práce se přesouvá do další výluky.":"Not finished within the closure: {list}. The work moves to the next closure.","Velmi dobrá práce. Pár rozhodnutí šlo udělat lépe – mrkni na poučení níže.":"Very good work. A few decisions could have been better – check the lessons below.","Velmi obtížná úroveň":"Very difficult level","Veškerý postup je smazaný. Můžeš začít od začátku.":"All progress has been deleted. You can start from scratch.","Vodopád tam, kde sedí":"Waterfall where it fits","Vrací se dřívější rozhodnutí…":"An earlier decision comes back…","Vrátilo se {n} dříve odložených problémů.":"{n} previously postponed problems came back.","Vrátit jde jen během plánování, ve kterém položka odešla. Po spuštění {gen} ji převzal provoz.":"You can return an item only during the planning in which it left. Once the {gen} starts, operations take it over.","Vrátit zpět do backlogu":"Return to the backlog","Vyber praktiky, kterými budeš projekt řídit. Každá stojí <b>režii řízení</b> (porady, reporty, schvalování) – rozpočet je {n} bodů. Hledej kombinace, které se doplňují a sedí na tento typ projektu.":"Choose the practices you will run the project with. Each one costs <b>management overhead</b> (meetings, reports, approvals) – the budget is {n} points. Look for combinations that complement each other and fit this type of project.","Vyber si projekt":"Choose a project","Vyhodnotit":"Evaluate","Vyhodnotit projekt":"Evaluate the project","Vyžaduje praktiku: {p}":"Requires practice: {p}","Vzorce a antivzorce řízení projektů, které jsi odhalil(a) ve svých hrách. Každý popisuje, <b>v jakém kontextu</b> a <b>jakou formou</b> se projekt řídil, <b>jakým mechanismem</b> to působilo a <b>jaký to mělo důsledek</b>. Neobjevené odhalíš jinými projekty a mixy praktik.":"The project management patterns and anti-patterns you uncovered in your games. Each one describes <b>in what context</b> and <b>in what form</b> the project was managed, <b>by what mechanism</b> it worked and <b>what consequence</b> it had. Uncover the rest with other projects and practice mixes.","Vzorce – mechanismy, které vytvářejí hodnotu":"Patterns – mechanisms that create value","Vzorce, které tvůj projekt vytvořil":"Patterns your project created","Vzorec je mechanismus, ne recept: funguje jen v kontextu, pro který vznikl.":"A pattern is a mechanism, not a recipe: it works only in the context it came from.","Víc praktik neznamená lepší řízení. Každá porada a report stojí čas, který chybí na práci.":"More practices do not mean better management. Every meeting and report costs time that is missing for the work.","Výborná volba":"Excellent choice","Výluka skončila podle plánu.":"The closure ended as planned.","Výluka skončila s nedodělky ({n}). Přesouvají se do další výluky.":"The closure ended with unfinished work ({n}). It moves to the next closure.","Výsledek: {n} z {all} správně":"Result: {n} of {all} correct","Výuková hra o řízení projektů: poznej, jestli projekt potřebuje plán, agilitu, nebo hybrid, a namíchej správné praktiky.":"An educational game about project management: find out whether a project needs a plan, agility or a hybrid, and brew the right practices.","Všechny projekty základní úrovně aspoň za ★★":"All basic-level projects with at least ★★","Všichni stakeholdeři řešení po roce aktivně používají a podporují.":"A year later, all stakeholders actively use and support the solution.","Z minulé výluky se přesunulo: {list}.":"Carried over from the last track closure: {list}.","Z projektu je teď <b>{now}</b> (dosud {before}).":"The project is now a <b>{now}</b> (previously a {before}).","Za 2 měsíce":"2 months later","Za 3 měsíce":"3 months later","Za 5 měsíců":"5 months later","Za 7 měsíců":"7 months later","Za 9 měsíců":"9 months later","Za měsíc":"A month later","Za rok":"A year later","Zadavatel přestal odpovídat na e-maily.":"The client has stopped answering emails.","Zadání je <b>pevně dané</b> – {contract}. Každá položka má jasnou hodnotu a priority dává smlouva (MoSCoW).":"The scope is <b>fixed</b> – {contract}. Every item has a clear value and the contract sets the priorities (MoSCoW).","Zahodit":"Discard","Zamčeno":"Locked","Zasáhni do mixu praktik":"Adjust the practice mix","Zatím nehráno":"Not played yet","Zatím žádná praxe. Dokonči první projekt.":"No experience yet. Finish your first project.","Zatím žádné synergie ani konflikty.":"No synergies or conflicts yet.","Zavedeno: {added} · zrušeno: {removed}":"Introduced: {added} · removed: {removed}","Zavřít":"Close","Začínající PM":"Junior PM","Začíná po":"Starts after","Začít diagnózou":"Start with a diagnosis","Zbytečná režie pro tento typ projektu: {list}":"Unnecessary overhead for this type of project: {list}","Zbytečné vazby: {list} – úkoly mohly běžet souběžně.":"Unnecessary links: {list} – the tasks could have run in parallel.","Zbývá dokončit <b>{n}</b> Must položek ({period} {s} z {all}).":"<b>{n}</b> Must items left to finish ({period} {s} of {all}).","Zdraví projektu":"Project health","Zdržení z událostí a okolností: {d}.":"Delay from events and circumstances: {d}.","Zkušený projektový manažer":"Experienced project manager","Zmizí rekordy a hvězdy ve všech projektech, kariéra a odznaky, objevené vzorce v atlasu, rozehraná hra a odemčené úrovně. Vrátit to nejde.":"Records and stars in all projects, career and badges, discovered patterns in the atlas, the game in progress and unlocked levels will be gone. This cannot be undone.","Změna kontextu":"Context change","Změna kontextu · po {loc} {n}":"Context change · after {loc} {n}","Změna kontextu: {title}":"Context change: {title}","Znalec průšvihů":"Connoisseur of disasters","Znalosti zůstaly v týmu":"The knowledge stayed in the team","Zrušit":"Cancel","Zrušit praktiku předchozího vedení nic nestojí. Každá nově zavedená praktika stojí −1 {b} a −1 {m} (změna zaběhnutého procesu v krizi). Nově zavedeno: {n}.":"Dropping a practice of the previous management costs nothing. Every newly introduced practice costs −1 {b} and −1 {m} (changing an established process in a crisis). Newly introduced: {n}.","Ztracená podpora":"Lost support","Ztratily hodnotu: {list}.":"Lost value: {list}.","Zvenku zelený, uvnitř červený. Když reporting ukazuje procenta místo hotové práce, pravda přijde pozdě.":"Green outside, red inside. When reporting shows percentages instead of finished work, the truth arrives late.","Základ":"Base","Základní úroveň":"Basic level","Základy pro {label}":"Essentials for a {label}","Základy pro {label} v tvém mixu":"Essentials for a {label} in your mix","Zásah do mixu praktik":"Intervention in the practice mix","Zásah je hotový":"The intervention is done","Závazek <b>{c} SP</b> při kapacitě <b>{cap} SP</b>":"Commitment <b>{c} SP</b> at a capacity of <b>{cap} SP</b>","Získej aspoň ★★ s mixem praktik nejméně o 3 body levnějším, než je rozpočet režie.":"Get at least ★★ with a practice mix at least 3 points under the overhead budget.","Získej ★★★ v agilně řízeném projektu.":"Get ★★★ in an agile project.","Získej ★★★ v libovolném projektu.":"Get ★★★ in any project.","Získej ★★★ v prediktivně řízeném projektu.":"Get ★★★ in a predictively managed project.","Získej ★★★ ve velmi obtížném projektu.":"Get ★★★ in a very difficult project.","Získej ★★★ ve všech hybridních projektech základní úrovně.":"Get ★★★ in all hybrid basic-level projects.","agilně":"agilely","agilně řízené prvky":"agile-managed parts","beze změny metrik":"no change in metrics","chybně: {list}":"wrong: {list}","chyběly základy: {list}":"missing essentials: {list}","dnem {d}":"on day {d}","do provozu":"to operations","etapě":"stage","fáze a milníky":"phases and milestones","hodnota pro uživatele":"value for users","hranice selhání":"failure threshold","k dispozici {n}":"{n} available","kapacita týmu −{n} každé období":"team capacity −{n} every period","konec každé etapy":"end of each stage","kritická cesta":"critical path","mix beze změny":"mix unchanged","namíchej správné řízení pro každý projekt":"brew the right management for every project","nedokončeno – zpět mezi nedodělané":"unfinished – back to the open items","nejdřív {d}. den":"not before day {d}","nejvíc {stars}":"best {stars}","neodhalený vliv":"undiscovered influence","nestihlo se {n} úkolů":"{n} tasks not finished","nic":"nothing","nikdo neumí":"nobody knows it","nově":"new","náročná úroveň":"hard level","odchází z projektu":"is leaving the project","odebráno":"removed","odehráno {n}×":"played {n}×","odešel{a}":"left","odešel{a} z projektu":"left the project","odhad ~{est} → skutečnost <b>{act}</b>":"estimate ~{est} → actual <b>{act}</b>","omylem předáno: {list}":"handed over by mistake: {list}","ověřené hypotézy: {n}":"hypotheses tested: {n}","ověřit":"test","pasti: {list}":"traps: {list}","plán do dne {finish} z {days}, konflikty {conflicts}, přetížení {over}":"plan ends on day {finish} of {days}, conflicts {conflicts}, overload {over}","plán po vlnách":"rolling-wave plan","plánovaná práce {p} MD, skutečná {a} MD":"planned work {p} PD, actual {a} PD","po 2 týdnech":"every 2 weeks","podle plánu":"as planned","prediktivně":"predictively","prediktivně řízené prvky":"predictively managed parts","propojení obou přístupů":"linking both approaches","provoz – není to projekt":"operations – not a project","provozu předáno {n} z {all} rutinních úkolů":"{n} of {all} routine tasks handed to operations","průměr 5 ukazatelů":"average of 5 metrics","přerušeno, den navíc":"interrupted, one extra day","přesah etap {o} · rezerva {b}":"stage overrun {o} · buffer {b}","přesah {d}":"overrun {d}","přetéká":"overflowing","převzal provoz":"taken over by operations","přidáno {added}, odebráno {removed}":"added {added}, removed {removed}","příprava projektu":"project preparation","přístup, mix praktik a rozhodnutí":"approach, practice mix and decisions","rok poté":"a year later","rozděleno: {note}":"split: {note}","rozdělit":"split","s":"with","sedí na kontext projektu":"fits the project context","skutečně po: <b>{list}</b>":"actually after: <b>{list}</b>","skutečně {f} z {d} dní":"actually {f} of {d} days","sprintu":"sprint","sprinty":"sprints","správně {hits} z {all} · navíc: {wrong} · přehlédnuto: {missed}":"{hits} of {all} correct · extra: {wrong} · missed: {missed}","této oblasti":"this area","týden {a}–{b}":"week {a}–{b}","těchto oblastech":"these areas","udržitelnost výsledku":"sustainability of the result","ukazatele a stakeholdeři":"metrics and stakeholders","uloženo {when}":"saved {when}","v projektu se dělalo: {list}":"done inside the project: {list}","velmi obtížná úroveň":"very difficult level","vhoď první praktiku":"add your first practice","vrátit":"return","vyhořel{a} a odchází":"burned out and is leaving","vůle {d}":"float {d}","z {d}":"of {d}","zavedl předchozí PM":"introduced by the previous PM","zdarma":"free","zdržení {d}":"delay {d}","základní úroveň":"basic level","závislosti":"dependencies","závislosti a inspekce":"dependencies and inspections","{area} umí jen {name}":"only {name} knows {area}","{a} po {b}":"{a} after {b}","{a} smí začít až po skončení {b}":"{a} may start only after {b} finishes","{d} dní · nahrubo {r}":"{d} days · roughly {r}","{d} dní · podrobný Gantt":"{d} days · detailed Gantt","{id}: začít dnem {d}":"{id}: start on day {d}","{label} na den":"{label} per day","{label}: odhad {lo}–{hi}, stav k minulému období":"{label}: estimate {lo}–{hi}, as of the previous period","{lock} – dostupné od {gen} {n}":"{lock} – available from {gen} {n}","{name} je na hraně sil.":"{name} is close to breaking point.","{name} na {n} části":"{name} into {n} parts","{name} se naučil{a}: {area}":"{name} learned: {area}","{name} – dokončení":"{name} – completion","{nom} přetáhla o {d} a rezerva projektu nestačila.":"The {nom} overran by {d} and the project buffer was not enough.","{nom} přetáhla o {d}, zatím to pokryla rezerva projektu.":"The {nom} overran by {d}; the project buffer has covered it so far.","{nom} skončila v plánované délce.":"The {nom} finished on schedule.","{nom} {k} – projekt skončil":"{nom} {k} – the project ended","{nom} {n} z {all}":"{nom} {n} of {all}","{nom} {n} z {all} · konec":"{nom} {n} of {all} · end","{nom} {n} z {all} · probíhá":"{nom} {n} of {all} · in progress","{n} SP kapacita {next}":"{n} SP capacity in the {next}","{n} b.":"{n} pts","{n} bodů":"{n} points","{n} skutečné hodnoty":"{n} real value","{n} z {all}":"{n} of {all}","{n} z {all} oblastí správně":"{n} of {all} areas correct","{n} ze 3 hvězd":"{n} of 3 stars","{n} ★ z {all} · odehráno her: {g}":"{n} ★ of {all} · games played: {g}","{product} běží spolehlivě a provoz hlásí jen drobnosti.":"{product} runs reliably and operations report only minor issues.","{product} funguje, ale každý měsíc se něco opravuje.":"{product} works, but something needs fixing every month.","{product} padá a opravy stojí víc, než projekt ušetřil.":"{product} keeps crashing and the fixes cost more than the project saved.","{p} vzorců, {a} antivzorců. Každý je zapsaný jako řetězec kontext → forma → mechanismus → důsledek.":"{p} patterns, {a} anti-patterns. Each is written as a chain of context → form → mechanism → consequence.","Úkol":"Task","Únava":"Fatigue","Únava roste prací v oblasti, kterou člověk umí (čím méně lidí ji umí, tím víc), přesčasy a přetížením. Kdo je vyčerpaný, odejde.":"Fatigue grows with work in a person’s own area (the fewer people know it, the more), overtime and overload. Whoever is exhausted leaves.","Úspěch projektu se pozná až po roce: jestli řešení žije, lidé ho umí a stakeholdeři ho chtějí.":"A project’s success shows only a year later: whether the solution lives on, people know it and stakeholders want it.","Úzká hrdla":"Bottlenecks","únava {n}":"fatigue {n}","Časová osa projektu":"Project timeline","Čistá agilita":"Pure agility","Čistý stůl":"Clean slate","Číslo na ose je konec {gen}. Pod osou jsou rozhodnutí ({ratings}) a odhalené vzorce ({patterns}) z daného období – najeď na graf pro detail.":"The numbers on the axis mark the end of each {gen}. Below the axis are the decisions ({ratings}) and revealed patterns ({patterns}) of each period – hover over the chart for details.","čekal na inspekci ({d}. den)":"waited for the inspection (day {d})","čekal na předchůdce ({d})":"waited for its predecessor ({d})","čekal na volné lidi ({d})":"waited for free people ({d})","čerpáno {d}":"used {d}","Ředitel PMO":"Head of PMO","Řiď projekt":"Run the project","Řídicí výbor zasedá":"The steering committee meets","Řídicí výbor ztratil důvěru a odvolal tě z projektu.":"The steering committee lost confidence and removed you from the project.","Řídíš i v horších podmínkách: s menším rozpočtem, se skrytými faktory a s rozhodnutími, která se vracejí.":"You manage even in tougher conditions: a smaller budget, hidden factors and decisions that come back.","Řízení jsi přizpůsobil(a) nové situaci":"You adapted your management to the new situation","Špatná volba":"Poor choice","Špatně zvolený přístup se v projektu projeví:":"A poorly chosen approach will show in the project:","Štíhlá režie":"Lean overhead","Životopis":"Résumé","Životopis projektového manažera":"Project manager résumé","Žádná z praktik necílí na kontext projektu.":"None of the practices targets the project context.","Žádné nápovědy, mlha v reportech, stakeholdeři, kteří chtějí každý něco jiného, konkrétní lidé, kteří se unaví nebo odejdou, rutina převlečená za projekt – a na konci se ukáže, co z projektu zbylo po roce.":"No hints, fog in the reports, stakeholders who all want something different, real people who get tired or leave, routine work disguised as a project – and at the end you see what is left of the project a year later.","žádné":"none","žádné praktiky":"no practices","– problém":"– problem","– se zpožděním":"– late","„{label}“ položky odstraněny":"“{label}” items removed"}, {"METRICS":[{"id":"rozpocet","label":"Budget"},{"id":"harmonogram","label":"Schedule"},{"id":"kvalita","label":"Quality"},{"id":"spokojenost","label":"Satisfaction"},{"id":"moralka","label":"Team morale"}],"MOSCOW":{"M":{"label":"Must","title":"Must have – no launch without it"},"S":{"label":"Should","title":"Should have – important, but not critical"},"C":{"label":"Could","title":"Could have – if time allows"},"W":{"label":"Won't","title":"Won't have this time – deliberately postponed"}},"CONTEXT_TAGS":{"zavislost":{"label":"Strong dependencies between parts"},"regulace":{"label":"Regulation and audits"},"verejny":{"label":"Public money – transparency matters"},"pevny_termin":{"label":"A deadline that can't move"},"nejistota_trhu":{"label":"Uncertain user response"},"bezpecnost":{"label":"Safety and certification"},"zmena_u_lidi":{"label":"Changing people's ingrained habits"},"pevne_okno":{"label":"A time window that can't move"},"jasne_zadani":{"label":"Clear, stable requirements"},"omezene_zdroje":{"label":"Money for just a few months"},"rychla_zpetna_vazba":{"label":"Users available for quick feedback"},"komunita":{"label":"A vocal player community"}},"PRACTICES":[{"id":"plan","name":"Schedule with milestones","desc":"A Gantt chart with dependencies, dates and milestones for work that can be planned.","mech":"Schedules tasks in the Gantt as early as dependencies allow. In a hybrid, milestones are met at 📅 ≥ 45 (without a plan only at ≥ 55). +5 📅"},{"id":"ccb","name":"Formal change control","desc":"The steering committee reviews changes to scope, contracts and plan by their impact on time, cost and risk.","mech":"Guards against uncontrolled extra work. +4 💰 +3 📅"},{"id":"risk","name":"Risk register and contingency reserve","desc":"Risks with response plans, plus a reserve of money and time set aside.","mech":"Event losses of 💰 and 📅 are 40% smaller. Unlocks “use the reserve” choices. −5 💰 for the reserve."},{"id":"detailgantt","name":"Detailed Gantt for the whole project","desc":"Every app feature gets a fixed date in the plan. The committee loves certainty.","mech":"The committee is thrilled. +6 😊 +3 📅. Also works as the scheduling tool."},{"id":"ccball","name":"One change board for everything","desc":"Every change – even in the backlog – is approved by a monthly board. Same rules for everyone.","mech":"Tight cost control. +5 💰, team capacity −1."},{"id":"cpm","name":"Critical path and project buffer","desc":"Analysis shows which activities must not slip and keeps a shared time buffer at the end of the project.","mech":"Shows the critical path and task float in the Gantt. +2 days of project buffer. +3 📅"},{"id":"evm","name":"Earned Value Management (EVM)","desc":"Measures work actually done against plan and cost (SPI, CPI). Assumes fixed scope.","mech":"Management sees the exact project status. +5 😊 +3 💰"},{"id":"sync","name":"Weekly sync of both approaches","desc":"The leads of the predictively and agilely managed work meet weekly to go over dependencies and risks.","mech":"Negative impacts of events at the interface of both approaches (🔗) are 30% smaller. +3 ⭐"},{"id":"integrace","name":"Shared integration milestones","desc":"The plan has points where outputs of predictively and agilely managed work must meet and be tested together.","mech":"+4 📅. Together with the sync, lowers the bar for meeting milestones by 10."},{"id":"dashboard","name":"Transparent committee dashboard","desc":"Milestones, budget, risks and work actually delivered (increments, burn-up) on a single page.","mech":"+6 😊. The committee sees the real project status."},{"id":"gate","name":"Stage gate with a live demo","desc":"At checkpoints the committee reviews both milestones and increments that actually work.","mech":"An extra +5 😊 at the stage gate."},{"id":"znalosti","name":"Knowledge sharing","desc":"Pair work, lightweight documentation and handover meetings across both parts.","mech":"+3 ⭐. Protects the project when a key person drops out."},{"id":"prescasy","name":"Overtime as a capacity reserve","desc":"When things catch fire, the team stays late. It costs nothing.","mech":"Team capacity +2 each period. Morale −4 each period."},{"id":"scrum","name":"Scrum in two-week sprints","desc":"Planning, daily, review and retrospective; a finished increment every 2 weeks.","mech":"At the review, users see the value: delivered value raises 😊 in full. +3 ⭐"},{"id":"kanban","name":"Kanban with WIP limits","desc":"A smooth flow of work with a cap on tasks in progress.","mech":"Overloading a sprint hurts less (💪 −3 instead of −8). Delivered value raises 😊 in full."},{"id":"po","name":"Product Owner with mandate and time","desc":"Someone from the user side decides the backlog order and is available to the team.","mech":"+6 😊 +3 ⭐. Without a PO, satisfaction drops every sprint."},{"id":"retro","name":"Retrospectives","desc":"After each sprint the team reviews what to improve in how it works.","mech":"Morale +2 each sprint."},{"id":"dod","name":"Strict Definition of Done","desc":"Done = tested, documented and compliant with the rules (security, GDPR).","mech":"Quality +2 each sprint."},{"id":"lean","name":"Hypotheses and experiments","desc":"Build–Measure–Learn: before building a feature, the team cheaply checks whether users actually want it.","mech":"During planning you can cheaply verify the real value of up to 2 uncertain items per sprint. +2 ⭐"}],"WORLD_LABEL":{"pred":"📐 Predictive practices","hybrid":"🔗 Bridging and shared practices","agile":"🔄 Agile practices"},"PRACTICE_PAIRS":[{"text":"Sprints with retrospectives: the team learns every two weeks."},{"text":"Smooth flow with regular improvement."},{"text":"Increments are truly done, not “almost done.”"},{"text":"Integration milestones that predictively and agilely managed work prepare for continuously."},{"text":"The committee reviews expensive changes, the PO decides cheap ones."},{"text":"The committee decides based on the real status."},{"text":"A plan that accounts for risks."},{"text":"Sprints inside a plan where everything is set in advance."},{"text":"Smooth flow vs. a fixed date for every feature."},{"text":"The PO can't decide when a board approves everything."},{"text":"Sprint feedback waits a month for approval."},{"text":"Double planning – pointless overhead."},{"text":"Two change control processes for the same thing."},{"text":"Retrospectives keep exposing fatigue, but nothing changes."},{"text":"WIP limits and overtime work against each other."},{"text":"A plan that shows what must not slip."},{"text":"Risks are watched mainly on the critical path."},{"text":"Exact project status figures in one place."},{"text":"The Product Owner decides based on validated data."},{"text":"Every sprint is also an experiment."},{"text":"EVM assumes fixed scope; sprints change it."},{"text":"Experiments vs. a preset date for every feature."}],"ESSENTIALS":{"hybrid":[{"name":"Iterative framework for agilely managed parts"},{"name":"Product Owner role"},{"name":"Plan for predictively managed parts"},{"name":"Bridging both approaches"},{"name":"Risk management"},{"name":"Transparent reporting"}],"pred":[{"name":"Detailed plan"},{"name":"Critical path and buffer"},{"name":"Change management"},{"name":"Risk management"},{"name":"Measuring status against the plan"}],"agile":[{"name":"Iterative framework"},{"name":"Product Owner role"},{"name":"Validating hypotheses"},{"name":"Continuous improvement"},{"name":"Increment quality"}]},"APPROACHES":{"hybrid":{"label":"Hybrid project"},"pred":{"label":"Predictive project"},"agile":{"label":"Agile project"}},"PATTERNS":[{"id":"integracni_milnik","name":"Integration milestone","story":"At the integration milestone, the outputs of both parts turned out to fit together. Two minor mismatches were fixed on the spot.","k":"The agile part depends on output from the predictive part (equipment delivery, approved layout, machines).","f":"Shared integration milestones in the plan + a weekly sync of the leads of both parts.","m":"Interface problems surface early, while fixing them is cheap. Both parts know when they're waiting on each other.","d":"Smoother integration and lower risk of missed milestones."},{"id":"ucici_se_tym","name":"Learning team","story":"At the retrospective, the team proposed shorter dailies and testing in pairs. It works.","k":"A new team, a new domain and requirements still taking shape.","f":"Short iterations ending with a retrospective.","m":"Every two weeks the team reviews how it works and introduces one improvement.","d":"Quality and morale rise steadily."},{"id":"dvourychlostni","name":"Two-speed governance","story":"Users wanted three features tweaked – the PO added them to the backlog within a day. Meanwhile, a change in the predictive part went through a proper review.","k":"One project has both expensive changes (construction, contracts) and cheap ones (software).","f":"Formal change control only for the predictive part; the Product Owner decides the backlog.","m":"Expensive changes get careful review; cheap ones are decided fast and close to users.","d":"A stable plan for the predictive part alongside flexible development."},{"id":"transparentni_gate","name":"Transparent stage gate","story":"The committee looked at the dashboard and tried the finished features themselves. The decision took 20 minutes.","k":"The steering committee decides whether the project continues and needs credible input.","f":"A stage gate with a hybrid dashboard and a live demo of finished features.","m":"The committee judges the real status, not the promised one; problems are handled openly.","d":"A fast, informed decision and growing sponsor trust."},{"id":"pripravena_rezerva","name":"Reserve at the ready","story":"The risk hit, but the response plan and the reserve were ready.","k":"A predictive part with foreseeable risks (deliveries, construction surprises, weather).","f":"A risk register with response plans and a dedicated contingency reserve.","m":"When a risk hits, you draw on the reserve per the prepared plan instead of crisis replanning.","d":"Smaller event impacts on budget and schedule."},{"id":"hotovo_je_hotovo","name":"Done means done","story":"The quality check found no hidden loose ends in the delivered increments.","k":"A regulated or safety-critical environment plus pressure for speed.","f":"A strict Definition of Done, including tests and compliance.","m":"Quality is built into every item continuously, not bolted on at the end.","d":"Fewer hidden defects, smoother audits."},{"id":"sdilene_knowhow","name":"Shared know-how","story":"In sprint 5 a key person fell ill. Thanks to shared knowledge, colleagues covered for them with no trouble.","k":"A temporary project team where key knowledge sits with a few people.","f":"Pair work, lightweight documentation and handover meetings.","m":"Knowledge spreads through the team and doesn't hinge on individuals.","d":"Losing a person doesn't endanger the project, and the results can be maintained afterward."},{"id":"water_scrum_fall","name":"Sprints set in concrete","story":"The team asks: “Why do we hold reviews when every feature's date is fixed in advance anyway?”","k":"An organization used to detailed planning introduces an agile team.","f":"Sprints inside a detailed plan where every feature has a fixed date.","m":"Sprint feedback can't change the plan; the team delivers the schedule “in chunks” and keeps rewriting the Gantt.","d":"Agile rituals without agile benefits, a frustrated team, declining quality."},{"id":"zamrzly_backlog","name":"Frozen backlog","story":"After the review, users wanted a small tweak. The board will discuss it in a month.","k":"A push for uniform rules and tight cost control.","f":"One monthly change board also approves changes in the agile part's backlog.","m":"Small tweaks wait weeks for approval; the team builds to outdated requirements.","d":"Lower capacity and falling user satisfaction."},{"id":"byrokraticky_hybrid","name":"Bureaucratic hybrid","story":"The team worked out that meetings, reports and approvals eat up almost a third of its time.","k":"An urge to take “the best of both worlds” and leave nothing out.","f":"Lots of practices from both approaches at once – more than the project can carry.","m":"Management overhead eats into time for real work.","d":"Team capacity drops by each point of overhead over budget."},{"id":"chaos","name":"Management without rules","story":"Two people did the same work, and everyone forgot about one important dependency.","k":"Pressure for a quick start and a belief that “management slows us down.”","f":"Minimal rules, roles and coordination.","m":"Nobody knows who decides; nobody watches dependencies and risks.","d":"Mistakes and slippage every sprint."},{"id":"bez_vlastnika","name":"Ownerless backlog","story":"The team delivered a feature no user cared about. The important one never made it in.","k":"An agile team without a clear user representative.","f":"The backlog is prioritized by the team or whoever is loudest at the moment.","m":"Priorities follow volume and technical appeal, not value.","d":"Less important things get delivered, satisfaction drops."},{"id":"bez_zpetne_vazby","name":"Building blind","story":"Users haven't seen anything yet – and nobody knows whether the team is building the right thing.","k":"Uncertain user requirements.","f":"An agile part with no iterative framework – no sprints, reviews or smooth flow.","m":"Users see the result only at the end; mistakes are discovered late.","d":"Delivered value raises satisfaction only halfway, and quality drops."},{"id":"slepy_plan","name":"Predictive part without a plan","story":"At the first milestone it turned out the orders went out late – nobody was tracking lead times.","k":"Predictive work with long lead times and fixed dependencies.","f":"No schedule for the predictive part – “we'll figure it out as we go.”","m":"Nobody tracks dependencies and lead times; orders are placed late.","d":"Milestones demand a much better schedule and are often missed."},{"id":"melounovy_reporting","name":"Watermelon reporting","story":"Reports were green for months. At the stage gate, the committee saw the real status for the first time.","k":"The committee wants to see “green numbers” and the project lacks transparent reporting.","f":"Reporting percent complete against the plan, with no demos of finished work.","m":"Problems stay hidden until they can't be – green outside, red inside.","d":"A sudden loss of trust at the stage gate."},{"id":"hrdinske_tempo","name":"Heroic pace","story":"The team is running flat out. The two most experienced people are thinking of leaving.","k":"A fixed deadline and growing slippage.","f":"Overtime and overloaded sprints as a permanent capacity reserve.","m":"More work in the short term; fatigue, mistakes and departures in the long term.","d":"Falling morale and quality."},{"id":"ostrov_znalosti","name":"Knowledge island","story":"In sprint 5, the only person who understood a key part of the solution fell ill. Work stalled for a week.","k":"A temporary team where key know-how sits with individuals.","f":"No systematic knowledge sharing.","m":"When a key person drops out, work stops and nobody knows how things work.","d":"A quality slump at the end of the project – and a risk the results can't be maintained long term."},{"id":"agilni_divadlo","name":"Agile theater","story":"At the “sprint review,” fitters show off a half-dismantled turbine. Nobody knows what users are supposed to comment on.","k":"A project with clear requirements, prescribed procedures and expensive changes.","f":"Sprints, a backlog, a Product Owner or experiments for work with a set procedure.","m":"The ceremonies expect change that never comes; there's nothing to iterate on.","d":"Overhead with no benefit and a frustrated team."},{"id":"bduf","name":"Big plan, uncertain brief","story":"The team builds features per the plan from week one, even though the data already shows users want something else.","k":"An uncertain market – nobody knows what users really want.","f":"A detailed plan, critical path or fixed scope up front (Big Design Up Front).","m":"The plan rests on unvalidated assumptions; the team sticks to the plan instead of the data.","d":"Things get built that nobody wants, and satisfaction drops."},{"id":"hybrid_za_kazdou_cenu","name":"Hybrid at any cost","story":"A weekly “sync of both approaches” – except the project only has one. The meeting lasts five minutes and everyone wonders why they're there.","k":"A project with a single character (fully predictive or fully agile).","f":"Hybrid bridging practices even when there's nothing to bridge.","m":"Coordinating an interface that doesn't exist just burns time.","d":"Pointless overhead. Hybrid isn't automatically better – it's a tool for projects with two faces."},{"id":"vodopad_kde_sedi","name":"Waterfall where it fits","story":"The unit was shut down exactly to plan. Every crew knows when it's up, and nobody waits on anybody.","k":"Clear, stable requirements, prescribed procedures, a fixed window and expensive changes.","f":"A detailed plan with a critical path and formal change management.","m":"Everyone knows what to do and when; expensive changes are reviewed before they're made.","d":"The project fits in the window and isn't caught off guard by what could be foreseen."},{"id":"kriticka_cesta","name":"Managed critical path","story":"When one task ran late, the team knew right away whether it pushed back the project end or had float.","k":"A project with many dependencies and a fixed end date.","f":"Critical path analysis and a shared project buffer (instead of padding hidden in every activity).","m":"Attention and people go where delays push back the project end; the buffer is used deliberately.","d":"Delays to individual tasks needn't threaten the deadline."},{"id":"build_measure_learn","name":"Build–Measure–Learn","story":"A landing page and five interviews in one afternoon saved a week of building a feature nobody wanted.","k":"High uncertainty and limited money.","f":"Hypotheses and cheap experiments before building features.","m":"The team learns before spending time and money; the backlog follows validated value.","d":"More real value for the same work."},{"id":"tovarna_na_funkce","name":"Feature factory","story":"The team shipped five features in three sprints. Users use two.","k":"A startup under pressure to show progress.","f":"Success is measured by features shipped; hypotheses go untested.","m":"Building follows guesses and wishes, not validated user interest.","d":"Much of the work brings no value, and the money runs out."},{"id":"adaptivni_rizeni","name":"Adaptive management","story":"When the situation changed, the team adjusted how it manages before the problem could grow.","k":"A project whose conditions change midway (regulation, market, deadline).","f":"Regular review of the methodology and a willingness to reshuffle practices on the fly.","m":"Practices match the current context, not the one from the project kickoff.","d":"The project handles the change without lasting damage."},{"id":"strnula_metodika","name":"Rigid methodology","story":"The context changed, but the team carries on “by the book.” Problems pile up every period.","k":"A project whose conditions have changed.","f":"A methodology set at the start and never changed afterward.","m":"Practices solve yesterday's problems; nobody systematically handles new demands.","d":"Losses of quality and trust every period."},{"id":"zametene_pod_koberec","name":"Swept under the rug","story":"A problem once “solved” by postponing it or patching it up came back – bigger.","k":"Pressure for speed and an unpleasant problem mid-project.","f":"Postponing, hushing up or a cheap stopgap instead of fixing the root cause.","m":"The problem grows in the meantime and returns at the worst possible moment.","d":"A costlier fix later and a loss of trust."},{"id":"investice_se_vraci","name":"An investment that pays off","story":"A decision that cost something back then has now paid off.","k":"A decision with an immediate cost and a later benefit.","f":"A willingness to pay today for prevention, quality or relationships.","m":"Investing in prevention shrinks future problems and opens up opportunities.","d":"Fewer crises and new opportunities later."}],"GATE_EVENT":{"id":"gate","title":"Stage Gate: halfway through","text":"You're halfway through the project. The steering committee ({committee}) decides whether to let the project into its final phase. How will you prepare the materials?","lesson":"A stage gate in a hybrid project assesses predictive milestones (contracts, handovers) as well as the value actually delivered by the agile part – ideally through a live demo.","choices":[{"text":"A 100-page document with a detailed plan for every remaining feature","feedback":"Writing it took the team a week, and the committee didn't read it anyway."},{"text":"Milestone and budget status + a live demo of finished features + a scope forecast","feedback":"Committee members tried the finished features themselves. Project approved with enthusiasm."},{"text":"Ask for a postponement until the agile part is entirely done","feedback":"Postponing the gate means uncertainty for everyone. And the agile part will never be “entirely done.”"}]},"GENERIC_EVENTS":[{"id":"pretizeni","title":"The team is overloaded","text":"Two agile team members are sick and the rest are running flat out. The Product Owner still pushes for more features.","lesson":"A sustainable pace is the foundation of agility. And beware Brooks's law: adding people to a late project slows it down even more in the short term.","choices":[{"text":"Lower the commitment next sprint and let people catch their breath","feedback":"The next sprint will be smaller, but the team comes back at full strength and without fatigue-induced mistakes."},{"text":"Order overtime","feedback":"Looks good in the short term, but fatigue = mistakes and frustration."},{"text":"Hire two contractors right away","feedback":"New people need onboarding and take up the veterans' time. Help arrives only later."}]},{"id":"datum","title":"“When will EVERYTHING be done?”","text":"A steering committee member wants an exact date when absolutely every feature in the backlog will be done.","lesson":"Hybrid projects often fix time and budget and keep the agile part's scope flexible. A burn-up forecast is more honest than a promise.","choices":[{"text":"Promise that absolutely everything will be done by launch day","feedback":"The committee is happy – for now. The team is under pressure from an impossible promise."},{"text":"Show a burn-up chart: Must features for sure, Should likely, Could maybe","feedback":"The committee appreciated the honesty and understood it will get the most important things by the fixed date."},{"text":"“We're agile, we don't do deadlines.”","feedback":"Agility is no excuse for opacity. The committee is losing trust."}]},{"id":"po","title":"The Product Owner has no time","text":"The Product Owner is swamped with day-to-day work and answers the team's questions by email days later.","lesson":"Product Owner availability is critical. Without quick decisions, the team either waits or builds the wrong things.","choices":[{"text":"Agree with the sponsor on dedicated time for the PO (and a deputy)","feedback":"The PO now has two mornings a week just for the team. Decisions are fast."},{"text":"The team will decide on its own","feedback":"The team guesses what {users} would want – and sometimes misses."},{"text":"The project manager takes over the PO role","feedback":"It works, but the PM no longer keeps up with managing the predictive part and doesn't know the needs of {usersGen} as well."}]},{"id":"gantt","title":"A Gantt for the agile part too?","text":"A new steering committee member is used to Gantt charts. They want one for the agile part too, with a date for every feature.","lesson":"A hybrid PM “translates” between worlds: agile progress can be shown in the language of milestones (releases, increments) without micro-planning every feature.","choices":[{"text":"Draw a Gantt with a date for every user story","feedback":"The plan is outdated after the first sprint and the team keeps rewriting it."},{"text":"A Gantt with release milestones (v1 at launch) + a list of delivered increments","feedback":"The new committee member got an overview in a form they understand, and the team can keep working agilely."},{"text":"Ignore the request","feedback":"The committee member starts distrusting the project."}]},{"id":"drobnost","title":"“Just one tiny thing…”","text":"The project sponsor ({sponsor}) comes straight to team members every week with “tiny” requests. The team handles them on the side and sprint goals fall apart.","lesson":"All requests for the agile part go through the Product Owner and the backlog. Work “on the side” destroys transparency and planning.","choices":[{"text":"Politely redirect them to the Product Owner – requests go into the backlog","feedback":"The sponsor grumbled for a while, but at the review they see their ideas in the backlog, ordered by value. The team has a clear sprint goal again."},{"text":"The team keeps handling the tiny things – it's the sponsor, after all","feedback":"Hidden work outside the backlog: the sprint plan is void and nobody knows where capacity goes."},{"text":"Forbid the sponsor from talking to the team","feedback":"The team gets peace, but the sponsor feels shut out. Communication should flow – just through the right role."}]},{"id":"dluh","title":"Technical debt is growing","text":"The team warns that it cut corners in the rush. The solution is fragile and every new feature takes longer.","lesson":"Technical debt needs to be paid down continuously. It's an investment in a sustainable pace, not “wasted time.”","choices":[{"text":"Reserve a slice of capacity in every sprint for paying down debt","feedback":"The next sprint is a bit smaller, but the pace stabilizes over time."},{"text":"Deal with the debt after launch","feedback":"Debt accrues interest: bugs pile up and fixing them after launch will cost more."},{"text":"Spend the whole next sprint on cleanup","feedback":"The solution is cleaner, but stakeholders see no new value for a whole sprint."}]},{"id":"smlouva","title":"Contract with an external vendor","text":"An outside firm handles part of the development. Procurement wants a fixed-price contract with a detailed scope for the whole project.","lesson":"Agile work with contractors is covered by agile contracts: fixed time and budget, variable scope (or pay-per-sprint with an exit option).","choices":[{"text":"Fixed price + fixed scope written down right now","feedback":"Every backlog change now means a contract amendment and negotiation. Agility is tied up."},{"text":"Framework contract: fixed budget and deadline, scope prioritized via the backlog","feedback":"Procurement gets price certainty, the Product Owner gets freedom over priorities. A classic agile contract."},{"text":"Pay for hours worked, with no cap","feedback":"Flexible, but without a ceiling you're gambling with the budget."}]},{"id":"hodiny","title":"Estimates in hours","text":"The CFO wants an hour estimate for every backlog item and will check who “went over” by how much.","lesson":"Story points and velocity give a more reliable forecast than detailed hour estimates. Measure the team, not individuals.","choices":[{"text":"Explain relative estimates and show a forecast based on team velocity","feedback":"A forecast from real data is more accurate than adding up hours. The team doesn't waste time on timesheets."},{"text":"Break everything down into hours and report variances","feedback":"The team spends hours estimating and reporting. And the estimates are still inaccurate."},{"text":"Ignore the request","feedback":"The CFO now sees the project as a black hole for money."}]},{"id":"spor","title":"Fight over a shared environment","text":"The predictive part's lead and the Scrum Master are arguing: both need the only test environment and the same technicians in the same week.","lesson":"A hybrid PM resolves conflicts over shared resources transparently – by dependencies and impact on goals, not by who's louder.","choices":[{"text":"Meet, lay out the dependencies and agree on an order by impact on milestones","feedback":"Both left with an agreement they understand. Next time they'll sort it out at the sync."},{"text":"Rule in favor of the predictive part – it has a fixed plan, after all","feedback":"The agile team feels like the “minor league.” Testing keeps getting postponed."},{"text":"Escalate straight to the steering committee","feedback":"The committee sorted it out, but a week later. And it asks why the project couldn't handle it alone."}]},{"id":"nefunguje","title":"Done, but broken","text":"At the sprint review it turns out a feature marked “done” doesn't work in the real environment. It ran fine on the developer's machine.","lesson":"A clear Definition of Done and a “blameless” approach to mistakes: look for the cause in the process, not a culprit.","choices":[{"text":"Tighten the Definition of Done: done = tested in a production-like environment","feedback":"A few items now take a hair longer, but “done” means done again."},{"text":"Find out who broke it","feedback":"The team starts hiding mistakes. Blame never helps improve the process."},{"text":"Fix it and carry on unchanged","feedback":"This bug is gone, but the cause remains – it'll happen again."}]},{"id":"daily","title":"Sponsor at the daily scrum","text":"The sponsor ({sponsor}) has started attending every daily scrum, grilling individuals and handing out tasks.","lesson":"The daily scrum is the team's planning meeting, not a report to the boss. Stakeholders have their place at the sprint review.","choices":[{"text":"Explain the point of the daily and invite them to the sprint review to see results","feedback":"At the review the sponsor eagerly tries out finished features, and the daily belongs to the team again."},{"text":"Let it be, they're the boss","feedback":"The team stopped talking about problems at the daily. All they report is “everything's fine.”"},{"text":"Better cancel the daily","feedback":"The problem is gone – and so is the team's daily coordination."}]},{"id":"velocity","title":"Velocity contest","text":"Management proposes: the team with the highest velocity gets a bonus. Velocity will also be compared across teams.","lesson":"Velocity is the team's planning tool, not a performance metric. Once it becomes a target, it stops working (Goodhart's law).","choices":[{"text":"Decline and propose measuring delivered value and user satisfaction","feedback":"Management adopted different metrics. The team focuses on outcomes, not numbers."},{"text":"Agree – motivation is good","feedback":"Estimates mysteriously start to “grow.” Velocity goes up, value doesn't."},{"text":"Agree, but compare only with the team's own past","feedback":"The lesser evil, but the team still starts inflating estimates."}]},{"id":"rizika","title":"Dusty risk register","text":"You find that nobody has opened the risk register since the initial phase. The agile part isn't in it at all.","lesson":"Risk management is an ongoing activity. In a hybrid, track the risks of both parts and their interface – ideally as part of the regular sync.","choices":[{"text":"Add a short risk review of both parts to the weekly sync","feedback":"The very first review surfaced two new interface risks. Now they have response plans."},{"text":"Nobody reads the register anyway – scrap it","feedback":"Without an overview of risks, the next problem will catch you unprepared."},{"text":"Update it once in a big workshop and then forget about it","feedback":"It's current for a while; in a month it'll be dusty again."}]},{"id":"pilot","title":"A pilot run?","text":"The Product Owner proposes releasing some finished features to a small group of users before the full launch.","lesson":"Delivering value early and in small steps reduces risk. A pilot run is a typical bridge between agile development and a fixed launch date.","choices":[{"text":"Yes – a pilot with a small group and regular feedback collection","feedback":"Pilot users found three unclear spots that would otherwise have hit hundreds of people at once."},{"text":"No, everything gets revealed at once at launch","feedback":"Big bang: bugs and misunderstood features surface only when everyone hits them at once."},{"text":"Pilot yes, but we'll process the feedback after launch","feedback":"Users are glad to see something, but their input is gathering dust for now."}]},{"id":"komise","title":"One change board for everything","text":"The quality manager proposes unifying the rules: every change, even in the agile part's backlog, must go through a change board that meets once a month.","lesson":"Hybrid governance runs at several speeds: formal change control where changes are expensive, quick PO decisions where they're cheap.","choices":[{"text":"Two levels: the board for predictive-part changes, the Product Owner runs the backlog","feedback":"The quality manager is happy to have expensive changes under control, and the agile team stays fast."},{"text":"Agree – uniform rules are fair","feedback":"The agile team now waits a month to get a small tweak approved. Agility is gone."},{"text":"Scrap change control entirely – agility everywhere","feedback":"In the predictive part, anyone can now change the requirements. Extra work and chaos."}]},{"id":"specialista","title":"One specialist for both approaches","text":"The only security specialist is supposed to work for the predictive and agile parts at the same time and can't keep up.","lesson":"Shared resources are a typical bottleneck in hybrid projects. Plan them centrally around critical milestones and pass the knowledge on.","choices":[{"text":"Schedule their time around milestones and gradually pass knowledge to the team","feedback":"The specialist knows when they're needed where, and the team learns from them. The bottleneck shrinks."},{"text":"Let the teams ask for them – first come, first served","feedback":"The specialist rushes between teams and finishes nothing. Both teams wait."},{"text":"Hire a second full-time specialist","feedback":"It helps, but it's expensive and the new person is still getting up to speed."}]},{"id":"agile_hype","title":"Agile fever","text":"A new head of innovation convinced management that “everything is done agile these days.” They want this project to run in sprints too, with a backlog and a Product Owner.","lesson":"Agile isn't universally better. Where requirements are clear and change is expensive, the plan wins. Individual agile practices can be borrowed if they add something.","choices":[{"text":"Explain why a critical-path plan fits here; borrow only the useful bits (short daily meetings, retrospectives)","feedback":"The head of innovation got that agility is a tool, not a goal. The team likes the daily meetings at the board."},{"text":"Switch to sprints and a backlog","feedback":"A fixed assembly sequence now gets “prioritized” every two weeks. Dependencies fall apart."},{"text":"Comply on paper only – rename stages to sprints","feedback":"Nothing changed but the names. The team laughs about it, management is happy – for now."}]},{"id":"plan_na_rok","title":"A year-ahead feature plan","text":"A potential investor wants a detailed plan of every app feature for the year ahead, with dates.","lesson":"In an uncertain environment you plan goals and hypotheses, not features. A year-long feature plan is a guess built on unvalidated assumptions.","choices":[{"text":"Show a roadmap of goals and hypotheses, traction metrics and how we make data-driven decisions","feedback":"The investor appreciated that the team knows what it measures and why. No feature plan needed."},{"text":"Write a detailed feature plan for the whole year","feedback":"Writing it took a week, and the plan was outdated after the first user test."},{"text":"Just give them the launch date","feedback":"The investor is uneasy – they don't know what the team bases decisions on."}]}],"SKILLS":{"lide":{"label":"People"},"obecne":{"label":"Workers"},"svarec":{"label":"Welders"},"jerab":{"label":"Crane"}},"GLOSSARY":[["Hybrid project management","An approach to project management that combines elements of traditional and agile project management to gain the advantages and suppress the drawbacks of both, thereby increasing project success. It balances flexibility, efficiency, productivity and control over the project. The ability to tailor the mix to specific needs makes it suitable for managing projects in many different contexts."],["Continuum of approaches","From purely agile, through tailored and combined agile methods, hybrid management, combined and tailored traditional methods, to purely traditional. Hybrid sits in the middle: it combines elements of both the traditional and the agile approach in a single project."],["What hybrid management is not","It's not tailoring an agile or traditional approach, it's not combining practices within one of them, and it's not a temporary mix of practices during a transition from one approach to the other."],["Predictive approach (waterfall)","Scope, time and cost are planned up front; phases follow one another. Suits clear, stable requirements (construction, procurement)."],["Agile approach","Working in short iterations with frequent feedback. Suits requirements that are uncertain or evolving (software, design)."],["Scrum","An agile framework: sprints, roles (Product Owner, Scrum Master, developers) and events (planning, daily, review, retrospective)."],["Sprint","A time-boxed iteration (typically 2 weeks) that ends with a finished, usable product increment."],["Daily Scrum","A short daily team meeting to plan work for the next day. It's not a report to the boss."],["Product Backlog","An ordered list of everything the product might contain. Managed by the Product Owner."],["Product Owner (PO)","The person accountable for maximizing product value; decides the order of backlog items."],["Story point (SP)","A relative estimate of an item's effort. The team compares items with each other, not in hours."],["Capacity / velocity","How many story points the team can handle per sprint. Used for planning, not for performance reviews."],["MoSCoW","Prioritization: Must (must have), Should (should have), Could (could have), Won't (not this time)."],["MVP","Minimum Viable Product – the smallest version of a product that already delivers value and lets you gather feedback."],["Milestone","A significant point in time (e.g., contract signing, building handover), often with a fixed date."],["Stage gate (phase gate)","A checkpoint between phases where the steering committee decides whether the project continues."],["Change control","A formal process for assessing and approving changes in the predictive part (impact on time, cost, risk)."],["Definition of Done (DoD)","A shared agreement on when an item is truly done (tested, documented, compliant…)."],["Burn-up chart","A chart of work delivered over time vs. total scope. Shows a forecast of what will get done."],["Risk register","A list of identified risks with probability, impact and response plan. Should be updated continuously."],["Technical debt","The consequences of shortcuts and quick fixes. If it isn't paid down, every further change costs more."],["Agile contract","A contract with fixed time and budget but variable scope driven by the backlog."],["Blameless approach","When mistakes happen, look for the cause in the process, not a culprit. Then people don't hide mistakes."],["Pilot run","Rolling out part of the solution to a small group of users before the full launch, to get feedback and reduce risk."],["Iron triangle","The relationship of scope, time and cost. Changing one affects the others; quality shouldn't be the “victim.”"],["Brooks's law","“Adding manpower to a late software project makes it later.” New people need onboarding."],["Projectification","The growing share of work organized as projects. It can bring flexibility as well as dysfunction (overload, loss of knowledge)."],["Pattern / anti-pattern","A recurring solution that creates value (pattern) or dysfunction (anti-pattern) in a given context. In the game it's described by the chain context → form → mechanism → consequence."],["Management overhead","The time and energy spent on meetings, reports and approvals. Every practice brings something, but it also costs something."],["WIP (work-in-progress) limit","A Kanban cap on the number of tasks in progress. Prevents overload and speeds up finishing."],["Water-Scrum-Fall","A hybrid model with the TAT pattern: traditional phases at the start (requirements, plan, contract), agile sprints in the middle and traditional phases at the end (testing, acceptance). One of the best-known hybrid models."],["Sprints set in concrete","Anti-pattern: sprints inside a plan where every feature has a fixed date in advance. The rituals stay, the benefits of agility vanish. Not to be confused with Water-Scrum-Fall – that phases the whole life cycle but keeps agile development inside it flexible."],["Gantt chart","A schedule of tasks as bars on a timeline of days, including the dependencies between them. A core tool of predictive planning."],["Person-day (PD)","A unit of effort: one person's work for one day. A 3-day task for 2 people = 6 PD. In predictive projects it replaces story points."],["Rolling wave planning","The nearest stage is planned in detail, later ones only roughly (milestones, effort estimates), and they are refined step by step."],["Resource leveling","Adjusting the schedule so that no day needs more people than the team has."],["Critical path (CPM)","The longest chain of dependent activities. A delay in any of them pushes back the project end; other activities have float."],["Project buffer","A shared time buffer at the end of the project that covers delays on the critical path."],["Earned Value Management (EVM)","A method of measuring project status: compares planned work, work actually done and costs (SPI, CPI)."],["Build–Measure–Learn","The Lean Startup cycle: build the smallest possible experiment, measure how users react and learn before you invest more."],["Pivot","A fundamental change in product strategy based on validated learning."],["Big Design Up Front (BDUF)","Trying to design and plan everything in detail up front. Fine with clear requirements, harmful under high uncertainty."],["Goodhart's law","“When a measure becomes a target, it ceases to be a good measure.” Typically velocity as a bonus metric."]],"SCENARIOS":[{"id":"druzice","stars":{"ko":[{"text":"Quality at least 25 – or the satellite fails in orbit"}],"top":[{"text":"Vacuum chamber test passed"},{"text":"Vibration test passed"}]},"name":"Student Satellite","tagline":"A small satellite and a launch window that won't wait","scope":"A small research satellite: structure, electronics, solar panels, onboard software, ground station and vacuum chamber tests. The rocket launch is booked for a specific day.","intro":"You lead a student team building a small research satellite. A seat on the rocket is booked – miss the launch and you fly a year later, which the grant wouldn't survive.","predWorld":"Structure, electronics, long-lead component purchasing, vibration and vacuum tests, launch certification.","agileWorld":"Onboard software, ground station and data processing. Tuned iteratively against a simulator, then against the real hardware.","terms":{"launch":"the rocket launch","predShort":"structure, electronics, tests","agileShort":"onboard and ground software","users":"scientists","usersGen":"scientists","sponsor":"head of department","poGood":"scientist who will use the data","committee":"grant agency"},"dependency":{"lock":"Waiting for flight hardware delivery (milestone)","hint":"<b>Software test on flight hardware</b> waits for a predictive milestone – hardware delivery."},"workstreams":[{"id":"konstrukce","name":"Satellite mechanical structure","why":"Size and mass are set by the rocket; drawings get approved and it's built once."},{"id":"nakup","name":"Flight component purchasing","why":"Space-certified parts have months-long lead times and fixed specs."},{"id":"zkousky","name":"Vibration and vacuum tests","why":"Test facilities are booked in advance and the rocket operator prescribes the test procedure."},{"id":"firmware","name":"Power management firmware","why":"Careful: it's software, but safety-critical. It's specified upfront, tested with the hardware and frozen – no last-minute iterations."},{"id":"palubni","name":"Onboard software for science measurements","why":"What the scientists need gets refined along the way; developed iteratively against a simulator."},{"id":"stanice","name":"Ground station and data reception","why":"The software can be built piece by piece and improved even after launch."},{"id":"data","name":"Data processing and visualization","why":"How to process the data only becomes clear from the first images – typical iterative work."},{"id":"skoly","name":"Education program for schools","why":"Content is tuned to teacher and student feedback, version by version."}],"backlog":[{"id":"orientace","name":"Attitude control (against simulator)"},{"id":"komunikace","name":"Communication with Earth"},{"id":"data","name":"Science data storage"},{"id":"safe","name":"Safe mode"},{"id":"test_hw","name":"Software test on flight hardware"},{"id":"prijem","name":"Ground station: data reception"},{"id":"planovani","name":"Automatic image scheduling"},{"id":"komprese","name":"Data compression"},{"id":"aktualizace","name":"Remote software update"},{"id":"mapa","name":"Web map of passes"},{"id":"bot","name":"Satellite on social media"},{"id":"mraky","name":"AI cloud detection"},{"id":"kamera2","name":"Second camera"}],"milestones":[{"id":"m1","name":"Flight hardware","okText":"Flight hardware is delivered. From sprint 3 the software can be tested on the real board.","lateText":"Hardware delivery slipped. Tests on the flight board can't start until sprint 4."},{"id":"m2","name":"Vacuum chamber","okText":"The vacuum chamber integration test passed: software and hardware work together.","lateText":"The vacuum chamber integration test failed."},{"id":"m3","name":"Vibration test","okText":"The satellite passed the vibration test.","lateText":"The vibration test slipped and has to be repeated."},{"id":"m4","name":"Rocket launch","failText":"The satellite wasn't ready for launch. The rocket left without it – the project failed.","okText":"The satellite is on the rocket and lifting off! The first signal is coming in from orbit.","lateText":"The satellite is incomplete – missing:"}],"shift":{"title":"The launch moves up","text":"The rocket's main payload is ready early – the launch moves two weeks forward. There's less time left than the team planned, and it can't be moved. Revealed factor: an immovable time window.","lesson":"When time shrinks and the deadline is absolute, freeze the configuration, let any further change through formal change control only – and cut scope deliberately. Otherwise last-minute tweaks break what was already verified."},"gate":{"id":"gate","title":"Critical Design Review (CDR)","text":"Agency experts assess whether the satellite design is mature enough to build the flight model. What will you present?","lesson":"A design review in a hybrid project judges hardware by documentation and tests, and software by what actually works on the simulator.","choices":[{"text":"Hardware documentation, test results and a live software demo on the simulator","feedback":"The review passed. The experts appreciated that you don't show software just on slides."},{"text":"Documentation only – we'll show the software once it's done","feedback":"The review passed with a caveat: \"Software is a big risk.\" You got an extra audit."},{"text":"Ask to postpone the review","feedback":"Postponing the review pushes back the flight model build. The launch won't wait, though."}]},"events":[{"id":"freeze","title":"When to freeze the software?","text":"Before integration you must decide when to \"freeze\" the onboard software. After the freeze, changes go only through formal change control.","lesson":"For systems that are hard to fix after launch, freeze the core in time and design the rest to be updatable. Tweaking until the last minute is a gamble.","choices":[{"text":"Freeze the core (attitude, comms, safe mode), keep developing the rest with remote updates","feedback":"The core is stable and tested. Science features can be tuned even after launch."},{"text":"Freeze nothing and keep tweaking until the last minute","feedback":"The team has freedom – for now."},{"text":"Freeze absolutely everything right now","feedback":"Stable, but the scientists are disappointed: half of their requests didn't make it."}]},{"id":"baterie","title":"Batteries delayed","text":"The certified battery supplier reports a three-week delay.","lesson":"In space projects, backup suppliers and response plans are prepared in advance. Certification shortcuts don't pay off.","choices":[{"text":"Call in the backup certified supplier from the risk register","feedback":"The backup supplier was vetted. The batteries arrived only a week late."},{"text":"Wait and shorten the thermal tests","feedback":"The schedule holds; the tests are shorter."},{"text":"Buy cheaper uncertified batteries","feedback":"The batteries arrived right away. Their paperwork didn't."}]},{"id":"kamera","title":"Scientists want a different camera","text":"After the demo the scientists declare the mission pointless without a better camera. But the camera is hardware and the design is almost done.","lesson":"A change touching hardware goes through change control with an impact analysis. Part of the need can often be met with software.","choices":[{"text":"Analyze the impact via change control and offer software image enhancement","feedback":"The analysis showed a new camera would exceed the mass limit. Software sharpening satisfied the scientists."},{"text":"Give in – swap the camera","feedback":"The scientists are thrilled. The engineers, less so."},{"text":"Refuse without discussion","feedback":"The design is protected, but the scientists are losing the will to cooperate."}]},{"id":"student","title":"Lead programmer is leaving","text":"The student who wrote the communication protocol is leaving for a semester abroad.","lesson":"In temporary teams, knowledge sharing is insurance. Without it, the project depends on a single person.","choices":[{"text":"Pair programming and documentation now, remote collaboration later","feedback":"The sprint is slower, but three people now understand the protocol."},{"text":"Let it be, it'll work out somehow","feedback":"The student left. The code stayed."},{"text":"Pay them to leave only after the launch","feedback":"They stayed, but the knowledge is still in just one head."}]},{"id":"sroub","title":"Loose screw","text":"During a preliminary vibration test, a screw on the antenna mount came loose.","lesson":"With hardware defects, look for the cause in the procedure, not just that one screw. Otherwise the defect pops up elsewhere.","choices":[{"text":"Investigate the assembly procedure and check all similar joints","feedback":"Two more under-tightened screws turned up. The assembly procedure is fixed."},{"text":"Tighten that one screw and move on","feedback":"The screw is tight. Nobody checked the others."},{"text":"Repeat the whole vibration test","feedback":"The test passed, but nobody looked for the cause."}]},{"id":"zprava","title":"Report for the grant agency","text":"The grant agency wants a progress report with a detailed Gantt – software included.","lesson":"Hybrid reporting \"translates\": Gantt and milestones for hardware, delivered increments and a forecast for software.","choices":[{"text":"Gantt and milestones for hardware + an overview of delivered software increments","feedback":"The agency got an overview it understands, and the team doesn't have to plan every feature."},{"text":"A detailed Gantt for every software feature","feedback":"The plan is outdated after the first sprint."},{"text":"Send just a written narrative","feedback":"The agency asked for more details."}]}],"followups":{"freeze_chaos":{"id":"freeze_chaos","title":"Last change broke the comms","text":"A week before integration, a final \"tiny tweak\" to the software broke communication with Earth.","lesson":"Without a frozen configuration, any change can break a verified whole. The safe move is to roll back to the last tested version.","unresolvedText":"A bug from the last unfrozen change showed up in orbit.","choices":[{"text":"Roll back to the last tested version and add the change via change control","feedback":"Comms work again. The new feature will wait."},{"text":"Keep fixing on the fly until integration","feedback":"The fix broke two more things."},{"text":"Postpone the integration test","feedback":"There's time for a fix, but the launch didn't get any further away."}]},"prehrivani":{"id":"prehrivani","title":"Electronics overheating","text":"The shortened thermal test missed a problem: in vacuum, the board overheats.","lesson":"Shortened tests only seem to save time. The defect is found later – at a higher price.","unresolvedText":"The satellite overheats in orbit and must run in a limited mode.","choices":[{"text":"Add a heat sink and redo the full thermal test","feedback":"Problem solved, and the test was complete this time."},{"text":"Throttle performance in software and hope","feedback":"The scientists lose half their measurements."},{"text":"Swap the board for a different type","feedback":"Expensive, but it works."}]},"certifikace":{"id":"certifikace","title":"Certification rejected the batteries","text":"The rocket operator rejected the uncertified batteries. Without replacements, the satellite won't fly.","lesson":"Skimping on certification comes back with interest. The rocket operator's rules are not up for negotiation.","unresolvedText":"The uncertified batteries surfaced only at the final inspection.","choices":[{"text":"Order certified ones immediately with express delivery","feedback":"Painful, but the satellite will fly."},{"text":"Tweak the paperwork so it passes","feedback":"The fraud came out. The agency is considering clawing back the grant."},{"text":"Request an exemption","feedback":"An exemption takes weeks and may not go through."}]},"hmotnost":{"id":"hmotnost","title":"The satellite is too heavy","text":"The new camera is 200 grams heavier. The satellite exceeds the rocket's mass limit.","lesson":"A hardware change without impact analysis has knock-on effects. That's why it goes through change control.","unresolvedText":"The excess mass was solved at the last minute by stripping equipment.","choices":[{"text":"Go back to the original camera and explain it to the scientists","feedback":"It hurts, but the satellite will fly."},{"text":"Remove the backup battery","feedback":"The mass fits, but the satellite now has no energy reserve."},{"text":"Pay for a bigger slot on the rocket","feedback":"The grant can carry it – barely."}]},"protokol":{"id":"protokol","title":"Nobody understands the protocol","text":"There's a bug in the communication protocol, and the only person who understands it is abroad and not responding.","lesson":"A knowledge island shows up exactly when time is shortest. Sharing knowledge is cheaper upfront.","unresolvedText":"A bug in the protocol nobody understood limited data reception.","choices":[{"text":"Two people study and document the protocol, even if it slows the sprint","feedback":"Bug found, and more people now understand the protocol."},{"text":"Rewrite the protocol from scratch","feedback":"The new protocol has new bugs."},{"text":"Hire an outside expert","feedback":"The expert found the bug. The knowledge left with them."}]},"antena":{"id":"antena","title":"The antenna didn't deploy","text":"During the final test the deployable antenna didn't open – a different screw came loose in exactly the same way.","lesson":"Fixing the symptom instead of the cause just postpones the problem. The same defect shows up elsewhere.","unresolvedText":"After launch the antenna only opened halfway.","choices":[{"text":"Now investigate the whole assembly procedure and fix all joints","feedback":"The procedure is fixed. Late, but better than never."},{"text":"Tighten this screw too","feedback":"How many more screws are waiting?"},{"text":"Replace the antenna with a fixed one","feedback":"More reliable, but with a weaker signal."}]}}},{"id":"elektrarna","stars":{"ko":[{"text":"The outage overruns by no more than 3 days – the grid is counting on the plant"}],"top":[{"text":"The project buffer doesn't end up in the red"}]},"name":"Power Plant Outage","tagline":"A unit overhaul in a fixed window","scope":"Preparation and orders, unit shutdown, turbine inspection, pipe replacement, control system update, pressure tests and restart. Procedures are prescribed by standards and equipment manufacturers.","approachText":"Clear and stable requirements, prescribed procedures, a fixed window and a high price for every change. The whole project is best managed predictively: a stage-by-stage plan, a detailed Gantt with a critical path, change and risk management. Agile practices would mostly be overhead here.","intro":"You're managing the planned overhaul of a power plant unit. From preparation to restart you have 46 working days – and every extra day costs millions.","terms":{"launch":"the unit restart","predShort":"the whole project","users":"operations technicians","usersGen":"operations technicians","sponsor":"plant director","poGood":"head of operations","committee":"plant management"},"workstreams":[{"id":"plan","name":"Outage schedule and contractor coordination","why":"Dozens of contractors must take turns in an exact order. Without an upfront plan they'd trip over each other and the window wouldn't be enough."},{"id":"turbina","name":"Turbine inspection per the manufacturer's procedure","why":"The manufacturer prescribes the inspection step by step. Nothing \"emerges\" here – you follow the plan."},{"id":"potrubi","name":"Replacement of worn piping","why":"The scope is known from measurements and parts are ordered months ahead. Classic planned work."},{"id":"ridici","name":"Control system software update","why":"Careful – even though it's software, it's a certified vendor release deployed and tested by an approved procedure. You don't iterate, you plan."},{"id":"bozp","name":"Workplace safety and work permits","why":"The rules come from regulations and every permit is formally issued in advance."},{"id":"logistika","name":"Parts, tools and scaffolding logistics","why":"What must arrive, when and where follows directly from the work schedule."},{"id":"skoleni","name":"Operator training on new equipment","why":"The content is set by the equipment changes and the deadline is fixed – operators must be ready before the restart."},{"id":"zkousky","name":"Pressure tests and unit restart","why":"Tests follow a procedure and criteria set by standards. No room for experiments."}],"phases":[{"id":"p1","name":"Preparation","goal":"Plan, orders, contractor agreements, scaffolding and training.","milestone":{"name":"Ready for the outage"},"tasks":[{"id":"A","name":"Detailed schedule and permits","note":"Without an approved plan nothing can be ordered or contracted."},{"id":"B","name":"Parts order","note":"What exactly to order comes out of the detailed plan."},{"id":"C","name":"Contracts with work contractors","note":"The plan defines the contractors' scope of work."},{"id":"D","name":"Scaffolding erection","note":"Built by the in-house crew from a standard design."},{"id":"E","name":"Contractor safety training","note":"Contractor staff get trained – so their contracts must already be signed."},{"id":"F","name":"Parts and tools staging","note":"Getting ready what was ordered."}]},{"id":"p2","name":"Shutdown and disassembly","goal":"Safely shut down the unit, let it cool and open up the equipment.","milestone":{"name":"Unit disassembled"},"tasks":[{"id":"A","name":"Unit shutdown","note":"The very first step of the outage."},{"id":"B","name":"Equipment cooldown","note":"Only a shut-down unit can cool off."},{"id":"C","name":"Insulation removal","note":"Hands off hot pipes."},{"id":"D","name":"Weld inspection","note":"Welds are only accessible once the insulation is off."},{"id":"E","name":"Turbine casing removal","note":"The turbine has to cool down first, too."}]},{"id":"p3","name":"Repairs and replacements","goal":"Turbine inspection, new piping, boiler and control system repairs.","milestone":{"name":"Repairs done"},"tasks":[{"id":"A","name":"Turbine inspection","note":"The longest job of the stage; the turbine was opened in the last one."},{"id":"B","name":"Pipe replacement","note":"The old piping is stripped of insulation and ready to go."},{"id":"C","name":"Boiler repair","note":"The boiler has been accessible since the last stage."},{"id":"D","name":"Control system update","note":"Vendor software, deployed on the shut-down unit."},{"id":"E","name":"Welding and testing new joints","note":"Welding the newly fitted pipe sections."},{"id":"F","name":"New insulation installation","note":"Insulation goes on the finished piping and the repaired boiler."}]},{"id":"p4","name":"Tests and restart","goal":"Verify everything is tight and working, and put the unit back on the grid.","milestone":{"name":"Unit restart"},"tasks":[{"id":"A","name":"Pressure tests","note":"Verify that the new piping and boiler don't leak."},{"id":"B","name":"Control system test","note":"Simulating operating states on the new software."},{"id":"C","name":"Unit restart","note":"Restart only with verified tightness and tested controls."},{"id":"D","name":"Trial operation","note":"Monitoring the running unit."},{"id":"E","name":"Handover documentation","note":"Written continuously from test reports, doesn't wait for the equipment."}]}],"gate":{"id":"gate","title":"Checkpoint review: outage halfway","text":"Plant management is checking whether the outage is on plan and whether the unit will restart on time. How do you prepare?","lesson":"A checkpoint in a predictive project is about the exact status against the plan: critical path, buffer burn, risks and truly finished work.","choices":[{"text":"Critical path status, buffer burn and top risks + an on-site tour of finished work","feedback":"Management sees the exact status and approved a stronger night shift where slippage looms."},{"text":"A presentation saying everything is \"green\"","feedback":"The director asked about one specific job and the answer didn't match the slides. Trust is gone."},{"text":"Cancel the checkpoint review, we don't have time","feedback":"Management started finding out the status on its own – by touring the foremen on site."}]},"events":[{"id":"trhlina","title":"Crack in a pipe","text":"Non-destructive testing found a crack in one pipe that nobody expected. Fixing it means extra work.","lesson":"Even a predictive project hits surprises. New work gets in through change control, with its impact on the critical path assessed.","choices":[{"text":"Change control: add the repair to the plan and assess the critical path impact","feedback":"The repair was scheduled off the critical path. The stage stretches by a day at most."},{"text":"Keep quiet, the pipe will last a few more years","feedback":"The inspector found the crack in the test report. Now there's a special audit of the whole project."},{"text":"Fix it now and pull people off other work","feedback":"The repair is underway, but other work has stalled – including work on the critical path."}]},{"id":"svarec","title":"No certified welder","text":"The contractor moved its only welder certified for high-pressure piping to another job.","lesson":"A risk register with prepared responses (e.g. backup contractors) turns a crisis into routine.","choices":[{"text":"Call in the backup contractor from the risk register","feedback":"The backup contractor was vetted in advance. A welder showed up the next day."},{"text":"Poach a welder from a competitor at triple the rate","feedback":"It works, but it's expensive and shaky."},{"text":"Let an uncertified worker do the welding","feedback":"The welds failed inspection and must be redone. And a fine is looming."},{"text":"Wait for the welder to come back","feedback":"Pipe work is stalled, and everything that follows with it."}]},{"id":"dily","title":"Turbine blades arrive late","text":"The manufacturer reports the replacement turbine blades will arrive a week late.","lesson":"If you know the critical path, you know what can be reshuffled and what can't – and one late delivery doesn't have to move the project end.","choices":[{"text":"Reshuffle work off the critical path so the float absorbs the delay","feedback":"The team pulled work with float forward. The project end didn't budge."},{"text":"Pay for air freight","feedback":"The blades arrived on time – for the price of a small car."},{"text":"Wait for the blades","feedback":"The turbine inspection is on the critical path – a week of waiting pushes the whole project."},{"text":"Use the old blades and replace them \"some other time\"","feedback":"The manufacturer refused to warranty the turbine."}]},{"id":"navic","title":"\"While we have it all apart…\"","text":"Management wants to use the outage to also replace the lighting in the whole hall and the camera system.","lesson":"In a predictive project the scope is fixed. Every extra request goes through change control – even the one that \"costs nothing\".","choices":[{"text":"Change control: assess the impact and add only what fits off the critical path","feedback":"Lighting will be done next outage; the cameras fit into the float."},{"text":"Add everything to the plan","feedback":"Management is happy, but a big chunk of work just landed in an already tight plan."},{"text":"Refuse without assessment","feedback":"The plan is protected, but management feels brushed off."}]},{"id":"unava","title":"Fatigue on the shifts","text":"Shifts have been running 12 hours a day for weeks on end. Small mistakes are piling up.","lesson":"Fatigue is a safety risk. Even in a fixed window it pays to respect shift limits and keep spare capacity.","choices":[{"text":"Respect shift limits and reinforce the night shift","feedback":"Mistakes dropped and people have the energy for the final push."},{"text":"Add even more overtime","feedback":"The next week: two injuries and one serious assembly error."},{"text":"Give time off only after the unit restart","feedback":"People will hang in there, but the mistakes aren't going away."}]},{"id":"skoronehoda","title":"Near miss on the scaffolding","text":"A wrench fell off the scaffolding and missed a fitter by a meter. Nobody got hurt.","lesson":"Near misses are free warnings. Investigate without blame and adjust the procedure.","choices":[{"text":"Stop scaffolding work, investigate the cause blamelessly and adjust the procedure","feedback":"The scaffolding got nets and tool boxes. People see that safety is taken seriously."},{"text":"Carry on, nothing happened","feedback":"A week later, something heavier fell."},{"text":"Punish the fitter who dropped the wrench","feedback":"Nobody reports near misses anymore."}]},{"id":"sit","title":"The grid wants the unit sooner","text":"The transmission system operator asks to restart the unit two days early because of an expected cold-snap peak.","lesson":"Shortening a deadline is assessed on the critical path. Cutting tests and inspections for speed doesn't pay off.","choices":[{"text":"Check the critical path and offer a partial-load restart without cutting tests","feedback":"The grid operator got partial output early and full output on time."},{"text":"Promise an earlier restart and shorten the tests","feedback":"The tests were rushed and a valve burst during the restart."},{"text":"Refuse","feedback":"The plan holds, but the relationship with the grid operator took a hit."}]}]},{"id":"festival","stars":{"ko":[{"text":"The festival starts with all Must items"},{"text":"Quality at least 30 – no cutting corners on visitor safety"}],"top":[{"text":"All milestones met"}]},"name":"Confluence Festival","tagline":"Stages and permits + app and campaign","scope":"Permits and site build, band contracts, safety, a festival app, ticketing and a campaign.","intro":"You're organizing the first Confluence music festival. In 12 weeks the gates open for 15,000 visitors.","predWorld":"Permits from the authorities, stage construction, band contracts, a safety plan. Fixed deadlines and official approvals.","agileWorld":"Festival app, ticketing, website and a social media campaign. Test, measure, adapt.","terms":{"launch":"the festival opening","predShort":"permits, stages, booking","agileShort":"app and campaign","users":"visitors","usersGen":"visitors","sponsor":"festival director","poGood":"head of visitor services","committee":"festival partners"},"dependency":{"lock":"Waiting for the approved site layout (predictive milestone)","hint":"<b>Site map</b> is waiting for a predictive milestone: approved permits and site layout."},"workstreams":[{"id":"povoleni","name":"Permits from authorities, health and fire departments","why":"Official processes have set deadlines and requirements. You can't iterate on them – they must be planned early and completely."},{"id":"podium","name":"Stage construction and sound equipment","why":"Physical construction with a fixed date and suppliers. Last-minute changes are expensive and dangerous."},{"id":"booking","name":"Band contracts (booking)","why":"Artist contracts are signed months ahead with fixed terms and dates."},{"id":"bezpecnost","name":"Safety plan and event staff","why":"The plan must be approved by the police and fire department. Clear requirements, fixed approval."},{"id":"app","name":"Festival app (lineup, tickets)","why":"Features can be delivered gradually and tuned based on tester feedback."},{"id":"kampan","name":"Social media campaign","why":"Only data will show what works. Short experiments, measurement and adaptation."},{"id":"web","name":"Festival website","why":"Content and features are added continuously; the first version can go live early and then improve."},{"id":"program","name":"Side program by fan vote","why":"The program takes shape gradually based on what fans want – classic iterative work."}],"backlog":[{"id":"program","name":"Festival lineup"},{"id":"tickets","name":"Online ticket purchase"},{"id":"qr","name":"Mobile ticket (QR)"},{"id":"map","name":"Site map"},{"id":"push","name":"Lineup change notifications"},{"id":"scan","name":"Entry check-in (QR scanning)"},{"id":"fav","name":"My lineup (favorite shows)"},{"id":"cashless","name":"Cashless payments on site"},{"id":"a11y","name":"Accessibility (WCAG)"},{"id":"transport","name":"Transport and parking"},{"id":"carpool","name":"Festival carpooling"},{"id":"vote","name":"Encore voting"},{"id":"dark","name":"Dark mode"},{"id":"ar","name":"AR site navigation"},{"id":"game","name":"Festival prize game"},{"id":"stream","name":"Concert livestream"}],"milestones":[{"id":"m1","name":"Permits and layout","okText":"The authorities approved the permits and the site layout. The digital team can build the map from sprint 3.","lateText":"Approvals dragged on. The final layout – and so the map – won't come until sprint 4."},{"id":"m2","name":"Stages and equipment","okText":"The stages are up and the sound is checked. Bring on the dress rehearsal.","lateText":"Stage construction fell behind. Penalties and nervous partners."},{"id":"m3","name":"Festival opening","okText":"The gates are open! Mobile tickets work, and so do the lineup and the map.","lateText":"The festival started, but key features are missing:"}],"events":[{"id":"bourka","title":"Forecast: thunderstorms","text":"The long-range forecast shows a high chance of thunderstorms on festival weekend. The risk is in the risk register.","lesson":"Risks with a response plan and a reserve won't catch you off guard. The predictive and agile parts can each respond in their own way – and complement each other.","choices":[{"text":"Activate the response plan: roofing from the risk reserve + the digital team adds weather alerts to the backlog","feedback":"Partners appreciate the preparedness and visitors will hear about the weather in time."},{"text":"Hope the forecast is wrong","feedback":"Partners ask what the plan is. There isn't one."},{"text":"Move the festival back a week","feedback":"Every contract (bands, stages, permits) has to be redone. Very expensive."},{"text":"Rush-order roofing and pay for it outside the budget","feedback":"With no reserve, it's extra money – and last-minute suppliers charge more."}]},{"id":"headliner","title":"Headliner cancels","text":"Five weeks before the festival, the headliner cancels due to illness.","lesson":"The predictive part (contracts) and the agile part (communication, app) must respond to a crisis in a coordinated way. The agile team can get the change out to people within hours.","choices":[{"text":"Booking secures a replacement per the contract; the digital team quickly updates the lineup and campaign","feedback":"Fans heard about the change from you, replacement included. The wave of outrage quickly faded."},{"text":"Stay silent until the replacement is signed","feedback":"The news leaked on social media before you said a word. Fans are furious."},{"text":"Offer everyone a refund","feedback":"Fair to fans, but the budget took a heavy hit."}]},{"id":"hasici","title":"Fire department wants another exit","text":"During an inspection, the fire department demands another emergency exit. Booths and the stage have to be rearranged.","lesson":"Mandatory (regulatory) changes go through change control in the predictive part – and their impact must flow into the agile part too.","choices":[{"text":"Change control: adjust the layout, update the permits and hand the new map to the digital team","feedback":"The fix took a few days, but everything is approved and the app map matches reality."},{"text":"File an appeal and change nothing","feedback":"The appeal failed and you lost two weeks."},{"text":"Quietly adjust the layout without new approval","feedback":"It came out at the final site inspection. The event may be banned."}]},{"id":"viral","title":"A video went viral","text":"A short clip of the stage build hit a million views. The other planned campaign posts are performing terribly.","lesson":"Agile marketing: measure, learn, adapt. The plan is a hypothesis; real-world data takes priority.","choices":[{"text":"Adapt the campaign: more behind-the-scenes content, fewer planned ads","feedback":"Ticket sales jumped and the campaign costs less than planned."},{"text":"Stick to the original campaign plan approved in January","feedback":"The plan is followed, but the opportunity flew by."},{"text":"Spend the entire remaining campaign budget promoting that one video","feedback":"The reach is huge, but there's no money left for the rest of the campaign."}]},{"id":"predprodej","title":"Presale crashed","text":"When ticket presale opened, the online store crashed under the load for two hours. Fans are angry.","lesson":"An incident is a chance to improve the process. Non-functional requirements (performance, security) belong in the Definition of Done.","choices":[{"text":"Blameless retrospective + load tests in the Definition of Done","feedback":"Root cause found, tests in place. The second wave of presale went smoothly."},{"text":"Replace the developer who built the store","feedback":"The team is scared and the new person doesn't know the system. The cause remains."},{"text":"Buy bigger servers and leave it at that","feedback":"It helped this time, but nobody knows where the real limit is."}]},{"id":"partner","title":"Partner wants a tent in the middle","text":"The main partner wants its big tent right in the middle of the site. But the layout is already approved by the authorities.","lesson":"Handle changes to an approved baseline through change control. Hybrid lets you look for compensation in the agile part, where changes are cheap.","choices":[{"text":"Change control: assess the impact on permits and offer the partner an alternative (visibility in the app)","feedback":"The tent stayed at the edge, but the partner has its own section in the app. Everyone's happy."},{"text":"Agree right away – the partner pays","feedback":"New layout approval and a site rebuild. An expensive favor."},{"text":"Refuse without discussion","feedback":"The layout is protected, but the partner is wondering whether to come back next year."}]},{"id":"dobrovolnici","title":"Not enough volunteers","text":"Three weeks before the festival, half of the volunteer event staff are missing.","lesson":"Quick experiments in the agile part can help solve a predictive-part problem – with a plan B just in case.","choices":[{"text":"The digital team launches a recruitment campaign; production reaches out to an agency in parallel as backup","feedback":"The campaign brought in 80% of the missing people. The agency only covers the rest."},{"text":"Wait, it'll sort itself out","feedback":"It didn't. The safety plan no longer matches reality."},{"text":"Just hire an expensive agency for everything","feedback":"Reliable, but expensive."}]}]},{"id":"fuze","stars":{"ko":[{"text":"The regulator approves the joint app"},{"text":"The app launches with all Must items"}],"top":[{"text":"A year later at least 50 %"},{"text":"No stakeholder below 40"}]},"name":"Merger of Two Companies","tagline":"A bank bought a fintech – now they must build one app together","scope":"A joint mobile app after a bank acquires a fintech: connection to the core banking system, single sign-on, customer migration, new features and regulatory approval.","intro":"A big bank bought a small fintech with a great mobile app. The board wants one joint app for customers of both companies within six months. The bank has a policy for everything, the fintech has a chat for everything. You lead the joint project – with people from both companies.","predWorld":"Connection to the core banking system, security audit, AML checks and regulatory approval. Bank policies apply here – and for good reason.","agileWorld":"The mobile app, onboarding and new customer features. That's the fintech's strength: try fast, measure and improve.","terms":{"launch":"the launch of the joint app","predShort":"core integration, security and regulatory approval","agileShort":"the mobile app and new features","usersGen":"customers","sponsor":"bank board member","committee":"joint steering committee","product":"The joint app"},"stakeholders":[{"id":"banka","name":"Bank CIO","wants":"security, policies and a plan","quit":"blocked deployment to the bank's infrastructure.","epilogBad":"put the app into the “standard process” – new versions now ship once a quarter."},{"id":"fintech","name":"Fintech founder","wants":"speed and his own product ideas","quit":"left, taking half of his team along.","epilogBad":"left to found a new startup and took the best people with him."},{"id":"klienti","name":"Customers of both companies","wants":"an app that works and takes nothing away from them","quit":"started leaving for competitors in droves.","epilogBad":"rate the app two stars and are leaving for competitors."}],"areas":{"core":{"label":"Core banking"},"security":{"label":"Security and AML"},"app":{"label":"Mobile app"},"api":{"label":"API and integration"}},"team":[{"id":"vera","name":"Věra","role":"core banking architect (bank)"},{"id":"milan","name":"Milan","role":"security and AML (bank)"},{"id":"kuba","name":"Kuba","role":"mobile developer (fintech)"},{"id":"bara","name":"Bára","role":"UX and onboarding (fintech)"},{"id":"tadeas","name":"Tadeáš","role":"backend and API (fintech)"}],"workstreams":[{"id":"jadro","name":"Connection to the core banking system","why":"The bank's core changes once a quarter under strict rules. The interface is designed, approved and built to plan."},{"id":"audit","name":"Security audit and AML","why":"Requirements come from regulation and the audit procedure is prescribed."},{"id":"regulator","name":"Regulatory approval","why":"The regulator has deadlines and a list of documents. The filing date is planned."},{"id":"aplikace","name":"Mobile app and onboarding","why":"What suits customers of both companies only shows in their behavior – you iterate."},{"id":"funkce","name":"New customer features","why":"Ideas must be tested with customers before they're built."},{"id":"design","name":"Unifying the design of both brands","why":"The design is tuned to user reactions, version by version."},{"id":"mzdy","name":"Payroll and accounting of the merged company","why":"Routine work of the finance department. After the staff transfer it's done by the line organization, not the app project."},{"id":"podpora","name":"Customer support for existing customers","why":"Support runs every day and will keep running after the project. It's operations."}],"backlog":[{"id":"login","name":"Single sign-on for customers of both companies"},{"id":"jadro","name":"Connecting the app to the core banking system"},{"id":"onboarding","name":"Moving bank customers into the app"},{"id":"platby","name":"In-app payments from bank accounts"},{"id":"aml","name":"AML checks per bank rules"},{"id":"design","name":"Unified design for both brands"},{"id":"pomocnik","name":"Budgeting assistant"},{"id":"predani","name":"Handover to bank operations: runbooks and training"},{"id":"chat","name":"Chat with a banker"},{"id":"krypto","name":"Crypto in the app (the founder's idea)"},{"id":"vykazy","name":"Monthly reports for bank headquarters"},{"id":"podpora","name":"Customer support for fintech customers"},{"id":"mzdy","name":"Moving fintech staff into the payroll system"}],"milestones":[{"id":"m1","name":"Security audit","okText":"Single sign-on passed the bank's security audit.","lateText":"There was nothing to run the security audit on."},{"id":"m2","name":"Core integration test","okText":"The app talks to the core banking system and AML checks work.","lateText":"The core integration test failed."},{"id":"m3","name":"Regulatory approval","okText":"The regulator approved the app.","lateText":"The application to the regulator went out late."},{"id":"m4","name":"Joint app launch","okText":"The joint app is out. Customers of both companies log in with the same button.","lateText":"The app shipped without key features – missing:"}],"shift":{"title":"The founders are leaving","text":"The fintech founders sold the rest of their shares to the bank and are leaving. Kuba goes with them and other fintech people are wavering – they feel the bank steamrolled them. Revealed factor: changing people's established habits.","team":{"reason":"leaves with the founders"},"lesson":"In a merger the biggest risk is people leaving with their knowledge. What helps is knowledge sharing across companies and retrospectives where people from both cultures agree on a shared way of working – not one side's rules imposed on the other."},"gate":{"id":"gate","title":"Joint steering committee","text":"The steering committee, with people from both the bank and the fintech, decides on the second half of the project. How do you prepare the materials?","lesson":"One project needs one picture of its state: milestones of the predictively managed parts and working increments of the agile parts in one overview. Two presentations mean two projects.","choices":[{"text":"A joint overview: bank milestones, a live app demo and risks in one place","feedback":"For the first time the committee sees one project, not two companies."},{"text":"Two presentations – the bank its Gantt chart, the fintech its demo","feedback":"Half the committee only listened to “their” presentation."},{"text":"Report using the bank's template","feedback":"The bank is happy. The founder stayed silent at the meeting."}]},"eventSlots":[[{"id":"hotovo","title":"What does “done” mean?","text":"For the bank a feature is done when security approves it. For the fintech, when it's in the app store. Each side claims the opposite about the “login” feature.","lesson":"Merging two cultures needs a shared vocabulary. A Definition of Done is an agreement, not one side's rules taken over.","choices":[{"text":"Write a joint Definition of Done: tested, security-reviewed and deployed","feedback":"The debate took two hours. Now everyone means the same thing."},{"text":"Let each side do it its own way","feedback":"A ceasefire. For now."},{"text":"Adopt the bank's definition","feedback":"The fintech sees it as its first defeat."}]},{"id":"smernice","title":"A policy for everything","text":"Bank policy says every new app version must go through a forty-page change request.","lesson":"Expensive changes (the bank's core) belong in formal change control; cheap ones (the app) can be decided by the Product Owner. Working around rules comes back to bite.","choices":[{"text":"Agree on two speeds: core changes via change control, app changes decided by the Product Owner","feedback":"Security got what it needs. The fintech can release every week."},{"text":"Comply – every version through the bank's change control board","feedback":"The first change request took three people two days."},{"text":"Work around the policy and release quietly","feedback":"Fast. And risky."}]}],[{"id":"vera","title":"Everything goes through Věra","text":"Only Věra understands the core banking system. Every question from the fintech ends up with her and Věra can't keep up.","lesson":"A knowledge island is doubly dangerous in a merger: the knowledge sits in one head and in one company. Pairing across companies spreads it.","choices":[{"text":"Pair Věra with Tadeáš on the core interface","feedback":"Tadeáš asks, Věra explains. After a week he answers half the questions himself."},{"text":"Věra can handle it, she's experienced","feedback":"Věra is handling it. For now."},{"text":"Bring in a consultant from the core vendor","feedback":"The consultant helped. The knowledge will leave with him."}]},{"id":"kultura","title":"Two cultures in one meeting","text":"Bank people talk about “the fintech kids”, the fintech about “the dinosaurs”. Meetings turn into tug-of-war.","lesson":"A culture clash isn't solved by separating teams, but by working together. Mixed pairs and joint retrospectives build one team.","choices":[{"text":"Mixed pairs on every feature and a joint retrospective","feedback":"The first week was bumpy. By the second, people were inviting each other to lunch."},{"text":"Split teams by company so they don't fight","feedback":"Peace. Each team does its own thing."},{"text":"Team building at a spa hotel","feedback":"It was nice. On Monday the old jokes were back."}]}],[{"id":"krypto","title":"The founder wants crypto","text":"The fintech founder wants crypto in the app. “Without it young customers won't take us seriously.”","lesson":"A powerful stakeholder's idea is a hypothesis like any other. A cheap experiment decides better than hierarchy.","choices":[{"text":"Test customer interest with a cheap experiment before building anything","feedback":"A landing page showed interest from 2 % of customers. The founder took it gracefully."},{"text":"Postpone until after launch","feedback":"The founder wrote it in his notebook. In red."},{"text":"Build it now – the founder has a vision","feedback":"The bank learned about crypto from the internal chat."}]},{"id":"regulator","title":"The regulator asks questions","text":"The regulator wants to know how the project decides on app changes and who is accountable for them.","lesson":"Agile doesn't mean undocumented decisions. In a regulated environment it must be clear who decided what – even in the backlog.","choices":[{"text":"Present the rules: change control for the core and a log of Product Owner decisions for the app","feedback":"The regulator closed its inquiry."},{"text":"Answer that the fintech decides in an agile way and documentation isn't needed","feedback":"The regulator requested a full process audit."},{"text":"Write the documentation retroactively","feedback":"Milan wrote for three evenings. It passed."}]}],[{"id":"klienti","title":"Fintech customers are worried","text":"Word is spreading on social media that after the merger fintech customers will lose their favorite features.","lesson":"Change for people needs transparency and a chance to try new things in advance. Migrating without warning destroys trust.","choices":[{"text":"Publish the migration plan and let customers try a beta","feedback":"Beta testers write more praise than complaints."},{"text":"Move everyone at once without warning","feedback":"Fast. The app rating dropped to 1.9."},{"text":"Send an FAQ email","feedback":"11 % of customers opened it."}]},{"id":"milan","title":"Milan got an offer","text":"Milan, the team's only security specialist, got an offer from a competitor.","lesson":"It's good to keep a key person – but above all, make sure their knowledge doesn't leave with them.","choices":[{"text":"Counteroffer, and Milan trains a colleague in AML","feedback":"Milan stayed and now two people understand security."},{"text":"Let him go, it'll work out somehow","team":{"reason":"leaves for a competitor"},"feedback":"Milan left on Friday. On Monday the first audit question arrived."},{"text":"Hire an external security firm","team":{"join":[{"id":"auditor","name":"External auditor","role":"external security"}]},"feedback":"The contractors are good. And expensive."}]}],[{"id":"vypadek","title":"A test crashed the bank's environment","text":"A fintech integration test took down the core banking test environment for a day. The bank is furious.","lesson":"A bug at the interface of two companies is a chance to learn together. Hunting for a culprit splits the team; banning tests pushes bugs into live operations.","choices":[{"text":"A joint blameless root-cause analysis and an updated test procedure","feedback":"Cause: a missing call limit. Procedure fixed, nobody lost face."},{"text":"Blame the fintech","feedback":"The bank calmed down. The fintech remembered whose side you're on."},{"text":"Ban tests on the bank's environment","feedback":"The environment is safe. Bugs will now be found in production."}]},{"id":"drive","title":"The board wants to launch earlier","text":"A competitor announced a similar app. The board wants to launch a month earlier.","lesson":"Schedule pressure can be met with a staged launch (an employee pilot), not by overloading the team.","choices":[{"text":"Launch early only for employees as a pilot, for customers on schedule","feedback":"Employees found 14 bugs before customers did."},{"text":"Promise an earlier launch","feedback":"The promise is out. The team learned about it from the press release."},{"text":"Refuse, pointing to the plan","feedback":"The board accepted it. Without enthusiasm."}]}],[{"id":"golive","title":"The night before launch","text":"Everything is ready. How do you release the app to customers?","lesson":"A staged rollout (a small percentage of customers first) limits the impact of bugs the tests missed.","choices":[{"text":"Gradually: 5 % of customers, watch, then more","feedback":"On day one a payments bug showed up. It hit only a few hundred customers."},{"text":"Everyone at once at midnight","feedback":"In the morning payments didn't work. For anyone."},{"text":"Postpone a week to be safe","feedback":"An extra week of testing. The founder is furious."}]}]],"followups":{"nehotovo":{"id":"nehotovo","title":"A “done” feature failed the audit","text":"A feature the fintech reported as done failed the bank's security review.","lesson":"Without a shared definition of done, hidden unfinished work piles up. Sooner or later someone finds it – worst case, a customer.","unresolvedText":"After launch it turned out some “done” features never passed the security review.","choices":[{"text":"Introduce a joint Definition of Done now and finish the feature","feedback":"Late, but better than never."},{"text":"Launch it anyway","feedback":"Bank security made a note of it."},{"text":"Turn the feature off","feedback":"Safe. Customers lost the feature."}]},"audit_nalez":{"id":"audit_nalez","title":"Internal audit found secret releases","text":"The bank's internal audit found that the fintech shipped three app versions outside the approved process.","lesson":"Working around rules solves speed only in the short term. The sustainable fix is to change the rules to match the risk of each change.","unresolvedText":"A year later the audit found unreported app versions and the bank was fined.","choices":[{"text":"Admit it and agree on rules based on change risk","feedback":"Audit closed with a recommendation. The rules are more sensible."},{"text":"Sweep it under the rug","feedback":"The auditor wasn't having it."},{"text":"Freeze releases for a month","feedback":"Safe. Customers noticed nothing is happening."}]},"rozhrani":{"id":"rozhrani","title":"Two teams, two interfaces","text":"The bank team and the fintech team each built their own version of the interface between the app and the core. They don't fit.","lesson":"Separate teams in one project create separate solutions. An interface needs a joint team and integration tests.","unresolvedText":"The interface between the app and the core breaks with every new version.","choices":[{"text":"A mixed team for the interface and joint integration tests","feedback":"One interface, one team."},{"text":"Let each team fix its own part","feedback":"Now they don't fit in a different way."},{"text":"Hire an integrator","feedback":"The integrator glued it together."}]}}},{"id":"hra","stars":{"ko":[{"text":"Version 1.0 hits its goal"}],"top":[{"text":"All three goals met"}]},"name":"Early Access Video Game","tagline":"Small studio, loud community, little money","scope":"A co-op survival game in early access: game mechanics, content, updates, community and marketing. Players already own the game and let you know every week what they like.","approachText":"Extreme uncertainty: only numbers and reviews show what players enjoy. Money drains every sprint, and only traction brings more. The whole project runs agile: short iterations, experiments, player data and a willingness to pivot.","intro":"You run a small game studio. The game is in early access, players are already playing it, and the money barely lasts a few months. Every sprint costs money – only features players truly enjoy pay off.","terms":{"launch":"the 1.0 release","agileShort":"the whole game","users":"players","usersGen":"players","poGood":"game designer with a mandate","committee":"publisher and investors"},"workstreams":[{"id":"mechaniky","name":"Game mechanics","why":"Whether the game is fun only shows when people play it. Prototype, playtest, tweak."},{"id":"obsah","name":"New maps and content","why":"Content ships with updates, and direction follows what players play most."},{"id":"balanc","name":"Game economy and balance","why":"Tuned from data on thousands of matches, not from a spreadsheet up front."},{"id":"servery","name":"Servers and stability","why":"Continuous deployment and quick fixes for whatever crashes – a smooth flow of work."},{"id":"komunita","name":"Community and Discord","why":"Talking to players means reacting to whatever is happening right now."},{"id":"lokalizace","name":"Localization into six languages","why":"Careful, it sounds like a plannable job – but texts change with every update. Translation runs continuously, in batches."},{"id":"marketing","name":"Streamer partnerships","why":"Only the numbers show what works. Short experiments and evaluation."},{"id":"zvuk","name":"Music and sound effects","why":"Sound is tuned through playtests, not by a spec."}],"backlog":[{"id":"coop","name":"4-player co-op missions"},{"id":"pady","name":"Crash fixes"},{"id":"cloud","name":"Cloud saves"},{"id":"zebricek","name":"PvP leaderboard"},{"id":"arena","name":"PvP arena"},{"id":"tutorial","name":"Tutorial for newcomers"},{"id":"skiny","name":"Paid cosmetic skins"},{"id":"crafting","name":"Item crafting"},{"id":"battlepass","name":"Battle pass"},{"id":"mody","name":"Mod support"},{"id":"gamepad","name":"Gamepad controls"},{"id":"foto","name":"Photo mode"},{"id":"ranked","name":"Ranked PvP seasons"},{"id":"kampan","name":"Story campaign"},{"id":"konzole","name":"Console version"}],"discoveries":[{"id":"hlas","name":"In-team voice chat","why":"After co-op missions, players want to talk to each other right in the game."},{"id":"workshop","name":"Community mod workshop","why":"Modders spoke up as soon as the tools came out: they want a place to share mods."}],"milestones":[{"id":"m1","name":"Positive reviews","okText":"Reviews are improving, players keep coming back.","lateText":"Reviews are mixed, players are leaving."},{"id":"m2","name":"Major update","okText":"The major update brought back old players and new ones too.","lateText":"The major update sank without a trace."},{"id":"m3","name":"Version 1.0","okText":"Version 1.0 launches to positive reviews!","lateText":"Version 1.0 is out, but players aren't excited."}],"shift":{"title":"The market flipped","text":"A big rival game focused on PvP combat came out, and the PvP players moved over. Your community now mostly wants co-op and mods – and says so loudly. Revealed factor: a loud player community.","lesson":"When the market flips, reordering the backlog isn't enough – the team has to test new assumptions fast. Hypotheses and experiments become the key practice."},"gate":{"id":"gate","title":"Publisher meeting","text":"The publisher decides whether to fund more months of development. What do you show?","lesson":"Funding decisions in an agile project rest on data: how many people play, how many come back, and what the team has learned.","choices":[{"text":"Player data, what we've learned and a playable new build","feedback":"The publisher added funding for three more months."},{"text":"A trailer and big plans for 1.0","feedback":"“And how many people play it today?” The publisher tied the money to results."},{"text":"Postpone the meeting until there's something to show","feedback":"Meanwhile, the publisher paused payments."}]},"events":[{"id":"recenze","title":"Wave of negative reviews","text":"Players are posting negative reviews over crashes. The rating is dropping.","lesson":"Stability is the foundation of value. Players forgive thin content, not a game that crashes.","choices":[{"text":"Spend a whole sprint on stability and tell the community openly","feedback":"Players appreciate the honesty. Fewer crashes."},{"text":"Ignore the crashes and ship new content","feedback":"New content shipped. The crashes stayed."},{"text":"Split the team in half","feedback":"Some fixes, some content. Nothing done properly."}]},{"id":"streamer","title":"Offer from a streamer","text":"A big streamer offers to showcase the game – in exchange for exclusive content.","lesson":"Promising dates for content that doesn't exist yet is dangerous in an agile project. Offer what you have.","choices":[{"text":"Offer early access to the new update, with no date promised","feedback":"The stream brought in hundreds of new players."},{"text":"Promise an exclusive map within two weeks","feedback":"The streamer is hyped. The team doesn't know about the map yet."},{"text":"Pay for a sponsored collab","feedback":"It works, but it's pricey."}]},{"id":"vydavatel","title":"Money for a battle pass","text":"The publisher offers extra money if you add a battle pass by the end of the month.","lesson":"When money and community trust are at stake, test the hypothesis before you commit.","choices":[{"text":"Gauge interest with a poll and a small test, then decide","feedback":"The poll was clear: the community doesn't want a battle pass. The item's value is now verified."},{"text":"Accept and add the battle pass","feedback":"The money came in. The community is frowning."},{"text":"Decline","feedback":"The publisher is disappointed, but the community is none the wiser."}]},{"id":"crunch","title":"Crunch before the update","text":"A major update is coming and the team proposes a month of crunch – working nights.","lesson":"Crunch boosts output short term and burns people out long term. A sustainable pace and smaller scope are cheaper.","choices":[{"text":"Cut the update's scope and keep a sustainable pace","feedback":"The update is smaller, but the team is OK."},{"text":"Go into crunch","feedback":"The update will be big. The team is exhausted."},{"text":"Delay the update by a week","feedback":"Players wait longer, the team can breathe."}]},{"id":"cheaty","title":"Cheaters","text":"Cheats are spreading through the game. Honest players are furious.","lesson":"A problem that ruins the experience for all players comes before new features.","choices":[{"text":"A quick anti-cheat fix and open communication with players","feedback":"Fewer cheaters, a calmer community."},{"text":"Leave it until 1.0","feedback":"Meanwhile, the cheaters are having a blast."},{"text":"Ban manually","feedback":"It helps, but the team spends hours reading reports."}]},{"id":"modder","title":"Popular mod","text":"A community modder made a mod that more people play than some official maps. They want official support.","lesson":"The community can be your best source of value. Test the interest and give it room.","choices":[{"text":"Collaborate and test interest in mod support","feedback":"Interest is huge. The value of mod support is now verified."},{"text":"Ban mods – they ruin our vision","feedback":"The modder leaves, and thousands of players with them."},{"text":"Hire them onto the team","feedback":"One more skilled person, but the community got no more openness out of it."}]}],"followups":{"lavina":{"id":"lavina","title":"“Mostly Negative” rating","text":"The game's rating dropped to “Mostly Negative”. Sales are tanking.","lesson":"Ignored quality comes back the moment everyone can see it. Fixing it now costs more than two sprints ago.","unresolvedText":"Bad reviews over crashes followed the game into version 1.0.","choices":[{"text":"A fix sprint, an apology and a gift for players","feedback":"Players accepted the apology. The rating is slowly recovering."},{"text":"Delete critical posts on Discord","feedback":"Screenshots of the deleted posts went viral."},{"text":"Run a sale","feedback":"New players came – and wrote more negative reviews."}]},"mapa":{"id":"mapa","title":"Where's the promised map?","text":"The streamer asks live where the promised exclusive map is. The team didn't make it in time.","lesson":"A deadline promised without the team is a debt the team pays off. Honesty is cheaper than a half-finished job.","unresolvedText":"The streamer kept griping about the broken promise for ages.","choices":[{"text":"Admit the slip and show the work-in-progress map live","feedback":"Viewers loved the behind-the-scenes look."},{"text":"Release the unfinished map","feedback":"The map is full of bugs and the streamer laughs at them the whole time."},{"text":"Weekend overtime","feedback":"The map is done. So is the team."}]},"bojkot":{"id":"bojkot","title":"Community boycotts the battle pass","text":"The community is boycotting the battle pass and review-bombing the game.","lesson":"An untested hypothesis gets paid for in lost trust. Trust comes back slower than money.","unresolvedText":"Players still remember the battle pass fiasco.","choices":[{"text":"Scrap the battle pass and refund players","feedback":"Painful, but the community appreciated it."},{"text":"Stick with it","feedback":"Reviews keep falling."},{"text":"Make it free","feedback":"The storm died down; the publisher's money is gone."}]},"odchody":{"id":"odchody","title":"Devs quit after the crunch","text":"Two experienced developers handed in their notice after the crunch.","lesson":"Crunch takes its toll with a delay. Losing people costs more than an update a week late.","unresolvedText":"More people left after release; the studio is weakened.","choices":[{"text":"Redistribute work, shrink the plan and hire juniors with mentoring","feedback":"A slower start, but the team stabilizes."},{"text":"More crunch so we make it","feedback":"More resignations on the desk."},{"text":"Freeze new features","feedback":"Players get nothing new."}]},"exodus":{"id":"exodus","title":"Honest players are leaving","text":"There are so many cheaters that honest players are leaving for the competition en masse.","lesson":"A problem that ruins the experience won't wait for 1.0.","unresolvedText":"The “game full of cheaters” reputation followed it into version 1.0.","choices":[{"text":"Anti-cheat right now, plus amnesty for players who come back","feedback":"Some players came back."},{"text":"Claim the problem is overblown","feedback":"The community sees it differently."},{"text":"Shut down the PvP servers","feedback":"Cheaters have nowhere to play. Neither do honest players."}]},"mody_bonus":{"id":"mody_bonus","title":"Mods bring in players","text":"Community mods are bringing in new players. Modders ask whether there could be a contest.","lesson":"Openness to the community is an investment that pays back – players create value themselves.","unresolvedText":"The modding community keeps the game alive even after version 1.0.","choices":[{"text":"Run a best-mod contest with a prize","feedback":"The contest brought dozens of mods and a wave of new players."},{"text":"Sell the best mods as paid content","feedback":"Modders feel robbed."},{"text":"Say thanks and leave it there","feedback":"A somewhat missed opportunity."}]}}},{"id":"knihovna","stars":{"ko":[{"text":"The library opens with all Must features"}],"top":[{"text":"All milestones met"}]},"name":"Library Project","tagline":"Building renovation + mobile app","scope":"Building renovation, new self-service kiosks, cabling, a mobile app and an online catalog for readers.","intro":"You've just taken over the project to modernize the city library. The grand opening is in 12 weeks.","predWorld":"Building renovation, kiosk procurement, cabling. Fixed contracts, deadlines and permits. The Gantt chart rules.","agileWorld":"Mobile app and online catalog. Requirements evolve, the team works in sprints and gathers feedback.","terms":{"launch":"the library opening","predShort":"construction, kiosks, cabling","agileShort":"app and catalog","users":"readers","usersGen":"readers","sponsor":"library director","poGood":"head of the lending department","committee":"city representatives"},"dependency":{"lock":"Waiting for kiosk delivery (predictive milestone)","hint":"<b>Kiosk–catalog integration</b> is waiting for a predictive milestone: kiosk delivery."},"workstreams":[{"id":"stavba","name":"Library building renovation","why":"The construction has a building permit, a fixed budget and strict sequencing (structure first, then plaster). Changes midway are extremely expensive, so it's planned up front."},{"id":"kiosky","name":"Self-service kiosk procurement","why":"Public tender: specification, bidding, contract and delivery time. The requirements are clear and the process is set by law."},{"id":"sit","name":"Cabling and network infrastructure","why":"Cables go into the walls at a precise phase of construction. It depends on the construction schedule and can't change later."},{"id":"gdpr","name":"GDPR compliance and security audit","why":"Regulatory requirements are set by law and need formal documentation and approval by a fixed date."},{"id":"appka","name":"Mobile app for readers","why":"Nobody knows in advance exactly what readers will value. Short iterations and feedback from real users lead to a better product."},{"id":"katalog","name":"Online catalog and reservations","why":"Software can be delivered in slices and improved continuously. Features are prioritized by value to readers."},{"id":"ux","name":"Kiosk interface design","why":"Design is best tuned through prototypes and testing with real visitors – and that's iterative work."},{"id":"ai","name":"Experiment: AI book recommendations","why":"High uncertainty: we don't know if it will work. Short-cycle experiments let us learn fast (or stop in time)."}],"backlog":[{"id":"login","name":"Reader sign-in"},{"id":"search","name":"Catalog search"},{"id":"reserve","name":"Book reservation"},{"id":"renew","name":"Loan renewal"},{"id":"kiosk","name":"Kiosk–catalog integration"},{"id":"notify","name":"Due date reminders"},{"id":"history","name":"Loan history"},{"id":"pay","name":"Online fee payment"},{"id":"a11y","name":"Accessibility (WCAG)"},{"id":"qr","name":"Library card on your phone (QR)"},{"id":"events","name":"Library events calendar"},{"id":"rating","name":"Book ratings"},{"id":"dark","name":"Dark mode"},{"id":"recommend","name":"AI book recommendations"},{"id":"challenge","name":"Reading challenge (gamification)"},{"id":"ebooks","name":"Third-party e-book lending"}],"milestones":[{"id":"m1","name":"Kiosk contract","okText":"The tender finished on time and the contract is signed. The kiosks arrive in sprint 3 and the team can start integrating.","lateText":"The tender dragged on. The kiosks won't arrive until sprint 4 – the agile team has to replan."},{"id":"m2","name":"Building handover","okText":"The building is handed over on schedule. The library can start moving in.","lateText":"Construction ran late. Contract penalties and an unhappy committee."},{"id":"m3","name":"Grand opening","okText":"The library opens and every “Must” feature works. Readers reserve books from their phones and the kiosks!","lateText":"The opening happened, but key features are missing:"}],"events":[{"id":"kavarna","title":"The director wants a café","text":"Midway through the renovation the director has an idea: “There should be a café on the ground floor!” The construction project doesn't account for it at all.","lesson":"In the predictive part, changes go through formal change control: assess the impact on time, cost and risk, then decide.","choices":[{"text":"Order the builders to do it now – the director's the boss","feedback":"The director is delighted, but extra work, a new permit and rerouted utilities cost time and money."},{"text":"Start change control: impact analysis and a steering committee decision","feedback":"After the analysis, the committee decided the café will come in stage two. The director understands – they saw the numbers."},{"text":"Reject it outright – scope is frozen","feedback":"The plan is protected, but the director feels ignored. You can't reject changes without assessing them."}]},{"id":"demo","title":"Librarians want a change after the demo","text":"At the sprint review, librarians realize reservations should also support “reserve for a whole class” – for teachers. Nobody saw that coming.","lesson":"In the agile part, change is welcome. The new requirement goes into the backlog and the Product Owner prioritizes it against everything else.","choices":[{"text":"Add it to the backlog; the Product Owner orders it by value","feedback":"The librarians see the team is listening. Findings like this are exactly why we hold reviews."},{"text":"Reject it – the requirements were clear","feedback":"We chose agile precisely so we could react to findings like this. And we just threw that away."},{"text":"Stop the sprint and rework it right away","feedback":"Work in progress went to waste and the team is frustrated. A sensible change can wait for the next planning."}]},{"id":"dodavatel","title":"The kiosks are delayed","text":"The kiosk supplier reports a 3-week production delay. The agile team had planned the kiosk integration.","lesson":"Dependencies between the predictive and agile parts belong in the risk register. The agile team can work around a delay (simulator, backlog replanning).","choices":[{"text":"Draw on the schedule buffer; meanwhile the team develops against a kiosk simulator","feedback":"The delay was absorbed. The simulator even caught two bugs before the kiosks arrived."},{"text":"Threaten the supplier with penalties and change nothing","feedback":"Penalties recover some money, but the kiosks still arrive late and the team waits."},{"text":"Cancel the kiosks – the app is enough","feedback":"The kiosks were a key requirement of the city. The steering committee is unpleasantly surprised."}]},{"id":"retro","title":"The retrospective found a gap","text":"At the retrospective it turns out the developers don't know when the building network will be ready – so they can't test the kiosks on site.","lesson":"The interface between the predictive and agile parts needs a shared dependency plan and regular communication.","choices":[{"text":"Set up a shared dependency map and a weekly sync with the site manager","feedback":"Both teams now see when they're waiting on each other. On-site testing is scheduled."},{"text":"Let the developers figure it out themselves","feedback":"Information gets lost and integration keeps slipping."},{"text":"Builders will attend every daily scrum","feedback":"Information flows, but it slows the builders down and the daily drags on."}]},{"id":"skrt","title":"Budget cut","text":"The city announces: the project budget is cut by 10%. You have to save somewhere.","lesson":"The iron triangle (time–cost–scope): in a hybrid project, the usual sacrifice is the agile part's scope (Could features), not quality or safety.","choices":[{"text":"Drop the app's “Could” features and defer them to the next stage","feedback":"Savings with no impact on key features. MoSCoW paid off."},{"text":"Save on testing","feedback":"Money saved today, you'll pay back many times over in post-launch bugs."},{"text":"Cut construction costs with cheaper materials","feedback":"Changing materials requires a new assessment and reworked design documentation."}]},{"id":"gdpr","title":"GDPR audit","text":"The data protection officer wants proof of how the app processes reader data. It can't launch without approval.","lesson":"Compliance requirements in the agile part are best handled by adding them to the Definition of Done – then every feature is “done” including documentation.","choices":[{"text":"Add GDPR requirements to the Definition of Done","feedback":"Every new feature is now compliant from the start. The audit goes smoothly."},{"text":"We'll deal with it at the end of the project","feedback":"Retroactive documentation and last-minute fixes are expensive and risky."},{"text":"Halt development for a whole sprint and document everything","feedback":"The audit is passed, but at the cost of a lost sprint."}]},{"id":"odchod","title":"Key developer is leaving","text":"The only developer who understands the integration with the old library system has resigned. She has a month left.","lesson":"A low “bus factor” is a risk. Knowledge sharing (pair programming, documentation) reduces dependence on individuals.","choices":[{"text":"Pair programming and knowledge transfer + start hiring","feedback":"Next sprint is slower, but the knowledge no longer walks out the door with one person."},{"text":"Change nothing, it'll work out somehow","feedback":"After she leaves, nobody knows how the integration works. Bugs pile up."},{"text":"Offer her a raise to stay","feedback":"She stayed, but the risk remains – she may leave again next time."}]},{"id":"azbest","title":"Builders found asbestos","text":"Asbestos was found while tearing down a partition wall. Removal will take time and money. This risk was in the risk register.","lesson":"Identified risks should have a prepared response and a reserve. Well-separated project parts let the agile team keep going even when construction hits trouble.","choices":[{"text":"Activate the risk reserve and adjust the construction schedule; development continues","feedback":"The risk response plan worked. The committee appreciates that the project was prepared."},{"text":"Stop the whole project, development included, until it's resolved","feedback":"App development has nothing to do with asbestos. Time wasted for nothing."},{"text":"Keep quiet and carry on","feedback":"Health inspectors shut the site down and the story hit the news. A major loss of trust."},{"text":"Negotiate emergency money with the sponsor and replan","feedback":"With no reserve ready, you have to find money and get a new plan approved. It costs time and trust."}]}]},{"id":"most","stars":{"ko":[{"text":"Track closures don't overrun the buffer – trains must run on time again"}],"top":[{"text":"Budget at least 30 at the end"}]},"name":"Railway Bridge Replacement","tagline":"A new structure built during weekend track closures","scope":"Dismantling the old bridge and erecting a new steel structure during four track closures, when no trains run. Between closures, traffic runs and no work is allowed on the bridge.","approachText":"Fixed closure windows, prescribed construction methods, rail authority oversight and a huge cost for every delay. Run purely predictively: a plan by closure, a detailed Gantt chart with a critical path, scheduling of specialists, change control and risk management.","intro":"You're managing a railway bridge replacement on a main line. You get just four track closures – whatever isn't done in one has to wait for the next. And in between, trains run.","terms":{"launch":"the bridge reopening","predShort":"the whole project","usersGen":"rail operators","sponsor":"construction director","poGood":"line operations manager","committee":"railway administration"},"workstreams":[{"id":"vyluky","name":"Closure plan and coordination with rail operators","why":"Closures are negotiated months ahead and their dates are fixed."},{"id":"demontaz","name":"Dismantling the old structure","why":"The method is set by the design and the structural engineer, step by step."},{"id":"montaz","name":"Fabricating and erecting the new structure","why":"The structure is fabricated to drawings in a steel shop and erected per an approved method."},{"id":"svary","name":"Welding and weld inspection","why":"Welding procedures and inspections are prescribed by standards and inspector sign-off."},{"id":"koleje","name":"Track and overhead lines","why":"Follows the finished structure and must be done by the end of the last closure."},{"id":"informovani","name":"Informing passengers about closures","why":"Careful: communication sounds flexible, but closure dates are fixed and notices go out within prescribed lead times."},{"id":"zabezpeceni","name":"Signaling software update","why":"Careful, software: but it's a safety system approved by the rail authority. It's deployed once, verified and approved."},{"id":"zkouska","name":"Load test and handover","why":"The test has a standard procedure, a booked test lab date and a formal report."}],"phases":[{"id":"p1","name":"Closure 1: Dismantling","goal":"Cut power to the line, remove the track and lift out the old bridge span.","milestone":{"name":"Old bridge gone"},"tasks":[{"id":"A","name":"Overhead line power-off","note":"No work on the bridge until the power is off."},{"id":"B","name":"Removing track on the bridge","note":"Work happens right under the overhead line."},{"id":"C","name":"Cutting up the old structure","note":"Cutting a structure that still has track on it? Not allowed."},{"id":"D","name":"Lifting out spans by crane","note":"The crane lifts the cut-up pieces."},{"id":"E","name":"Preparing bearings on the piers","note":"Work on the piers below the bridge can start as soon as the closure begins."},{"id":"F","name":"Hauling away scrap","note":"Hauls away what the crane removed."}]},{"id":"p2","name":"Closure 2: Substructure","goal":"Repair the piers, set new bearings and prepare drainage.","milestone":{"name":"Piers ready"},"tasks":[{"id":"A","name":"Repairing bearing seats","note":"Concrete seats the bearings will rest on."},{"id":"B","name":"Setting new bearings","note":"Bearings go on the repaired seats."},{"id":"C","name":"Welding anchor elements","note":"Anchors the set bearings."},{"id":"D","name":"Pier drainage","note":"Independent work at the foot of the piers."},{"id":"E","name":"Survey measurement","note":"Surveys the anchored bearings."}]},{"id":"p3","name":"Closure 3: Erecting the structure","goal":"Slide in the new spans, weld the joints and get them signed off by the inspector.","milestone":{"name":"Structure standing"},"tasks":[{"id":"A","name":"Sliding in new span 1","note":"There's only one big crane on site."},{"id":"B","name":"Sliding in new span 2","note":"Same crane as for span 1."},{"id":"C","name":"Welding the span 1 joint","note":"Welds the placed span 1."},{"id":"D","name":"Welding the span 2 joint","note":"Welds the placed span 2."},{"id":"E","name":"Inspector weld sign-off","note":"The inspector checks all welds and arrives on day eight of the closure at the earliest."},{"id":"F","name":"Installing railings and inspection walkways","note":"Installed on both placed spans."}]},{"id":"p4","name":"Closure 4: Track and testing","goal":"Lay the track, restore the overhead line, run the load test and hand over the bridge.","milestone":{"name":"Bridge in service"},"tasks":[{"id":"A","name":"Track laying","note":"Track goes on the finished structure."},{"id":"B","name":"Rail welding","note":"Welds the laid rails."},{"id":"C","name":"Overhead line installation","note":"Overhead line above the bridge, independent of the track."},{"id":"D","name":"Load test","note":"Tests the finished track and overhead line. The test lab arrives on day five of the closure."},{"id":"E","name":"Rail authority acceptance","note":"The bridge is accepted after a successful test."}]}],"shift":{"title":"Rail authority tightens oversight","text":"After an accident on another site, the rail authority ordered: every weld in the load-bearing structure must be signed off by an inspector, and the bridge needs full quality documentation. Revealed factor: regulation and audits.","lesson":"When regulation increases, practices must cover it: a strict Definition of Done with quality documentation for every weld. Otherwise the inspector sends work back and closures drag on."},"gate":{"id":"gate","title":"Checkpoint review after two closures","text":"The railway administration assesses whether the project can make it through the remaining closures. How do you prepare?","lesson":"A checkpoint in a predictive project is about exact status against the plan: what got done in the closures, what was moved, and the risks for the next closures.","choices":[{"text":"Status vs. the closure plan, moved work, risks and a site visit","feedback":"The railway administration sees the exact status and approved extra crew for the next closure."},{"text":"A presentation saying everything is on plan","feedback":"The inspector asked about the moved work. The presentation said nothing about it."},{"text":"Cancel the checkpoint review to prepare the next closure","feedback":"The railway administration sent its own inspector."}]},"events":[{"id":"koroze","title":"Corroded pier","text":"Once exposed, the pier turned out to be more corroded than the survey said.","lesson":"In a predictive project, an unexpected finding goes through change control – even if it hurts. Quick fixes come back to bite.","choices":[{"text":"Change control: plan the pier repair, even at the cost of a tighter closure","feedback":"The repair is planned. The closure will be tight, but the bridge will last a hundred years."},{"text":"Just paint the pier and carry on","feedback":"The paint looks good. For now."},{"text":"Stop and wait for a new assessment","feedback":"The assessment arrived, but the closure lost three days."}]},{"id":"jerab","title":"Which crane for erection?","text":"The crane for erecting the structure must be ordered now. A big one is pricey; a smaller one is cheaper but at the limit of its capacity.","lesson":"For critical resources, spare capacity pays off. Skimping on them risks the whole closure.","choices":[{"text":"Order the big crane with spare capacity","feedback":"Expensive, but erection is a safe bet."},{"text":"Order the smaller crane","feedback":"Savings. The crane is at its limit."},{"text":"Decide right before the closure","feedback":"The decision can wait. The cranes can't."}]},{"id":"svarec","title":"Welders out sick","text":"Two certified welders fell ill right before the closure.","lesson":"Backup capacity for critical trades belongs in the risk register. Overloading the rest leads to defects.","choices":[{"text":"Call in the backup crew from the risk register","feedback":"The backup crew was vetted and arrived on time."},{"text":"Reshuffle work: weld only critical joints","feedback":"Critical joints done, the rest will wait."},{"text":"Weld with one welder on overtime","feedback":"The welder is working sixteen-hour days."}]},{"id":"dopravce","title":"Rail operator wants a shorter closure","text":"A rail operator wants the closure cut by a day for a special train.","lesson":"A conflict over a fixed window is solved by negotiating with data and compensation. Refusing without talks comes back.","choices":[{"text":"Negotiate a detour for the special train and offer compensation","feedback":"The train takes a detour; the closure stays intact."},{"text":"Agree and shorten the closure","feedback":"The operator is happy; the closure plan is a day shorter."},{"text":"Refuse without discussion","feedback":"The operator left angry."}]},{"id":"dest","title":"Rain during the closure","text":"Heavy rain is forecast for the closure. Structural welds can't be done in the rain.","lesson":"Weather is a known risk of outdoor work. A response plan (cover, reshuffled work) turns it into routine.","choices":[{"text":"Put up a tent over the welding area from the contingency reserve","feedback":"Under the tent, welding goes on even in the rain."},{"text":"Reshuffle work: do other tasks in the rain","feedback":"Some work moved; the closure is tight."},{"text":"Weld in the rain anyway","feedback":"The welds are done. The ultrasound test is still to come."}]},{"id":"ministr","title":"Minister wants an earlier opening","text":"The construction director wants to invite the minister to the grand opening – a week earlier than the plan allows.","lesson":"Dates promised publicly must come from the plan. A political promise without a plan comes back at the worst moment.","choices":[{"text":"Show the closure plan and set the ceremony for the real date","feedback":"The director isn't thrilled, but the date is realistic."},{"text":"Promise the earlier date","feedback":"The director is thrilled. Invitations go out."},{"text":"Refuse without explanation","feedback":"The director is offended."}]}],"followups":{"koroze_navrat":{"id":"koroze_navrat","title":"Inspector finds corrosion","text":"During a check, the rail authority inspector found unrepaired pier corrosion under fresh paint.","lesson":"A hidden problem costs more than an admitted one. And lost trust gets added to the repair bill.","unresolvedText":"The pier corrosion showed up at the first inspection after reopening.","choices":[{"text":"Admit the mistake and repair it immediately","feedback":"Painful but honest. The inspector approved continuing."},{"text":"Claim the pier was fine","feedback":"The inspector halted work and ordered a structural assessment."},{"text":"Negotiate a temporary train speed limit","feedback":"The bridge opens, but trains will crawl across it."}]},"jerab_volno":{"id":"jerab_volno","title":"Big crane has capacity to spare","text":"The big crane handles erection with room to spare. A neighboring site asks to borrow it for a day.","lesson":"Investing in a critical resource pays back: in certainty, and sometimes in money.","unresolvedText":"The big crane proved itself on later projects too.","choices":[{"text":"Rent it out for a fee on days we don't need it","feedback":"Part of the crane's cost came back."},{"text":"Lend it even on a day we need it","feedback":"The money came in, but erection stalled."},{"text":"Refuse","feedback":"No risk, no bonus."}]},"vitr":{"id":"vitr","title":"Small crane can't handle the wind","text":"A crosswind picks up while a span is being slid in. The small crane is at its limit and the operator refuses to lift.","lesson":"Skimping on a critical resource costs you exactly when time is shortest.","unresolvedText":"Wind pushed erection past the end of the closure.","choices":[{"text":"Wait for calm and reshuffle the work around it","feedback":"Safe, but the closure is now very tight."},{"text":"Risk the lift","feedback":"The span swung and damaged a pier. Nobody was hurt – this time."},{"text":"Rush in a big crane","feedback":"The big crane arrived the next day. At double the price."}]},"jerab_pozde":{"id":"jerab_pozde","title":"Cranes are all booked","text":"No big cranes are available for the closure. The postponed decision backfired.","lesson":"Long-lead resource decisions can't be put off. Not deciding is also a decision.","unresolvedText":"Erection without a suitable crane dragged on.","choices":[{"text":"Rent two smaller cranes and adjust the erection method","feedback":"Trickier erection, but it works."},{"text":"Pay double for a crane from abroad","feedback":"The crane arrived. The budget weeps."},{"text":"Postpone erection to the next closure","feedback":"The whole closure is practically lost."}]},"vady":{"id":"vady","title":"Ultrasound finds weld defects","text":"Ultrasonic testing revealed defects in welds from the last closure.","lesson":"Quality can't be made up with overtime or by defying the weather. Weld defects get fixed before the inspector signs off.","unresolvedText":"Defective welds showed up at the bridge's first inspection.","choices":[{"text":"Grind out and re-weld right away","feedback":"The welds are fine now. The closure is two days shorter."},{"text":"Hide the defect under paint","feedback":"The inspector noticed. An extraordinary inspection of the whole site follows."},{"text":"Request an extra closure for repairs","feedback":"Rail operators are furious, but the welds get fixed properly."}]},"dopravce_odveta":{"id":"dopravce_odveta","title":"Rail operator demands an audit","text":"At a public hearing, the rail operator criticizes the project and demands an independent schedule audit.","lesson":"A stakeholder nobody negotiated with finds a way – through the public and the bosses.","unresolvedText":"The dispute with the rail operator dragged on after reopening.","choices":[{"text":"Openly show the closure plan and offer regular updates","feedback":"The operator calmed down. The relationship is slowly mending."},{"text":"Ignore it","feedback":"The criticism made it into the media."},{"text":"Let the audit happen","feedback":"The audit confirmed the plan, but cost time and money."}]},"ministr_prijel":{"id":"ministr_prijel","title":"Minister arrives, bridge isn't done","text":"The minister showed up for the promised opening. The bridge isn't finished.","lesson":"A promise without a plan comes back in public. Owning up and offering an alternative program beats cutting tests short.","unresolvedText":"Photos of the minister on an unfinished site went all over the media.","choices":[{"text":"Hold a site tour instead of the opening and explain the plan","feedback":"The minister liked the tour more than ribbons and scissors."},{"text":"Cut the tests short to open in time","feedback":"The bridge is open without a proper test. The rail authority is furious."},{"text":"Cancel the event at the last minute","feedback":"The minister found out from the papers."}]}}},{"id":"nemocnice","stars":{"ko":[{"text":"The ED opens with all Must items"},{"text":"The building passes occupancy approval"}],"top":[{"text":"All milestones met"}]},"name":"Hospital Emergency Department","tagline":"An extension built during full operation, plus triage software","scope":"Building a new emergency department extension while the hospital runs at full capacity, plus medical equipment and patient triage software connected to the hospital information system.","intro":"You're running construction of a new emergency department. Meanwhile the hospital runs at full tilt – doctors have no time, patients mustn't suffer, and the region watches every penny.","predWorld":"Construction during operation, medical equipment from public tenders, occupancy approval and hygiene standards.","agileWorld":"Patient triage software and a dispatch screen, tuned with doctors and nurses on simulated shifts.","terms":{"launch":"the ED opening","predShort":"construction, equipment, occupancy approval","agileShort":"patient triage software","users":"doctors and nurses","usersGen":"doctors and nurses","sponsor":"hospital director","poGood":"ED head nurse","committee":"hospital management and the region"},"dependency":{"lock":"Waiting for the network and equipment in the extension to go live (milestone)","hint":"<b>Pilot operation in the new premises</b> waits for a predictive milestone – the network and equipment going live."},"workstreams":[{"id":"pristavba","name":"Extension built during hospital operation","why":"Building permit, stages set around hospital operations, and fixed dependencies."},{"id":"technika","name":"Medical equipment via public tender","why":"Procurement law prescribes the procedure and deadlines; the specification must be done up front."},{"id":"kolaudace","name":"Occupancy approval and hygiene standards","why":"Requirements are set by regulations and checked formally."},{"id":"rozhrani","name":"Interface to the hospital information system","why":"Careful, even though it's software: the interface is defined by a standard and a contract with the system vendor, and it's tested formally."},{"id":"trideni","name":"Patient triage software","why":"How triage should work in real operation only shows up on simulated shifts with doctors and nurses."},{"id":"dispecink","name":"ED dispatch screen","why":"What the screen needs is tuned with staff bit by bit."},{"id":"skoleni","name":"Staff training on new procedures","why":"Training is tuned in simulations based on where staff make mistakes – iteratively."},{"id":"pacienti","name":"Wait time info for patients","why":"A small service you can launch early and improve based on reactions."}],"backlog":[{"id":"formular","name":"Triage form"},{"id":"fronta","name":"Patient queue by urgency"},{"id":"napojeni","name":"Hospital system integration"},{"id":"dispecink","name":"Dispatch screen"},{"id":"pilot","name":"Pilot operation in the new premises"},{"id":"zhorseni","name":"Deterioration alerts"},{"id":"statistiky","name":"Wait time statistics"},{"id":"web","name":"Wait times on the website"},{"id":"diktovani","name":"Voice dictation"},{"id":"zachranka","name":"Mobile version for ambulances"},{"id":"tmavy","name":"Screen night mode"},{"id":"ai","name":"AI diagnosis suggestions"}],"milestones":[{"id":"m1","name":"Network and equipment","okText":"The network and equipment in the extension are up. Pilot operation can be prepared from sprint 3.","lateText":"Construction slipped. Pilot operation can't be prepared until sprint 4."},{"id":"m2","name":"Occupancy approval","okText":"The extension has passed occupancy approval.","lateText":"Occupancy approval is postponed. The region is unhappy."},{"id":"m3","name":"ED opening","okText":"The new emergency department is open and the software is triaging its first patients.","lateText":"The ED opened, but without key features:"}],"shift":{"title":"Software is a medical device","text":"The State Institute for Drug Control has ruled: software that ranks patients by urgency is a medical device. It can't be used without technical documentation, risk analysis and change control. Revealed factor: regulation and audits.","addItems":[{"id":"dokumentace","name":"Technical documentation and risk analysis"},{"id":"validace","name":"Clinical validation with staff"}],"lesson":"When part of the agile work becomes a regulated product, formal elements must enter the agile part: a strict Definition of Done with documentation, and change control. Still agile, but with rules."},"gate":{"id":"gate","title":"Regional review","text":"The region, as the hospital's founder, checks whether the project is on plan and on budget. What do you present?","lesson":"A public founder needs transparency: the state of construction and budget, plus proof that the software really works in operation.","choices":[{"text":"Construction and budget status + video of a simulated shift with the software","feedback":"The region sees where the money goes and that the software helps doctors."},{"text":"Only construction figures; the software once it's done","feedback":"The region asks why it's paying for software nobody has seen."},{"text":"Postpone the review – too busy","feedback":"The region sends its own inspector."}]},"events":[{"id":"hluk","title":"Construction disturbs patients","text":"Construction noise is disturbing ICU patients. The head physician demands an immediate stop.","lesson":"Building during operation means planning work around operations – and talking to people before they complain upstairs.","choices":[{"text":"Noisy work only outside surgeries and quiet hours; offer patients other rooms","feedback":"The head physician agrees. Construction is slower, but conflict-free."},{"text":"Continue as planned","feedback":"Construction rolls on. So do the complaints."},{"text":"Stop noisy work for two weeks","feedback":"Peace in the ICU, but construction slips."}]},{"id":"lekari","title":"Doctors have no time to test","text":"Doctors and nurses are fully booked on shifts. There's no time left to test software.","lesson":"Without real users, agile development loses its point. Their time must be negotiated and paid for.","choices":[{"text":"Negotiate paid hours for simulated shifts with management","feedback":"Staff test on simulated shifts. It's expensive, but you see real use."},{"text":"Test without them, just in IT","feedback":"Tests pass. On paper."},{"text":"Test with one willing doctor","feedback":"Better than nothing, but one view isn't enough."}]},{"id":"nis","title":"System vendor stalls the interface","text":"The hospital system vendor wants double for the interface and won't deliver it for eight weeks.","lesson":"Dependency on an external system is handled by contract and technically (a simulator). Bending the rules with medical data is a gamble.","choices":[{"text":"Lock the interface by contract per the standard; develop against a simulator meanwhile","feedback":"The interface is pricey but certain. Development doesn't stop."},{"text":"Bypass the interface with direct database access","feedback":"Works right away, for free. For now."},{"text":"Wait eight weeks","feedback":"Safe, but slow."}]},{"id":"epidemie","title":"Flu epidemic","text":"The hospital is overcrowded and wants to use the finished part of the extension as a temporary ward.","lesson":"A crisis request goes through change control: what can be safely handed over now and what gets replanned.","choices":[{"text":"Hand over the finished part temporarily per the crisis plan; replan the rest","feedback":"The hospital handled the surge and construction continues in a new order."},{"text":"Refuse – construction has its plan","feedback":"Hospital management is furious. Patients lie in the corridors."},{"text":"Hand over the whole unfinished extension","feedback":"Help arrived instantly. Builders now work among patients."}]},{"id":"tendr","title":"Tender challenged","text":"A losing bidder challenged the medical equipment tender at the competition authority.","lesson":"Public procurement risks belong in the risk register with a ready plan B. Ignoring the authority doesn't pay.","choices":[{"text":"Activate plan B from the risk register: rent equipment temporarily","feedback":"Rented equipment bridges the wait for the authority's ruling."},{"text":"Wait for the authority's ruling","feedback":"The authority will rule in two months."},{"text":"Sign the contract anyway","feedback":"The equipment is ordered. The authority hasn't ruled yet."}]},{"id":"tablety","title":"Nurses want bedside tablets","text":"Nurses want the software to work on bedside tablets too. It wasn't in the brief.","lesson":"A new user request goes into the backlog and the Product Owner orders it. Building it on the side, off-plan, breaks the sprint.","choices":[{"text":"Into the backlog; the head nurse orders it and tests it on one shift","feedback":"One shift showed a simplified view is enough. Small effort, big payoff."},{"text":"Build it now, off-plan","feedback":"The sprint fell apart and the tablet version is half-baked."},{"text":"Refuse – it's not in the brief","feedback":"Nurses feel nobody listens to them."}]}],"followups":{"stiznost":{"id":"stiznost","title":"Complaint to the region","text":"Patients and the head physician complain to the regional authority. The region has announced a construction inspection.","lesson":"An ignored stakeholder conflict comes back through their bosses – and worse.","unresolvedText":"Complaints about the construction hurt the hospital's reputation.","choices":[{"text":"Admit the mistake, adjust the noisy-work schedule and inform patients","feedback":"The inspection went calmly. Relations are slowly mending."},{"text":"Argue that construction complies with the permit","feedback":"Formally true, but the region won't forget."},{"text":"Stop noisy work entirely","feedback":"Quiet, but a big slip."}]},"odmitnuti":{"id":"odmitnuti","title":"Nurses reject the software","text":"During the pilot, nurses refuse to use the software: it doesn't fit real operations and slows them down.","lesson":"Software tested without real users fails in operation. Feedback is cheaper early on.","unresolvedText":"Staff work around the software and keep paper lists.","choices":[{"text":"Stop the pilot, run simulated shifts with nurses and rework key screens","feedback":"After two iterations, nurses say: “Now this works.”"},{"text":"Order them to use it","feedback":"Nurses fill in the software for show; the real queue is on paper."},{"text":"Keep the pilot running and collect feedback","feedback":"There are a hundred comments. Some contradict each other."}]},"simulace_bonus":{"id":"simulace_bonus","title":"Nurses want more","text":"Simulated shifts paid off. Nurses come up with ideas on their own and want the software launched sooner.","lesson":"User involvement is an investment: people who co-create a solution then champion it themselves.","unresolvedText":"Staff recommend the software to other departments on their own.","choices":[{"text":"Make the most active nurses ambassadors for other shifts","feedback":"Training the other shifts almost runs itself."},{"text":"Launch the whole software now, unfinished","feedback":"The enthusiasm faded fast."},{"text":"Say thanks and continue as planned","feedback":"A somewhat missed opportunity."}]},"unik":{"id":"unik","title":"Unauthorized access to patient data","text":"A security audit found direct access to the patient database outside the approved interface.","lesson":"Bending the rules on sensitive data is a project's most expensive “saving”. Incidents get reported and handled openly.","unresolvedText":"Unauthorized access to patient data came to light only after the opening.","choices":[{"text":"Block the access immediately, report the incident and build the interface properly","feedback":"Painful but honest. The authority appreciated the quick response."},{"text":"Keep quiet and remove the access on the sly","feedback":"The audit logged it anyway. Now it's a cover-up too."},{"text":"Block it and wait for the official interface","feedback":"Safe, but the software now has no data for weeks."}]},"dodelavky":{"id":"dodelavky","title":"Finishing work among patients","text":"Finishing work in the temporarily used extension clashes with operations: hygiene inspectors threaten a fine.","lesson":"Handing over unfinished work without a punch-list plan means the problems move into operations.","unresolvedText":"Unfinished work in the extension dragged on for months after the opening.","choices":[{"text":"Draw up a punch-list plan with operations and work section by section","feedback":"Slower, but no clash with the hygiene inspectors."},{"text":"Finish it fast over a weekend","feedback":"Sloppy work and exhausted tradespeople."},{"text":"Pay the fine and carry on","feedback":"The problem remains, just pricier."}]},"zruseni":{"id":"zruseni","title":"Authority voids the contract","text":"The competition authority canceled the tender. The ordered equipment must be returned and re-tendered.","lesson":"Getting ahead of the authority's ruling is a bet. Plan B from the risk register would have saved months here.","unresolvedText":"The ED opened with temporary equipment.","choices":[{"text":"Rent equipment temporarily and re-run the tender properly","feedback":"Expensive, but the ED opens on time."},{"text":"Sue the authority","feedback":"The lawsuit will outlast the whole project."},{"text":"Open without the new equipment","feedback":"The ED works only halfway."}]}}},{"id":"promena","stars":{"ko":[{"text":"The solution reaches the Market interest goal"}],"top":[{"text":"A year later at least 50 %"},{"text":"The regional pilot took place"}]},"name":"The Shape-Shifting Project","tagline":"Lunches for one school, then the whole region, finally the market","scope":"A school lunch ordering system: orders and cancellations, payments, an export for accountants and a menu. What comes next, nobody knows yet.","intro":"A small software company won a contract: a lunch ordering system for one grammar school. The tender documentation is detailed, the price fixed, the deadline September 1. You lead the project. You just don't know yet that this project won't stay what it started as.","approachText":"The requirements are clear and stable, price and deadline are fixed and the customer knows exactly what they want. That's a predictive project. For now.","terms":{"launch":"the September 1 launch","contract":"as set by the contract with the grammar school","predShort":"connection to regional accounting","agileShort":"cafeteria rules and the pilot","users":"diners","usersGen":"diners","sponsor":"grammar school principal","committee":"company management","product":"The lunch system"},"stakeholders":[{"id":"skola","name":"Grammar school principal","wants":"what's in the contract, on time and without complications","quit":"withdrew from the contract.","epilogBad":"switched to another vendor a year later – “for one school it's needlessly complicated now”."},{"id":"rodice","name":"Parents and students","wants":"simple ordering from a phone","quit":"went back to paper meal tickets and the project lost its point.","epilogBad":"use the app only when they have to."},{"id":"kraj","name":"Regional authority","wants":"one system for 40 schools and a connection to regional accounting","quit":"issued a new tender for the system.","epilogBad":"is considering replacing the system a year later."}],"areas":{"web":{"label":"Web and app"},"platby":{"label":"Payments"},"integrace":{"label":"Integration"},"analyza":{"label":"Analysis and rules"},"ux":{"label":"User research"}},"team":[{"id":"ivana","name":"Ivana","role":"backend and payments"},{"id":"marek","name":"Marek"},{"id":"olga","name":"Olga","role":"analyst who knows the contract and the cafeteria"},{"id":"filip","name":"Filip"}],"workstreams":[{"id":"objednavky","name":"Orders and cancellations per the spec","why":"The school rules and the contract describe exactly how lunches are ordered and canceled."},{"id":"platby","name":"Bank transfer payments and matching","why":"The payment rules are given and changing them would be expensive."},{"id":"export","name":"Export for the school accountant","why":"The export format is dictated by the school's accounting software."},{"id":"jidelnicek","name":"Menu with allergens","why":"The scope set by the allergen regulation is described precisely in the contract."},{"id":"skoleni","name":"Cafeteria training before launch","why":"A one-off part of the handover – it belongs to the project and is planned for the launch date."},{"id":"vkladani","name":"Entering the daily menu","why":"The cafeteria manager does it every day. That's operations – the project just gives her the tool."},{"id":"ucty","name":"Creating accounts for new students every September","why":"It repeats every year. After launch the school does it, not the project team."}],"backlog":[{"id":"objednavky","name":"Ordering and canceling lunches"},{"id":"platby","name":"Bank transfer payments and matching"},{"id":"export","name":"Export for the school accountant"},{"id":"jidelnicek","name":"Menu with allergens"},{"id":"predani","name":"Guide and training for the cafeteria"},{"id":"ucty","name":"Manually creating student accounts (every September)"},{"id":"vkladani","name":"Entering the daily menu"}],"milestones":[{"id":"m1","name":"Launch at the grammar school","okText":"The system has been running at the grammar school since September 1.","lateText":"The launch slipped – for the first week lunches were ordered on paper."},{"id":"m2","name":"Regional pilot","okText":"The pilot runs at three schools in the region and data flow into regional accounting.","lateText":"The regional pilot never got going."},{"id":"m3","name":"Market interest","okText":"Private schools and kindergartens are signing up on their own.","lateText":"Market interest is lukewarm."}],"shifts":[{"title":"The region wants the system for all schools","text":"The regional authority saw the system at the grammar school and wants it for all 40 schools in the region – each with a slightly different cafeteria, subsidies and prices. The connection to regional accounting must go through approval; the rules of individual cafeterias are yet to be discovered.","addItems":[{"id":"vice_skol","name":"Managing multiple schools and cafeterias"},{"id":"ucetnictvi","name":"Connection to regional accounting"},{"id":"pravidla","name":"Different cafeteria rules (subsidies, prices)"},{"id":"pilot","name":"Pilot at three schools"}],"lesson":"When a clearly specified project gains a part with uncertain requirements (the rules of 40 cafeterias), waterfall planning alone is no longer enough. The accounting connection is still managed by plan, the cafeteria rules iteratively – and the two parts are linked by synchronization and integration milestones."},{"title":"The project becomes a product","text":"Parents love the app. The company wants to offer it to private schools and kindergartens nationwide – as a product on the market. Nobody knows which features will be in demand. The fixed-scope contract ends; the search for value begins.","team":{"join":[{"id":"dana","name":"Dana","role":"user research"}]},"addItems":[{"id":"mobil","name":"Mobile app for parents"},{"id":"notifikace","name":"Alert for an uncanceled lunch"},{"id":"hodnoceni","name":"Students rating lunches"},{"id":"predplatne","name":"Online subscription for private schools"},{"id":"skolky","name":"Kindergarten version"}],"lesson":"In a market with uncertain demand, neither the contract nor the plan decides anymore – validated value does. You need a Product Owner who sets the order, and experiments that validate interest before a feature is built. A detailed plan or EVM now mostly slows you down."}],"gate":{"id":"gate","title":"The regional council decides on expansion","text":"The regional council decides whether to roll the system out to all schools. What do you present?","lesson":"In a hybrid project you promise differently: firmly what can be planned (the accounting connection), and openly what is still being discovered (the cafeteria rules).","choices":[{"text":"Pilot data, the accounting connection plan, and openly what's still being learned about cafeteria rules","feedback":"The council appreciated that nobody promised the impossible. Expansion approved."},{"text":"Promise a fixed date and price for all 40 schools","feedback":"The council is thrilled. For now."},{"text":"Ask for more analysis before deciding","feedback":"The council postponed the decision by a month."}]},"eventSlots":[[{"id":"zmena","title":"The principal wants a “small” change","text":"The grammar school principal would like to add special diet menus. They're not in the contract.","lesson":"In a fixed-price predictive project, a scope change is a contract change: assess the impact, price it and agree on a date. Free work endangers what is in the contract.","choices":[{"text":"Assess the impact and offer it as a contract change with a price and date","feedback":"The principal ordered the change for the second semester."},{"text":"Do it for free to keep her happy","feedback":"The principal is delighted. The schedule, less so."},{"text":"Refuse – it's not in the contract","feedback":"Formally correct. The relationship suffered."}]},{"id":"banka","title":"The bank changed its statement format","text":"The school's bank announced a new format for electronic statements. Payment matching will stop working.","lesson":"Changes at suppliers and partners are a typical risk of a predictive project. A prepared response is cheaper than improvising.","choices":[{"text":"Per the risk register, use the prepared format converter","feedback":"The converter was ready. Done in two days."},{"text":"Replan and add work on matching","feedback":"The plan slipped by a few days."},{"text":"Match payments by hand for now","feedback":"Olga matches payments every morning."}]}],[{"id":"olga","title":"Olga fell ill","text":"Olga the analyst, the only one who knows the contract and the cafeteria's operations in detail, is out sick for two weeks.","lesson":"Even in a small team, knowledge in one head is a risk. A short write-up of key rules and a handover to a colleague cost little and protect the project.","choices":[{"text":"Olga briefly writes down the key rules from home and Marek takes them over","feedback":"Marek now knows why lunches must be canceled by eight."},{"text":"Wait until she's back","feedback":"Answers took two weeks."},{"text":"Ask the principal about every unclear point","feedback":"The principal answers. More and more tersely."}]},{"id":"kuchyne","title":"Testing with the cafeteria","text":"The cooks tried the system. It meets the contract, but the serving screen confuses them.","lesson":"Meeting the contract isn't enough if the result won't be usable. Feedback can be handled in a controlled way as a change within the project.","choices":[{"text":"Adjust the serving screen and log it as an approved change","feedback":"The cooks praise the serving screen."},{"text":"The contract is met, ignore the feedback","feedback":"Lines form at the serving counter."},{"text":"Write a detailed guide","feedback":"The guide hangs in the kitchen. Nobody reads it."}]}],[{"id":"pravidla_jidelen","title":"Every cafeteria is different","text":"The region's first three schools each have different rules for subsidies, prices and cancellations. Nobody has seen the other 37.","lesson":"Uncertain requirements are discovered iteratively with real users. A complete upfront analysis would be outdated before it was finished.","choices":[{"text":"Discover the rules step by step with three pilot cafeterias and grow the backlog","feedback":"After three weeks it's clear 80 % of cafeterias have just four rule variants."},{"text":"Write a complete analysis of all 40 cafeterias before development","feedback":"The analysis runs to 200 pages. Half of it is already outdated."},{"text":"One rule for everyone, they'll get used to it","feedback":"Simple. Parents at small schools pay more."}]},{"id":"dva_svety","title":"Accounting and the pilot drift apart","text":"The regional accounting connection is built to an approved spec, while the school pilot changes the rules every week. The data stop fitting together.","lesson":"In a hybrid project the predictively and agile managed parts must meet regularly. Without synchronization they drift apart.","choices":[{"text":"Weekly synchronization and a joint integration milestone","feedback":"Half an hour every Monday. Differences get caught early."},{"text":"The project manager coordinates both parts alone","feedback":"It works as long as you have time to watch everything."},{"text":"Let the parts run independently and connect them at the end","feedback":"Both parts move fast. In different directions."}]}],[{"id":"zarlivost","title":"The grammar school feels sidelined","text":"The grammar school principal complains that since the region arrived, nobody has time for her school.","lesson":"When a stronger stakeholder arrives, the original customer must not drop out of the game. Give them a new role.","choices":[{"text":"Make the grammar school a reference school with regular reviews","feedback":"The principal now shows the system to other schools herself."},{"text":"The region pays more, the grammar school must wait","feedback":"The principal won't forget."},{"text":"Promise the grammar school priority on fixes","feedback":"Marek fixes the grammar school's bugs even on Saturdays."}]},{"id":"filip","title":"Filip carries the integration alone","text":"Only Filip knows the regional accounting connection. He's tired and bugs are piling up.","lesson":"No critical part of a project should rest on a single person. Rotation and knowledge sharing are your insurance.","choices":[{"text":"Ivana takes turns with Filip on the integration and learns it","feedback":"Ivana can now deploy a new version on her own."},{"text":"Filip pushes it through with overtime","feedback":"Filip pushes it through. At what cost, we'll see."},{"text":"Move the integration deadline","feedback":"Filip breathed a sigh of relief. The region, less so."}]}],[{"id":"napady","title":"Ten ideas, one team","text":"Since the app became a product, ideas pour in from all sides: sales, parents, kindergartens, company management.","lesson":"In an agile product the Product Owner sets the order based on validated value – not whoever is loudest.","choices":[{"text":"The Product Owner ranks ideas by validated data","feedback":"Half the ideas ended up in the trash. The other half make sense."},{"text":"A team vote","feedback":"The technically interesting stuff won."},{"text":"Build everything sales promised","feedback":"Sales is happy. Parents can't find anything in the app."}]},{"id":"roadmapa","title":"Sales wants a fixed feature plan","text":"A salesperson wants to promise customers which features will be done when – a year ahead.","lesson":"An agile product communicates a roadmap of goals (what we want to improve), not a list of features with fixed dates.","choices":[{"text":"A roadmap with quarterly goals instead of feature dates","feedback":"Customers understand goals better than a feature list."},{"text":"A detailed feature plan a year ahead","feedback":"The plan lasted three weeks."},{"text":"Promise customers nothing","feedback":"Customers don't know what to expect."}]}],[{"id":"vykon","title":"At 7:30 a.m. the server can't keep up","text":"In the morning, when everyone cancels lunches, the app crashes. Customers grow every week.","lesson":"Technical debt and performance are part of value. Pausing new features for a sprint to fix the foundation is an investment.","choices":[{"text":"Pause new features for a sprint and fix performance","feedback":"The app runs even at 7:30."},{"text":"Keep adding features, performance can wait","feedback":"Parents write in reviews that the app doesn't work in the morning."},{"text":"Buy a bigger server","feedback":"It helped. For a few months."}]},{"id":"konkurence","title":"A competitor copies you","text":"A competing company released a similar app at half the price.","lesson":"You don't answer competition by copying, but by understanding your own users better.","choices":[{"text":"User interviews: where are we better for them?","feedback":"Parents love the alert for an uncanceled lunch. The competitor doesn't have it."},{"text":"Cut the price","feedback":"The price war has begun."},{"text":"Copy all the competitor's features","feedback":"Now there are two identical apps."}]}]],"followups":{"parovani":{"id":"parovani","title":"Manual matching can't keep up","text":"Payments keep growing and Olga matches them by hand every morning. She's starting to make mistakes.","lesson":"A stopgap done “for now” quickly becomes a permanent burden – usually carried by one person.","unresolvedText":"Manual payment matching stayed – and with it, billing errors.","choices":[{"text":"Finish automatic matching","feedback":"Olga has her mornings free again."},{"text":"Olga keeps matching","feedback":"Olga matches. Less and less accurately."},{"text":"Hire a temp","feedback":"The temp matches payments. Until the semester ends."}]},"slib_kraji":{"id":"slib_kraji","title":"The promised price doesn't add up","text":"It turns out the cafeteria rules are more complex than expected. The promised price and date for 40 schools don't add up.","lesson":"A firm promise on uncertain work is a gamble. When it doesn't add up, openly renegotiating scope beats keeping the promise at any cost.","unresolvedText":"The promise to the region was still being paid off a year after the project.","choices":[{"text":"Admit it openly and agree on a staged rollout","feedback":"The region wasn't thrilled, but accepted the stages."},{"text":"Keep the promise at any cost","feedback":"The promise stands. The team and the budget pay for it."},{"text":"Quietly drop some features","feedback":"The region noticed during acceptance."}]},"nesedi":{"id":"nesedi","title":"The pilot and accounting don't fit","text":"The school pilot and the regional accounting connection finally met. The data don't match.","lesson":"Predictively and agile managed parts that meet only at the end almost never fit together. The integration milestone belongs in the middle of the project, not at the end.","unresolvedText":"Data between the schools and regional accounting are still fixed by hand to this day.","choices":[{"text":"A joint integration test and an interface fix","feedback":"Two weeks of work. Now it fits."},{"text":"Transfer data to accounting by hand","feedback":"Olga has a new monthly chore."},{"text":"Postpone the pilot","feedback":"The pilot can wait. So can the region – reluctantly."}]}}},{"id":"startup","stars":{"ko":[{"text":"The public launch hits its traction target"}],"top":[{"text":"All three traction targets met"}]},"name":"Food Rescue Startup","tagline":"An app against food waste","scope":"Mobile app, partner business acquisition, marketing, user research and the business model. Nobody knows yet what exactly will work.","approachText":"High uncertainty: nobody knows what users want or which business model will work. The whole project is best managed in an agile way: short iterations, testing hypotheses and data-driven decisions. A detailed plan would rest on untested assumptions.","intro":"You're co-founding a startup that connects restaurants and shops with leftover food to people nearby. The money lasts 12 weeks – by then you must prove people actually want the app.","terms":{"launch":"the app launch","agileShort":"the whole product","users":"users","usersGen":"users","sponsor":"lead investor","poGood":"co-founder in charge of the product","committee":"investors"},"workstreams":[{"id":"mvp","name":"Mobile app (MVP)","why":"Only users will show what the app should do. Small releases, fast feedback, adjustments."},{"id":"vyzkum","name":"User research","why":"Research runs continuously and its questions change with whatever the team just learned."},{"id":"partneri","name":"Partner business acquisition","why":"Which pitch wins businesses over can only be found by trying – a pilot with a few, then adjust."},{"id":"marketing","name":"Marketing and growth","why":"Channels and messages are tested in short experiments, and money goes where it works."},{"id":"model","name":"Business model and pricing","why":"Careful, even though it sounds like planning: nobody knows upfront how much people and businesses will pay. It's tested by experiments."},{"id":"znacka","name":"Brand and design","why":"Design is tuned with users; the first version can be simple and improve over time."},{"id":"data","name":"Metrics and analytics","why":"What to measure gets clearer as the team learns its product and market."},{"id":"investori","name":"Investor talks","why":"The pitch is tuned to investor reactions and fresh traction data – iterative work."}],"backlog":[{"id":"nabidka","name":"Posting leftover food offers"},{"id":"registrace","name":"User sign-up"},{"id":"mapa","name":"Map of nearby offers"},{"id":"rezervace","name":"Food reservation and pickup"},{"id":"platba","name":"In-app payment"},{"id":"hodnoceni","name":"Business ratings"},{"id":"chat","name":"Chat with the business"},{"id":"vernost","name":"Loyalty program"},{"id":"uspory","name":"Rescued food and CO₂ counter"},{"id":"ai","name":"AI meal recommendations"},{"id":"tmavy","name":"Dark mode"},{"id":"firmy","name":"Packages for corporate cafeterias"},{"id":"socialni","name":"Social media login"},{"id":"web","name":"Web version of the app"},{"id":"oblibene","name":"Favorite businesses"},{"id":"podniky","name":"Sales stats for businesses"},{"id":"recepty","name":"Leftover recipes"},{"id":"odznaky","name":"Rescuer badges and leaderboards"},{"id":"pripominka","name":"Pickup reminder"},{"id":"charita","name":"Donating unsold food to charity"}],"discoveries":[{"id":"notifikace","name":"Alerts for food nearby","why":"After reservations go live, users write: \"Let me know when something shows up nearby!\""},{"id":"sdileni","name":"Sharing savings on social media","why":"Users screenshot the savings counter and share it. They want to do it right from the app."}],"milestones":[{"id":"m1","name":"First users","okText":"The first users are using the app and coming back.","lateText":"The app isn't giving users enough value yet."},{"id":"m2","name":"Demo Day","okText":"At demo day you can show growing numbers.","lateText":"At demo day there are no numbers that would convince investors."},{"id":"m3","name":"Public launch","okText":"The app has traction: people use it and recommend it!","lateText":"The app is out, but traction is weak."}],"gate":{"id":"gate","title":"Demo day: more money?","text":"Investors are deciding whether the startup gets money for another 6 months. What will you show them?","lesson":"In an agile project the best basis for a decision is a working product and data on what the team learned – failures included.","choices":[{"text":"A live product, traction metrics and what we learned (including what didn't work)","feedback":"Investors were impressed by how fast the team learns. Funding for the next period is secured."},{"text":"Slides with a big vision and market estimates, no data","feedback":"\"Nice vision. So how many people use it today?\" Silence."},{"text":"Postpone the demo until everything is done","feedback":"Investors postponed their decision and the money is running thin."}]},"events":[{"id":"jinak","title":"Users use it differently","text":"Data shows people open the app mostly on Friday afternoons – for bakery goods, not restaurants.","lesson":"Data on user behavior beats the original vision. Findings get validated and reflected in the backlog.","choices":[{"text":"Validate it with user interviews and update the backlog","addItems":[{"id":"pekarny","name":"Friday bakery deals"}],"feedback":"Interviews confirmed it. Friday bakery deals were added to the backlog."},{"text":"Stick to the original vision: restaurants","feedback":"Users keep coming for bread – the app just doesn't support it in any way."},{"text":"Rebuild everything around bakeries right now","addItems":[{"id":"pekarny","name":"Friday bakery deals"}],"feedback":"Maybe the right direction, but unvalidated and with a derailed sprint."}]},{"id":"konkurence","title":"Big competition","text":"A big delivery company announced a similar feature in its app.","lesson":"Against big players a startup wins by learning faster and staying focused, not by copying.","choices":[{"text":"Focus on what makes us different (local businesses, community) and test it","feedback":"Local businesses love that the startup knows them personally. The test confirmed interest."},{"text":"Copy all their features","feedback":"The team is chasing a giant at its own game. No chance."},{"text":"Ignore it","feedback":"Nothing changed – but the team doesn't know how to stand out."}]},{"id":"pivot","title":"Companies are calling","text":"Three companies reached out wanting to offer leftover cafeteria food to their employees through the app. It's a whole different segment.","lesson":"A pivot is a strategy change based on validated learning – not a panic move, nor stubborn clinging to the original vision.","choices":[{"text":"Test the hypothesis with a cheap experiment (landing page + 5 interviews), then decide","feedback":"The experiment showed strong interest. The value of \"Packages for corporate cafeterias\" is now validated."},{"text":"Pivot to companies right away and ditch the rest","feedback":"Bold, but unvalidated. The team also threw away ideas in progress."},{"text":"Refuse – that's not our vision","feedback":"The opportunity went elsewhere."}]},{"id":"runway","title":"Running out of money","text":"The money will barely last the rest of the planned period. The investor wants to see that the product makes sense.","lesson":"With limited resources, focus on the metric that shows real value and cut everything that doesn't lead to it.","choices":[{"text":"Focus on repeat reservations and cut the \"Could\" features","feedback":"The team only builds what drives repeat use. The money will last."},{"text":"Spend the rest on ads to get the numbers up","feedback":"Downloads spiked, but people don't come back. And the money is gone."},{"text":"Freeze development and save","feedback":"The money lasts longer, but the product isn't moving."}]},{"id":"vypadek","title":"Friday night outage","text":"The app crashed on Friday evening – right at peak traffic.","lesson":"An incident is a chance to improve the process. Look for the cause in the system, not for someone to blame.","choices":[{"text":"Fix it, then a blameless retrospective + monitoring and tests in the Definition of Done","feedback":"Cause found; monitoring now raises the alarm before users notice."},{"text":"Find out who broke it","feedback":"The team is scared and bugs start getting swept under the rug."},{"text":"Pay for beefier servers and leave it at that","feedback":"It helped, but the real cause remained."}]},{"id":"sms","title":"Businesses don't want another tablet","text":"Partner restaurants refuse to install the business app. \"Just text us, we'll reply.\"","lesson":"The simplest solution that works for users is often the best MVP.","choices":[{"text":"Build the simplest SMS version and test it with three businesses","addItems":[{"id":"sms","name":"Posting offers via SMS"}],"feedback":"The businesses love it. Two days brought more new offers than the whole past month."},{"text":"Insist on the business app","feedback":"Two businesses ended the partnership."},{"text":"Hire salespeople to win them over","feedback":"They won over a few businesses, but the expensive way."}]}]},{"id":"tovarna","stars":{"ko":[{"text":"Production starts with all Must items"},{"text":"The line gets CE certification – without it, no production"}],"top":[{"text":"All milestones met"}]},"name":"E-bike Production Line","tagline":"Machine installation + production software","scope":"Factory hall modifications, machine purchase and installation, certification, and software for production and maintenance.","intro":"An e-bike maker is building a new production line. In 12 weeks the first bike should roll off it.","predWorld":"Hall modifications, machine purchase and installation, CE certification. Long lead times and standards.","agileWorld":"Production management software, a maintenance app and digital work instructions. Tuned with operators right on the line.","terms":{"launch":"the production start","predShort":"hall, machines, certification","agileShort":"production software","users":"operators","usersGen":"operators","sponsor":"production director","poGood":"experienced shift supervisor","committee":"company management"},"dependency":{"lock":"Waiting for machine delivery (predictive milestone)","hint":"<b>Line machine integration</b> is waiting for a predictive milestone: machine delivery."},"workstreams":[{"id":"instalace","name":"Production line installation","why":"Assembly and commissioning of machines follow a fixed technical plan with strict sequencing."},{"id":"hala","name":"Factory hall modifications","why":"Construction work with a permit and a clear specification. Changes are expensive."},{"id":"ce","name":"Machine safety certification (CE)","why":"The standards and certification process are set. They must be met completely and on time."},{"id":"nakup","name":"Machine and spare parts procurement","why":"Tender and contracts with long lead times. The specification is clear up front."},{"id":"mes","name":"Manufacturing execution software (MES)","why":"Software can be built in parts and tuned based on experience from operations."},{"id":"udrzba","name":"Mobile app for maintenance staff","why":"Maintenance needs are best learned in practice – iterate directly with users."},{"id":"navody","name":"Digital work instructions","why":"Instructions improve based on feedback from operators right on the line."},{"id":"ai","name":"Experiment: predictive maintenance from sensor data","why":"Uncertain outcome – you need to experiment and learn from the data."}],"backlog":[{"id":"login","name":"Operator badge sign-in"},{"id":"order","name":"Production order view"},{"id":"report","name":"Output reporting"},{"id":"machines","name":"Line machine integration"},{"id":"fault","name":"Fault reporting"},{"id":"oee","name":"Line performance overview (OEE)"},{"id":"guides","name":"Digital work instructions"},{"id":"scrap","name":"Scrap tracking"},{"id":"maint","name":"Maintenance schedule"},{"id":"shift","name":"Shift report for the supervisor"},{"id":"predict","name":"Predictive maintenance (AI)"},{"id":"contest","name":"Shift competition (gamification)"},{"id":"dark","name":"Dark mode"},{"id":"voice","name":"Voice control"},{"id":"photo","name":"Defect photo documentation"},{"id":"erp","name":"Supplier system integration"}],"milestones":[{"id":"m1","name":"Machine delivery","okText":"The machines arrived on time. They can be connected to the software from sprint 3.","lateText":"Delivery was late. The machines can't be connected until sprint 4."},{"id":"m2","name":"Installation and CE","okText":"The line is installed and certified.","lateText":"Installation ran late and certification slips. Management isn't thrilled."},{"id":"m3","name":"Production start","okText":"The first bike rolls off the line and operators report output in the new system!","lateText":"Production is running, but key features are missing:"}],"events":[{"id":"clo","title":"Machines stuck in customs","text":"The machine shipment is stuck in customs. At least a two-week delay. The software team had planned the machine integration.","lesson":"Dependencies between the predictive and agile parts belong in the risk register. The agile team can work around a delay (simulator, backlog replanning).","choices":[{"text":"Draw on the schedule buffer; meanwhile the software is developed against a machine simulator","feedback":"The simulator (a simple “digital twin”) caught bugs before the machines arrived."},{"text":"Pay for express customs clearance","feedback":"Fast, but expensive."},{"text":"Pause the software team until the machines arrive","feedback":"The team waited two weeks, even though it could have worked on items with no dependency."}]},{"id":"tablety","title":"Operators don't want tablets","text":"At the sprint review, operators declare: “The paper job sheets were faster.” They don't want to use the new system.","lesson":"Managing change for people is part of the project. Involving users in iterations increases adoption.","choices":[{"text":"Involve the operators: testing on the line, changes based on their input and an “ambassador” on every shift","feedback":"After two iterations the system beats paper and operators recommend it to colleagues themselves."},{"text":"Mandate it from the top","feedback":"Operators use the system, but enter data “blind” at the end of the shift."},{"text":"Run paper and the system side by side until the end of the project","feedback":"Double record-keeping is slow and the data drift apart."}]},{"id":"kryt","title":"Machine safety audit","text":"The auditor finds that one station lacks an adequate safety guard. Without a fix, there's no CE certification.","lesson":"Safety and certification are fixed requirements of the predictive part – never sacrificed for speed.","choices":[{"text":"Start change control, order the guard and adjust the installation schedule","feedback":"The guard arrived and certification passed. The delay fit within the buffer."},{"text":"Try to “talk your way” through certification","feedback":"The auditor didn't agree and company management is horrified."},{"text":"Remove the station from the line and run without it","feedback":"The line runs, but at lower capacity."}]},{"id":"zakaznik","title":"Customer wants an earlier start","text":"A key customer wants the first bike delivery two weeks early. They're offering a higher price for it.","lesson":"Fixed deadlines are negotiated through scope: delivering the most important part first (MVP) is a strength of hybrid.","choices":[{"text":"Analyze the impact and offer a limited start: Must software features and partial line capacity","feedback":"The customer got the first bikes early and the company a higher price. Full operation stayed on plan."},{"text":"Promise a full start two weeks early","feedback":"The customer is thrilled, both teams are in a panic."},{"text":"Refuse","feedback":"The plan is protected, but the sales department is disappointed."}]},{"id":"sit","title":"Machines on the office network?","text":"IT security discovers the machines are supposed to be on the same network as the office computers. That's a security risk.","lesson":"Cybersecurity concerns both parts: infrastructure is planned up front, software safeguards go into the Definition of Done.","choices":[{"text":"Add network segmentation to the installation plan and security to the Definition of Done","feedback":"The network is safely separated and every new feature passes a security check."},{"text":"Leave it – nobody's going to attack us","feedback":"A security risk now hangs over the whole production."},{"text":"Disconnect the machines from the network entirely","feedback":"Safe, but the software now gets no data from the machines."}]},{"id":"podlaha","title":"The floor can't bear the press","text":"The structural engineer finds the hall floor can't bear the new press. The foundations need reinforcing. The risk was in the register.","lesson":"Identified risks should have a prepared response and a reserve. Well-separated project parts let the agile team keep going even when construction hits trouble.","choices":[{"text":"Activate the risk reserve and replan the installation; the software team carries on","feedback":"The response plan worked. Meanwhile, software development continues."},{"text":"Install the press there anyway","feedback":"The engineer refused to sign off. You risk injuries and a fine."},{"text":"Stop the whole project until it's resolved","feedback":"The software has nothing to do with the floor. Time wasted for nothing."},{"text":"Negotiate emergency money with the sponsor and replan","feedback":"With no reserve ready, you have to find money and get a new plan approved. It costs time and trust."}]}]},{"id":"zachrana","stars":{"ko":[{"text":"The go-live migration happens"}],"top":[{"text":"A year later at least 50 %"}]},"name":"Rescuing a Project in Crisis","tagline":"You take over a running project that is falling apart","scope":"A new insurance claims system: migrating data from the old system by a fixed date, a new app for claims adjusters and new hardware at the branches.","intro":"Three months ago an insurance company launched a project for a new claims system. The previous project manager has left and the project is now yours. Four sprints remain until the go-live migration – then the old system is switched off and the contract with its vendor ends.","predWorld":"Data migration by a fixed date, new branch hardware, the contract with the old system's vendor.","agileWorld":"The claims adjusters' app, tuned to how people actually work with it.","terms":{"launch":"the go-live migration","predShort":"data migration and branch hardware","agileShort":"the claims adjusters' app","users":"claims adjusters","usersGen":"claims adjusters","sponsor":"CEO","committee":"board of directors","product":"The new claims system"},"stakeholders":[{"id":"reditel","name":"CEO","wants":"the migration date and costs","quit":"lost patience and stopped the project.","epilogBad":"called the project an expensive mistake a year later and refused to fund further development."},{"id":"likvidatori","name":"Claims adjusters","wants":"an app they can actually work with","quit":"refused to use the new system – the project lost its point.","epilogBad":"went back to spreadsheets and avoid the new system."},{"id":"it","name":"IT operations","wants":"stability, monitoring and a proper handover","quit":"refused to take the system over into operations.","epilogBad":"took the system over only on paper – every incident now bounces back to the project team."}],"areas":{"data":{"label":"Data migration"},"app":{"label":"App"},"backend":{"label":"Backend and integration"},"pobocky":{"label":"Branch hardware"}},"team":[{"id":"karel","name":"Karel","role":"data specialist"},{"id":"jana","name":"Jana","role":"app developer"},{"id":"ondrej","name":"Ondřej","role":"backend and integration"},{"id":"lucie","name":"Lucie","role":"tester who knows claims handling"},{"id":"petr","name":"Petr","role":"branch technician"}],"takeover":{"situation":"This is the state the project was handed to you in. You have one week to find out what is going on – then you must act.","symptoms":["Every app feature has a fixed date in the Gantt chart. Sprint reviews happen, but nothing changes because of them – “the plan is the plan”.","In March the claims adjusters asked to move one field on a form. The monthly board put it on the agenda in May.","Work order is set by whoever pushes hardest – sales on Monday, the CEO on Wednesday, IT on Friday.","The status report for the board of directors has been green for three months. Nobody on the team believes the migration date.","The team works late nights and weekends. Two people have already been on sick leave from exhaustion.","Only Karel understands the data migration. When he was sick for a week, the migration stood still."],"diagLesson":"Rescuing a project starts with a diagnosis: from the symptoms (consequences) you trace back to the mechanisms and the form of management causing them. Treating only the symptoms – more overtime, more reports – makes the problem worse.","lesson":"Adding “more management” won't rescue a project. You need to drop the practices that do harm (a detailed Gantt chart for agile work, one board for everything, overtime) and add what is missing: a backlog owner, transparent reporting, knowledge sharing and a plan only for what can be planned."},"backlog":[{"id":"hlaseni","name":"Fix the claim report form"},{"id":"migrace_test","name":"Trial data migration"},{"id":"migrace","name":"Go-live data migration"},{"id":"schvalovani","name":"Payout approval"},{"id":"pobocky","name":"Hardware at the remaining branches"},{"id":"monitoring","name":"Monitoring and alerts"},{"id":"predani","name":"Handover to operations: documentation and training"},{"id":"fotky","name":"Photo upload from mobile"},{"id":"chatbot","name":"Customer chatbot (the CEO's wish)"},{"id":"reporty","name":"Monthly reports for sales"},{"id":"hotline","name":"Branch hotline"},{"id":"skoleni_novacku","name":"Regular training for new branch staff"}],"milestones":[{"id":"m1","name":"Migration dress rehearsal","okText":"The trial migration went through and claims adjusters filed the first claims in the new app on migrated data.","lateText":"The migration dress rehearsal failed."},{"id":"m2","name":"Branches ready","okText":"All branches have the new hardware.","lateText":"Some branches are not ready for the migration."},{"id":"m3","name":"Go-live migration","okText":"The go-live migration is done, the old system is off and claims adjusters work in the new one.","lateText":"The go-live migration only half happened – missing:"}],"gate":{"id":"gate","title":"The board considers stopping the project","text":"The board of directors wants to know whether it still makes sense to invest in the project. What do you present?","lesson":"When rescuing a project, a true picture of its state is the first step to rebuilding trust. Another “green” report would destroy it for good.","choices":[{"text":"The real state, what you changed, and a realistic migration plan","feedback":"The board was taken aback but valued the honesty. The project got a chance."},{"text":"A green report as before – surely we'll make it now","feedback":"A board member asked about one number and the report fell apart."},{"text":"Ask to postpone the migration by two months","feedback":"The delay was approved. But extending the old system costs money."}]},"eventSlots":[[{"id":"karel","title":"Karel is at the edge","text":"After a meeting Karel, the only one who understands the data migration, tells you he can't keep up this pace much longer.","lesson":"When a critical part of the project rests on one exhausted person, lighten their load and spread their knowledge – don't motivate them to more overtime.","choices":[{"text":"Free Karel from everything but the migration and pair him with Lucie so she learns it","feedback":"Karel breathed a sigh of relief. Lucie asks about everything and takes notes."},{"text":"Promise him a bonus if he pulls it off – overtime is necessary now","feedback":"Karel nodded. He didn't look thrilled."},{"text":"Hire an external data specialist","team":{"join":[{"id":"viktor","name":"Viktor","role":"external data specialist"}]},"feedback":"Viktor is expensive, but he understands migrations."}]},{"id":"chatbot","title":"The CEO wants a chatbot","text":"The CEO saw a chatbot at a competitor and wants one before the migration. “It's just a small feature.”","lesson":"Stakeholders have different interests. The PM's job is not to please the strongest one, but to explain the impacts and protect what the project really needs.","choices":[{"text":"Explain that the chatbot doesn't belong before the migration and offer it as the first enhancement after","feedback":"The CEO frowned but understood. The claims adjusters appreciated someone thinking of them."},{"text":"Add the chatbot right away – the CEO pays","feedback":"The CEO is happy. The rest of the project, less so."},{"text":"Build a simple chatbot mock-up for the demo","feedback":"The mock-up pleased the CEO and cost two days of work."}]}],[{"id":"ztracena_data","title":"The trial migration lost data","text":"During the trial migration 3 % of insurance claims vanished. Two sprints remain until the go-live migration.","lesson":"A data migration error is fixed at its cause (the mapping), not by filling in numbers by hand. Otherwise it comes back in live operations.","choices":[{"text":"Stop, find the cause in the data mapping and repeat the trial","feedback":"The bug was in converting data from 2009. The second trial passed."},{"text":"Fill in the missing 3 % by hand and move on","feedback":"The numbers add up. Why they were missing, nobody knows."},{"text":"Postpone the go-live migration by a sprint","feedback":"There's time for the fix. But the CEO is furious."}]},{"id":"bojkot","title":"Claims adjusters refuse to test","text":"The claims adjusters stopped showing up for testing. “Nobody listens to us anyway.”","lesson":"Users nobody listens to stop cooperating. It helps to pull them right into the team and show that their feedback changes things.","choices":[{"text":"Invite two claims adjusters into the team for every review","feedback":"At the first review an adjuster moved the form field herself. The next day the fix was done."},{"text":"Order testing through the CEO","feedback":"The adjusters show up. They stay silent and tick off tests."},{"text":"Hold a one-off workshop","feedback":"The workshop was pleasant. Then everything went back to the old ways."}]}],[{"id":"it_odmita","title":"IT operations won't take over the system","text":"The head of IT operations announces they won't take the system into operations without monitoring and documentation.","lesson":"A project ends with a handover. Conditions for the handover to operations belong in the project from the start – otherwise the project team “runs” the system for a year after the end.","choices":[{"text":"Agree handover conditions with IT and put them into the plan","feedback":"For the first time IT feels like a partner, not an obstacle."},{"text":"Escalate to the CEO to order them","feedback":"The CEO ordered it. IT will remember."},{"text":"Promise the project team will support the system on its own for six months","feedback":"IT agrees. The team knows what that means for its summer."}]},{"id":"dodavatel","title":"The old system's vendor","text":"The old system's vendor reminds you the contract ends in three weeks. An extension won't come cheap.","lesson":"Insurance against a failed migration (the option to go back to the old system) is classic risk management. Refusing it to save money is a gamble.","choices":[{"text":"Per the risk register, negotiate a one-month extension as insurance","feedback":"The insurance is pricey, but cheaper than claims handling going down."},{"text":"Pay for a three-month extension","feedback":"Extended. The budget feels it."},{"text":"Refuse – the migration will make it","feedback":"The CEO appreciated the savings."}]}],[{"id":"vikend","title":"The last week before migration","text":"One week to the go-live migration. The CEO suggests the whole team work over the weekend “just to be safe”.","lesson":"Before a critical operation you need a rested team and a verified procedure (dress rehearsal, checklist), not exhausted people making mistakes.","choices":[{"text":"Dress rehearsal on Friday, weekend off, go-live migration on Monday by the checklist","feedback":"The team came in rested on Monday. The checklist caught two forgotten steps."},{"text":"The whole team over the weekend, so we have a buffer","feedback":"On Monday morning nobody knew which version of the script was the right one."},{"text":"Half the team on call, half resting","feedback":"A compromise. The on-call crew was needed twice."}]},{"id":"novinar","title":"A journalist calls","text":"A journalist heard the insurer's project is in trouble and wants a statement.","lesson":"Crisis communication rests on short, truthful information through the right channel. Denial comes back to bite.","choices":[{"text":"Refer them to the press office with a short, truthful statement","feedback":"The article came out short and factual."},{"text":"Say everything is fine","feedback":"The journalist had an internal email saying the opposite."},{"text":"No comment","feedback":"The article ran under the headline “Insurer Stays Silent”."}]}]],"followups":{"karel_odchazi":{"id":"karel_odchazi","title":"Karel handed in his notice","text":"Karel is joining a competitor. He wants to spend most of his notice period on vacation.","lesson":"Paying an exhausted person to do more overtime doesn't work. A knowledge island shows up exactly when time is shortest.","unresolvedText":"Karel left after the migration and nobody knows why some data look odd.","choices":[{"text":"Karel writes up the migration procedure before leaving and Lucie takes it over","team":{"reason":"leaves for a competitor after the handover"},"feedback":"The documentation is brief, but Lucie understands the migration."},{"text":"Talk him into staying until the migration","feedback":"Karel stayed. He works, but his mind is elsewhere."},{"text":"Hire an external specialist and let Karel go","team":{"reason":"leaves for a competitor","join":[{"id":"viktor","name":"Viktor","role":"external data specialist"}]},"feedback":"Viktor is learning from the code. Slowly."}]},"chybejici_data":{"id":"chybejici_data","title":"Customers are looking for their claims","text":"Customers' open insurance claims have vanished. The call center is swamped.","lesson":"Filling in by hand covered up the bug but didn't remove it. A problem swept under the rug comes back bigger.","unresolvedText":"A year after the migration, lost insurance claims keep turning up.","choices":[{"text":"Find the cause, fix the mapping and migrate the affected data again","feedback":"Cause found. It hurt, but it's behind us."},{"text":"Handle complaints one by one","feedback":"Complaints pile up faster than they get resolved."},{"text":"Set up a team to track them down by hand","feedback":"Tracked down. The cause remains."}]},"vypnuti":{"id":"vypnuti","title":"The vendor switches off the old system","text":"The contract ended and the vendor switched the old system off. The go-live migration isn't verified yet.","lesson":"Without insurance, every migration delay is a crisis. Risk management means preparing a way back before you need it.","unresolvedText":"The old system's vendor charged double for the forced extension.","choices":[{"text":"Pay for an express extension","feedback":"The system is running again. At a price that hurts."},{"text":"Migrate immediately without a dress rehearsal","feedback":"The migration happened. What broke along the way remains to be seen."},{"text":"Work on paper without a system for two weeks","feedback":"The claims adjusters hauled binders up from the basement."}]}}}]});
